it=20` hits `:778`, `heap_limit=21` hits `:791`. `pcre2_get_match_data_heapframes_size()` staying at 20480 is asserted to prove no growth happened.\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_BAD_BACKSLASH_K` requires `\\K` reached *by recursion* from inside a lookaround (`(a\\K)(?=(?1))` with **no** `PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK`) — syntactic `\\K` in a lookaround is a compile error, and the extra option suppresses the runtime error.\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX` at `pcre2_convert.c:872` is **provably unreachable**: `pcre2_set_glob_separator` only accepts `/ \\ .` and `pcre2_set_glob_escape` only accepts 0 or ASCII punctuation, so neither field can ever be ≥ 128.\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPESCAPE` at `pcre2_substitute.c:1585` is unreachable: `_pcre2_check_escape` only returns `ESC_g` for `\\g<`, so `*ptr != '<'` can never hold there.\n- `pcre2_dfa_match` `PCRE2_ERROR_DEPTHLIMIT` cannot fire at top level (`rlevel++ > limit` with `rlevel` starting at 0), so the recipe needs a recursion/assertion pattern.\n- 16 context setters have **no validation at all** (including `pcre2_set_heap_limit/match_limit/depth_limit(0)` which return 0 and only fail later at match time). These are listed as rows with expected `0 (never rejects)` so a translation that *adds* a check gets caught.\n- 14 rows cover the PRIV()-only files in scope (`pcre2_study.c`, `pcre2_auto_possess.c`, `pcre2_find_bracket.c`, `pcre2_extuni.c`, `pcre2_script_run.c`, `pcre2_xclass.c`, `pcre2_ord2utf.c`, `pcre2_chkdint.c`, `pcre2_string_utils.c`, `pcre2_newline.c`) — none has a non-compile public entry point, so all are `UNREACHABLE` with the reason given.\n\n## Rejections I could not reach with a recipe\n\nAll 33 are `UNREACHABLE` by construction, in these categories (each with the reason in the notes field): JIT-only paths (4), 16-bit-only (1), `#ifndef SUPPORT_UNICODE` stubs (2), internal-corruption-only `PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL`/`LCOV_EXCL` assertions (11), needs >2^63-byte allocations or 2^31 substitutions (3), compiler-never-emits-this