rpreter handles and, for each group, one concrete pattern that reaches it: backreferences (OP_REF/OP_REFI/OP_DNREF/OP_DNREFI + the match_ref helper + PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF), recursion (OP_RECURSE), atomic groups (OP_ONCE), possessive quantifiers, conditionals (OP_COND/OP_SCOND, DEFINE, (?(R)), (?(<name>)), (?(VERSION)), lookaheads/lookbehinds (OP_ASSERT*, OP_ASSERTBACK*, variable-length lookbehind, OP_ASSERTBACK_NA), \\K (OP_MARK/OP_KET vs Fstart_match), the verbs OP_MARK/OP_PRUNE/OP_SKIP/OP_THEN/OP_COMMIT/OP_ACCEPT/OP_FAIL and their _ARG forms, script runs (OP_SCRIPT_RUN), \\X (OP_EXTUNI), XCLASS/ECLASS, OP_CALLOUT/OP_CALLOUT_STR, OP_DOLL/OP_DOLLM/OP_CIRC/OP_CIRCM/OP_EOD/OP_EODN/OP_SOD/OP_SOM/OP_SET_SOM, OP_ANY/OP_ALLANY, \\R (OP_BSR with bsr convention), \\b/\\B (OP_WORD_BOUNDARY, OP_NOT_WORD_BOUNDARY, and the UCP variants), \\g / OP_ANYNL.\n\n5. Partial matching: every PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT vs PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD branch in both files, mb->hitend / mb->partial, what subject shapes yield PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL vs NOMATCH, and how partial interacts with PCRE2_NOTEOL / end-of-subject assertions.\n\n6. pcre2_dfa_match() specifics: workspace size checks (PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE), PCRE2_DFA_RESTART (what workspace state is required, PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_BADRESTART), PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST, the unsupported-item errors PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UITEM / UCOND / UFUNC / UINVALID_UTF / DFA_RECURSE, the internal recursion (recursion via internal_dfa_match), match_limit/depth_limit use in DFA, and how DFA reports multiple matches in the ovector.\n\n7. Newline handling at match time: mb->nltype/nllen/nl, the six conventions, and the bsr convention; where CRLF is treated atomically (bumpalong skipping CRLF).\n\n8. PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF at match time: which code paths differ (the \"valid UTF fragment\" logic), lines.\n\nBe exhaustive on line numbers but terse in prose. No file writes."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_token