{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ygpuvamyzevxnrymvibuqivll6ufb74nw7dp7giyww4irn46loja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All line numbers below are in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wwiWoN/c_src/src/pcre2_substitute.c` unless another path is given.\n\n## 0. Preliminaries / global shape\n\n- `SUBSTITUTE_OPTIONS` mask (which bits are stripped from `options` before `pcre2_match`): 48-52; saved at 951, stripped at 952. Any bit **not** in this mask + `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` is passed through to `pcre2_match` (so `PCRE2_ANCHORED`, `PCRE2_NOTBOL`, `PCRE2_PARTIAL_*`, `PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT` etc. reach the matcher).\n- Entry bookkeeping: `buff_offset=0`, `lengthleft=buff_length=*blength` (777-778), `*blength=PCRE2_UNSET` (779).\n- NULL handling axes: `replacement==NULL` (802-806) — `rlength!=0` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL`, else replaced by `null_str`; `subject==NULL` (813-817) same; `PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` for rlength (808) and length (819).\n- `start_offset > length` → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSET` (956-961).\n- `match_data==NULL` → internal match data created (887-896), `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` on failure.\n- Sanity/limit branches: `\\K` weirdness `ovector[1]<ovector[0] || ovector[0]<start_offset` → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSPATTERN` (1001-1005); progress assert → `PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL_DUPMATCH` (1015-1024, LCOV-excluded); `subs==INT_MAX` → `PCRE2_ERROR_TOOMANYREPLACE` (1032-1036).\n- Error exits: `NOROOM`/NOMEMORY 1771, `CASEERROR`/REPLACECASE 1775, `TOOLARGEREPLACE` 1779, `BAD`/BADREPLACEMENT 1783, `BADESCAPE`/BADREPESCAPE 1787, `PTREXIT` (sets `*blength = ptr-replacement`, i.e. error offset in replacement) 1790-1792. `EXIT` 1766-1769: on the internal-match-data path the block is freed, otherwise `match_data->rc = rc` is written back (observable side effect axis).\n- **State-leak axis:** `escaped_literal` is declared/initialised once at 754, outside the global loop; set TRUE at 1553, cleared only by `\\E` at 1090-1095. A replacement ending inside `\\Q` leaves the *next* global iteration starting in literal mode. Contrast `forcecase` which **is** reset per iteration (975-977). Good differential test: `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_GLOBAL|EXTENDED`, replacement `\\Qa$1`, subject with 2 matches.\n\n## 1. PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_* option bits\n\n| Option | Tested at | Input shape that makes it matter |\n|---|---|---|\n| `LITERAL` | 1054 (`CHECKMEMCPY(ptr, rlength)` 1056) | any replacement containing `$` or `\\`, e.g. `$1`/`\\U`: with LITERAL copied verbatim, else interpreted. Note whole-replacement copy bypasses all case-forcing. |\n| `GLOBAL` | 1715; cleared at 1673 by negative substitute_callout | subject with ≥2 matches |\n| `EXTENDED` | 1290 (`${name:+/:-}`), 1472 (backslash escapes) | replacement `\\U$1`, `${1:-x}`, `\\Q..\\E`, `\\x41`; without EXTENDED a `\\` is a literal code unit (1617-1631) and `${1:-x}` → `PCRE2_ERROR_REPMISSINGBRACE` at 1316-1320 |\n| `UNKNOWN_UNSET` | 1191 (`$+` with `top_bracket==0`), 1258 (`$99` numeric > top_bracket), 1371 (`${name}` not in nametable), 1408 (NOSUBSTRING from `substring_length_bynumber` re-mapped to UNSET) | replacement `$9` / `${nosuch}` on a pattern with fewer groups. Off → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING`; on → treated as unset (then subject to UNSET_EMPTY / `:-` / `:+`) |\n| `UNSET_EMPTY` | 1212 (`$+` all-unset), 1415 (plain group substitution, `special==0`) | pattern `(a)|(b)` matched on `b`, replacement `$1`. Off → `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET`; on → empty. Only applies when `special==0`, so `${1:-d}` is unaffected. |\n| `REPLACEMENT_ONLY` | 825 (`replacement_only`), used 796, 965, 1045, 1669, 1735 | any subject with non-match prefix/suffix; also *required* whenever `PCRE2_PARTIAL_*` is set (796-797 → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION`) |\n| `OVERFLOW_LENGTH` | 649 (CHECKMEMCPY), 675 (CHECKCASECPY_BASE); result at 1748-1755 | buffer too small: off → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` with `*blength` still `PCRE2_UNSET`; on → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` with `*blength = buff_length + extra_needed` (1754) |\n| `MATCHED` | 824, 840, 898, 979-983 | see §7 |\n\n## 2. EXTENDED syntax parsed\n\n`$` branch (1101-1465), all of which is active regardless of EXTENDED except where noted:\n- `$$` → literal `$` (1111).\n- `$&` → group 0 (1126-1131).\n- `` $` `` (pre-match) and `$'` (post-match) (1132-1164); `$'` errors `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIALSUBS` under partial (1153-1157).\n- `$_` whole subject (1165-1179); `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIALSUBS` under partial (1170-1174).\n- `$+` highest set group (1180-1217): `top_bracket==0` path 1187-1197; `oveccount < top_bracket+1` → `PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE` (1202-1206); scan loop 1207-1208. Explicitly *not* taken for `$+{`(1181).\n- `${...}` (1219-1224, close-brace check 1316-1320, `ptr++` 1323).\n- `$<name>` JS syntax (1225-1233, close check 1326-1331); `$<` rejects `*` (1235) and digits (1242).\n- `${*MARK}` / `$*MARK` (1235-1240 star flag, 1336-1354); non-MARK star name → `BAD`; mark length read from `mark[-1]` (1345).\n- `$12` numeric (1242-1270); `${name}` via `read_name_subst` (1271-1280).\n- **EXTENDED-only** `${name:-default}` / `${name:+set:unset}`: 1288-1312. `special` must be `+` or `-` else `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSTITUTION` (1294-1298). Requires `!star && ptr < repend - 2` (1291) — note the `-2` slack is an off-by-one-style edge worth testing (`${1:-}` at exact end). `find_text_end` calls 1301 (last=`special=='-'`) and 1308. Reprocessing via pointer stack: 1424-1448; `ptrstackptr >= PTR_STACK_SIZE` (20, line 46) → `BAD` (1433). `-` with set group jumps to `LITERAL_SUBSTITUTE` (1428).\n\nBackslash branch, **EXTENDED only** (1472-1613):\n- Case escapes recognised locally (not by `check_escape`): `\\L` 1480-1484, `\\l` 1486-1497 (incl. `\\l\\U` → `REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST` 1490-1496), `\\U` 1499-1503, `\\u` 1505-1516 (incl. `\\u\\L` → `TITLE_FIRST`, single_char FALSE 1509-1515). Guard `ptr < repend - 1` (1478); the lookahead guards are `ptr + 2 < repend` (1490, 1509) — so `\\u\\L` at the very end of the replacement does **not** collapse (test `\"\\\\u\\\\L\"` as the entire replacement vs `\"\\\\u\\\\Lx\"`).\n- `\\E` → `SETFORCECASE` with `CASE_NONE` (1549-1550, label 1524).\n- `\\Q` → `escaped_literal = TRUE` (1552-1554); literal-mode exit 1090-1095.\n- Data escapes via `PRIV(check_escape)` 1543-1544: `case 0`, `ESC_b`→`CHAR_BS`, `ESC_v`→`CHAR_VT` (1556-1576); UTF encode via `ord2utf` at 1564.\n- `\\g<name>` 1578-1602 (`<` required 1584, `>` required 1593, name via `read_name_subst` 1589) → `GROUP_SUBSTITUTE`.\n- `rc < 0` from check_escape = numeric backreference `\\1`, `\\g{2}`, `\\o`, `\\x`… → `group = -rc-1` (1604-1610); positive non-handled `erc` → `BADESCAPE` (1611); `errorcode != 0` → `BADESCAPE` (1545).\n\nCase-forcing state machine:\n- State type `case_state {int to_case; BOOL single_char;}` 272-275; internal values `CASE_NONE=0` (268), 1/2/3 = LOWER/UPPER/TITLE_FIRST (comment 269), `CASE_REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST=4` (270).\n- Per-global-iteration reset: 975. `SETFORCECASE` block 1522-1540: flushes pending delayed case (1532-1534), assigns `forcecase = new_forcecase`, records `casestart_offset = buff_offset` (1537) and `casestart_extra_needed = extra_needed` (1538).\n- Consumers test `forcecase.to_case != CASE_NONE && substitute_case_callout == NULL` at 1346-1350 (`${*MARK}`), 1459-1463 (group / `$&` / `` $` `` / `$'` / `$_`), 1571-1575 (escaped data char), 1626-1630 (literal code unit). Trailing flush at 1641-1643.\n- Transitions inside the default handler: TITLE_FIRST → LOWER (346), REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST → UPPER (352), `single_char` → CASE_NONE (357-358); mirrored in `do_case_copy` 490-491, 572, 595.\n- Distinguishing inputs: `\\u$1` (single char, group of length ≥2, first char multi-code-unit in UTF), `\\uabc`, `\\u\\Labc`, `\\l\\Uabc`, `\\U$1\\Eabc`, `\\l` immediately followed by a group that is empty (single_char with `input_len==0` → early return at 328 / assert at 468).\n\n## 3. substitute_case_callout path\n\n- Fetched from mcontext at 781-785 (`mcontext->substitute_case_callout`, `..._data`). NULL vs non-NULL is the top-level axis: NULL → immediate `default_substitute_case_callout` via `CHECKCASECPY_DEFAULT` (687-700) at 1348/1461/1573/1628; non-NULL → *delayed*, in-place transformation via `DELAYEDFORCECASE()` (714-737) → `CHECKCASECPY_CALLOUT` (702-709) → `do_case_copy` (443).\n- Signature `(PCRE2_SPTR in, PCRE2_SIZE in_len, PCRE2_UCHAR *out, PCRE2_SIZE out_cap, int to_case, void *data)` 771-772 / 447-448.\n- Call sites inside `do_case_copy`: 487-488 (whole run, `state->to_case` = 1/2/3), 539-540 (leading char only, `ch1_to_case`), 578-581 (remainder, `rest_to_case`).\n- `int` flag values actually passed: only 1 `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_CASE_LOWER`, 2 `UPPER`, 3 `TITLE_FIRST` — the internal 4 (`REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST`) is decomposed into LOWER for ch1 + UPPER for rest (501-502), and `\\l` single-char becomes LOWER for ch1 + `CASE_NONE`/memmove for rest (496-497, 563-573).\n- Return value: `~(PCRE2_SIZE)0` = error → propagated at 541, 582, 598-599 → `CHECKCASECPY_CALLOUT` 708 → `CASEERROR` → `PCRE2_ERROR_REPLACECASE` (1776). A return > capacity is a length request: retry loop 537-560 (memmove of `rest` to the right at 553, `ch1_cap = rc` 556); `rc > max_ch1_cap` sets `ch1_overflow` (545-549), `rc2 > output_cap - rc` sets `rest_overflow` (584), clamp `rc2 = rest_len` when ch1 overflowed (592-593). Overflow then flows to `CHECKCASECPY_BASE` 673-684 → NOROOM or `extra_needed`.\n- **Multi-pass axis:** with a case callout + `OVERFLOW_LENGTH`, the required length is only *estimated* (`pessimistic_case_inflation`, 289-293, `(len>>3)+10`) at 722, so two calls may not suffice (comment 280-287). Good differential input: callout that expands characters (e.g. ß→SS) with a small buffer.\n- A \"naughty\" callout returning different lengths for identical input is explicitly tolerated (comment 524-527) — worth fuzzing.\n\n## 4. substitute_callout path\n\n- Called only if `mcontext != NULL && mcontext->substitute_callout != NULL` (1648) **and** `!overflowed` (165