length + extra_needed` (1748-1755); else `rc = subs`, `*blength = buff_offset - 1` (1760-1764, i.e. excludes NUL).\n- Buffer-size input axes worth tabulating: `*blength == 0` (even the NUL at 1742 overflows); exactly `needed-1`; exactly `needed` (must succeed, `lengthleft` hits 0 only on the NUL); `needed+1`; with `start_offset > 0` and `REPLACEMENT_ONLY` on/off; overflow occurring *inside* a case-forced run so `DELAYEDFORCECASE` takes the pessimistic-guess arm (720-726) rather than the rewind arm (728-733).\n- `casestart_offset`/`casestart_extra_needed` (976-977, 1537-1538) plus `chars_outstanding = (buff_offset-casestart_offset)+(extra_needed-casestart_extra_needed)` (716-717) — the \"straddling\" case (case run started before overflow, ended after) is the interesting one.\n- `sub_start_extra_needed` (1048, used 1689) isolates one substitution's contribution for the overflowed-callout estimate.\n\n## 6. GLOBAL loop\n\n- Loop 971-1730. Continuation is fully delegated in 10.48-DEV: `pcre2_next_match(match_data, &start_offset, &goptions)` at 1716; on FALSE, `start_offset = ovector[1]` and break (1718-1719). `goptions` initialised 751 and OR'd into the match options at 984.\n- There is **no** `PCRE2_ANCHORED` retry in this version. The empty-match logic lives in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wwiWoN/c_src/src/pcre2_match_next.c`: empty match → `*poptions = PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART` at the same offset (147-160), end-of-subject → stop (151-152); `\\K` zero-progress case (`ovector[0] != start_offset && ovector[1] == start_offset`) → `do_bumpalong` (129-141); CRLF atomic skip (61-71, only for `PCRE2_NEWLINE_CRLF/ANY/ANYCRLF`) and UTF `FORWARDCHARTEST` character advance (75-85) in `do_bumpalong` (49-88).\n- Consequence for testing: `pcre2_substitute` itself never memcpys a bumpalong gap — `PCRE2_ASSERT(start_offset == ovector[1])` at 1728. Inputs: empty-matching pattern (`a*`, `(?=x)`, `\\b`) on non-empty subject; CRLF subject with each newline convention; UTF subject with multi-code-unit chars at the bumpalong point; `\\K` in a lookahead.\n- `utf` → `options |= PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` after the first match (987-989), so a malformed subject is only validated once.\n\n## 7. PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED\n\nRequired prior state on the caller's `match_data`, checks at 840-872:\n- `match_data == NULL` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` (827).\n- `match_data->rc < 0 && != PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH` → that rc returned verbatim (845-846). `rc == PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH` is accepted and yields 0 substitutions (used at 981, break at 994).\n- `matchedby == PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER` → `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UFUNC` (849-850).\n- `code != match_data->code` → `PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSPATTERN` (852-853).\n- subject identity: `length != match_data->subject_length` **or** not (`original_subject == match_data->subject` or (`PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT` set and (`length==0` or `memcmp` equal))) → `PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSSUBJECT` (859-864). Note `original_subject` (762) is the *pre*-NULL-substitution pointer, so NULL-vs-NULL matches strictly.\n- `start_offset != match_data->start_offset` → `PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSOFFSET` (866-867).\n- `(options & ~(SUBSTITUTE_OPTIONS|PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK)) != (match_data->options & ~PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK)` → `PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSOPTIONS` (869-871). So differing `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_*` or `NO_UTF_CHECK` is fine; differing `PCRE2_NOTBOL`/`ANCHORED`/`PARTIAL_*` is not.\n- Cloning the match data (898-917): `pairs = min(top_bracket+1, oveccount)` (905-906), `pcre2_match_data_create(match_data->oveccount)` (907), partial `memcpy` up to `offsetof(...ovector) + 2*pairs*sizeof` (910-911), `heapframes` cleared (912-913), `PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT` cleared (915). Test axis: small oveccount (e.g. 1 pair) + `$1`/`$+`.\n- First iteration consumes the match (979-983), then `use_existing_match = FALSE` so subsequent global iterations call `pcre2_match`.\n\n## 8. UTF / NO_UTF_CHECK / COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT / PARTIAL\n\n- `utf` from `code->overall_options & PCRE2_UTF`: 758; use