written back (observable side effect axis).\n- **State-leak axis:** `escaped_literal` is declared/initialised once at 754, outside the global loop; set TRUE at 1553, cleared only by `\\E` at 1090-1095. A replacement ending inside `\\Q` leaves the *next* global iteration starting in literal mode. Contrast `forcecase` which **is** reset per iteration (975-977). Good differential test: `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_GLOBAL|EXTENDED`, replacement `\\Qa$1`, subject with 2 matches.\n\n## 1. PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_* option bits\n\n| Option | Tested at | Input shape that makes it matter |\n|---|---|---|\n| `LITERAL` | 1054 (`CHECKMEMCPY(ptr, rlength)` 1056) | any replacement containing `$` or `\\`, e.g. `$1`/`\\U`: with LITERAL copied verbatim, else interpreted. Note whole-replacement copy bypasses all case-forcing. |\n| `GLOBAL` | 1715; cleared at 1673 by negative substitute_callout | subject with ≥2 matches |\n| `EXTENDED` | 1290 (`${name:+/:-}`), 1472 (backslash escapes) | replacement `\\U$1`, `${1:-x}`, `\\Q..\\E`, `\\x41`; without EXTENDED a `\\` is a literal code unit (1617-1631) and `${1:-x}` → `PCRE2_ERROR_REPMISSINGBRACE` at 1316-1320 |\n| `UNKNOWN_UNSET` | 1191 (`$+` with `top_bracket==0`), 1258 (`$99` numeric > top_bracket), 1371 (`${name}` not in nametable), 1408 (NOSUBSTRING from `substring_length_bynumber` re-mapped to UNSET) | replacement `$9` / `${nosuch}` on a pattern with fewer groups. Off → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING`; on → treated as unset (then subject to UNSET_EMPTY / `:-` / `:+`) |\n| `UNSET_EMPTY` | 1212 (`$+` all-unset), 1415 (plain group substitution, `special==0`) | pattern `(a)|(b)` matched on `b`, replacement `$1`. Off → `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET`; on → empty. Only applies when `special==0`, so `${1:-d}` is unaffected. |\n| `REPLACEMENT_ONLY` | 825 (`replacement_only`), used 796, 965, 1045, 1669, 1735 | any subject with non-match prefix/suffix; also *required* whenever `PCRE2_PARTIAL_*` is set (796-797 → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION`) |\n| `OVERFLOW_LENGTH` | 649 (CHECKMEMCPY), 675 (CHECKCASECPY_BASE); result at 1748-1755 | buffer too small: off → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` with `*blength` still `PCRE2_UNSET`; on → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` with `*blength = buff_length + extra_needed` (1754) |\n| `MATCHED` | 824, 840, 898, 979-983 | see §7 |\n\n## 2. EXTENDED syntax parsed\n\n`$` branch (1101-1465), all of which is active regardless of EXTENDED except where noted:\n- `$$` → literal `$` (1111).\n- `$&` → group 0 (1126-1131).\n- `` $` `` (pre-match) and `$'` (post-match) (1132-1164); `$'` errors `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIALSUBS` under partial (1153-1157).\n- `$_` whole subject (1165-1179); `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIALSUBS` under partial (1170-1174).\n- `$+` highest set group (1180-1217): `top_bracket==0` path 1187-1197; `oveccount < top_bracket+1` → `PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE` (1202-1206); scan loop 1207-1208. Explicitly *not* taken for `$+{`(1181).\n- `${...}` (1219-1224, close-brace check 1316-1320, `ptr++` 1323).\n- `$<name>` JS syntax (1225-1233, close check 1326-1331); `$<` rejects `*` (1235) and digits (1242).\n- `${*MARK}` / `$*MARK` (1235-1240 star flag, 1336-1354); non-MARK star name → `BAD`; mark length read from `mark[-1]` (1345).\n- `$12` numeric (1242-1270); `${name}` via `read_name_subst` (1271-1280).\n- **EXTENDED-only** `${name:-default}` / `${name:+set:unset}`: 1288-1312. `special` must be `+` or `-` else `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSTITUTION` (1294-1298). Requires `!star && ptr < repend - 2` (1291) — note the `-2` slack is an off-by-one-style edge worth testing (`${1:-}` at exact end). `find_text_end` calls 1301 (last=`special=='-'`) and 1308. Reprocessing via pointer stack: 1424-1448; `ptrstackptr >= PTR_STACK_SIZE` (20, line 46) → `BAD` (1433). `-` with set group jumps to `LITERAL_SUBSTITUTE` (1428).\n\nBackslash branch, **EXTENDED only** (1472-1613):\n- Case escapes recognised locally (not by `check_escape`): `\\L` 1480-1484, `\\l` 1486-1497 (incl. `\\l\\U` → `REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST` 1490-1496), `\\U` 1499-1503, `\\u` 1505-1516 (incl. `\\u\\L` → `TITLE_FIRS