single_char with `input_len==0` → early return at 328 / assert at 468).\n\n## 3. substitute_case_callout path\n\n- Fetched from mcontext at 781-785 (`mcontext->substitute_case_callout`, `..._data`). NULL vs non-NULL is the top-level axis: NULL → immediate `default_substitute_case_callout` via `CHECKCASECPY_DEFAULT` (687-700) at 1348/1461/1573/1628; non-NULL → *delayed*, in-place transformation via `DELAYEDFORCECASE()` (714-737) → `CHECKCASECPY_CALLOUT` (702-709) → `do_case_copy` (443).\n- Signature `(PCRE2_SPTR in, PCRE2_SIZE in_len, PCRE2_UCHAR *out, PCRE2_SIZE out_cap, int to_case, void *data)` 771-772 / 447-448.\n- Call sites inside `do_case_copy`: 487-488 (whole run, `state->to_case` = 1/2/3), 539-540 (leading char only, `ch1_to_case`), 578-581 (remainder, `rest_to_case`).\n- `int` flag values actually passed: only 1 `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_CASE_LOWER`, 2 `UPPER`, 3 `TITLE_FIRST` — the internal 4 (`REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST`) is decomposed into LOWER for ch1 + UPPER for rest (501-502), and `\\l` single-char becomes LOWER for ch1 + `CASE_NONE`/memmove for rest (496-497, 563-573).\n- Return value: `~(PCRE2_SIZE)0` = error → propagated at 541, 582, 598-599 → `CHECKCASECPY_CALLOUT` 708 → `CASEERROR` → `PCRE2_ERROR_REPLACECASE` (1776). A return > capacity is a length request: retry loop 537-560 (memmove of `rest` to the right at 553, `ch1_cap = rc` 556); `rc > max_ch1_cap` sets `ch1_overflow` (545-549), `rc2 > output_cap - rc` sets `rest_overflow` (584), clamp `rc2 = rest_len` when ch1 overflowed (592-593). Overflow then flows to `CHECKCASECPY_BASE` 673-684 → NOROOM or `extra_needed`.\n- **Multi-pass axis:** with a case callout + `OVERFLOW_LENGTH`, the required length is only *estimated* (`pessimistic_case_inflation`, 289-293, `(len>>3)+10`) at 722, so two calls may not suffice (comment 280-287). Good differential input: callout that expands characters (e.g. ß→SS) with a small buffer.\n- A \"naughty\" callout returning different lengths for identical input is explicitly tolerated (comment 524-527) — worth fuzzing.\n\n## 4. substitute_callout path\n\n- Called only if `mcontext != NULL && mcontext->substitute_callout != NULL` (1648) **and** `!overflowed` (1652).\n- Block `pcre2_substitute_callout_block scb`: `version=0` (930), `input=subject` (931), `output=(PCRE2_SPTR)buffer` (932), `ovector` (933), `oveccount = rc` i.e. match's pair count or `ovector_count` when rc==0 (1043, 1047), `output_offsets[0] = buff_offset` before replacement (1046), `output_offsets[1] = buff_offset` after (1655), `subscount = subs` (1654).\n- Return handling 1662-1674: `0` → keep substitution; `!=0` → rewind (`buff_offset -= newlength`, `lengthleft += newlength`, 1667-1668) and copy the original matched fragment instead (1669, skipped under REPLACEMENT_ONLY); `<0` additionally clears `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_GLOBAL` (1673) so the loop stops after this iteration. Note `subs` is **not** decremented, so the returned count still includes rejected substitutions.\n- `overflowed` branch 1686-1709: callout is *not* invoked; requests the max of accept/reject lengths (`oldlength > newlength` → `extra_needed += oldlength-newlength`, 1698-1704); integer overflow → `TOOLARGEREPLACE`. So the callout is invisible in a length-only first pass — differential axis: same call with a big buffer vs `blength` too small.\n\n## 5. Two-pass / overflow bookkeeping\n\n- Macros: `CHECKMEMCPY` 638-660 (three-way: `overflowed` → accumulate `extra_needed` 641-646 with `TOOLARGEREPLACE` on integer overflow 643; `lengthleft < len` → NOROOM unless OVERFLOW_LENGTH, then set `overflowed` and `extra_needed = len - lengthleft` 647-652; else memcpy and advance 653-658). `CHECKCASECPY_BASE` 668-685 (note: no `overflowed`-accumulate arm; the DEFAULT variant handles that at 691-699 by passing capacity 0 and adding to `extra_needed`).\n- `CHECKMEMCPY` call sites: 965 (prefix up to start_offset), 1045 (between-matches fragment), 1056 (LITERAL replacement), 1350 (MARK), 1463 (group/subject fragment), 1575 (escaped char), 1630 (literal code unit), 1669 (callout-rejected fragment), 1738 (tail), 1742 (trailing NUL).\n- Final accounting: `overflowed` → `rc = PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`, `*blength = buff_length + extra_needed` (1748-1755); else `rc = subs`, `*blength = buff_offset - 1` (1760-1764, i.e. excludes NUL).\n- Buffer-size input axes worth tabulating: `*blength == 0` (even the NUL at 1742 overflows); exactly `needed-1`; exactly `needed` (must succeed, `lengthleft` hits 0 only on the NUL); `needed+1`; with `start_offset > 0` and `REPLACEMENT_ONLY` on/off; overflow occurring *inside* a case-forced run so `DELAYEDFORCECASE` takes the pessimistic-guess arm (720-726) rather than the rewind arm (728-733).\n- `casestart_offset`/`casestart_extra_needed` (976-977, 1537-1538) plus `chars_outstanding = (buff_offset-casestart_offset)+(extra_needed-casestart_extra_needed)` (716-717) — the \"straddling\" case (case run started before overflow, ended after) is the interesting one.\n- `sub_start_extra_needed` (1048, used 1689) isolates one substitution's contribution for the overflowed-callout estimate.\n\n## 6. GLOBAL loop\n\n- Loop 971-1730. Continuation is fully delegated in 10.48-DEV: `pcre2_next_match(match_data, &start_offset, &goptions)` at 1716; on FALSE, `start_offset = ovector[1]` and break (1718-1719). `goptions` initialised 751 and OR'd into the match options at 984.\n- There is **no** `PCRE2_ANCHORED` retry in this version. The empty-match logic lives in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wwiWoN/c_src/src/pcre2_match_next.c`: empty match → `*poptions = PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART` at the same offset (147-160), end-of-subject → stop (151-152); `\\K` zero-progress case (`ovector[0] != start_offset && ovector[1] == start_offset`) → `do_bumpalong` (129-141); CRLF atomic skip (61-71, only for `PCRE2_NEWLINE_CRLF/ANY/ANYCRLF`) and UTF `FORWARDCHARTEST` character advance (75-85) in `do_bumpalong` (49-88).\n- Consequence for testing: `pcre2_substitute` itself never memcpys a bumpa