{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_scbd4vhidq53f7kcwlj3pm5j3cyv2glbp377kt7rdccx3pszpfpa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Findings below. All paths absolute: files are in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wwiWoN/c_src/src/`.\n\n---\n\n# A) pcre2_convert.c — `pcre2_pattern_convert()` (1116-1237)\n\n## A1. Option masks / accept-reject\n| Check | Line | Shape |\n|---|---|---|\n| `TYPE_OPTIONS` = GLOB \\| POSIX_BASIC \\| POSIX_EXTENDED | 46-47 | |\n| `ALL_OPTIONS` = UTF \\| NO_UTF_CHECK \\| GLOB_NO_WILD_SEPARATOR \\| GLOB_NO_STARSTAR \\| TYPE_OPTIONS | 49-52 | |\n| `pattern==NULL && plength==0` → substitute `null_str` (`{0xcd}`) | 1122, 1129-1130 | legal \"empty pattern\" via NULL |\n| `pattern==NULL` (plength≠0) or `bufflenptr==NULL` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL`; sets `*bufflenptr=0` only if non-NULL | 1132-1136 | |\n| undefined bit set (`options & ~ALL_OPTIONS`) → BADOPTION, offset 0 | 1138, 1143 | e.g. `0x80000000` |\n| more than one type bit (`(pattype & (~pattype+1)) != pattype`) → BADOPTION | 1139 | GLOB\\|POSIX_BASIC, all three, etc. |\n| `pattype == 0` → BADOPTION | 1140 | UTF alone, NO_STARSTAR alone, 0 |\n| `plength == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` → strlen | 1146 | |\n| `ccontext == NULL` → `PRIV(default_convert_context)` | 1147-1148 (defaults: pcre2_context.c:199-208; non-Win sep `/`, escape `\\`) |\n| dispatch GLOB (options with GLOB bit *cleared*) | 1190-1193 | |\n| dispatch POSIX_BASIC / POSIX_EXTENDED (pattype passed through) | 1195-1199 | |\n| unreachable default → INTERNAL | 1203-1207 | |\n| unreachable post-loop → INTERNAL | 1233-1236 | |\n\nNote: `GLOB_NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` / `GLOB_NO_STARSTAR` are silently *accepted but ignored* for the POSIX converters (never inspected in `convert_posix`, 149-384).\n\n## A2. UTF / NO_UTF_CHECK\n- `utf = (options & PCRE2_CONVERT_UTF) != 0` — 1126.\n- no-Unicode build: `UNICODE_NOT_SUPPORTED`, offset 0 — 1152-1157 (not compiled here).\n- `utf && !NO_UTF_CHECK` → `PRIV(valid_utf)`; on failure returns the UTF error code and sets `*bufflenptr = erroroffset` — 1159-1168. Shapes: valid UTF-8, truncated/overlong/surrogate/5-byte, plus same input with NO_UTF_CHECK set (skips check, then feeds ill-formed bytes to GETCHARLENTEST at 194 / GETCHARINCTEST at 705,753,760,784).\n- posix converter: `utf` only affects `GETCHARLENTEST` multi-unit copying (194, 243, 371) — `(void)utf` at 166 for non-Unicode.\n- glob converter: `utf` only used for the ASCII sep/escape guard 867-874 and `GETCHARINCTEST` (705 etc.).\n\n## A3. Two-pass length/output logic (1174-1229)\nThree distinct caller shapes:\n1. `buffptr == NULL` → length-only; `dummyrun` TRUE; single pass; writes into `dummy_buffer[100]` (1123-1125); returns after first iteration (1211).\n2. `buffptr != NULL && *buffptr == NULL` → pass 1 `dummyrun=TRUE` into the 100-byte dummy buffer to compute length; allocate `sizeof(pcre2_memctl) + (*bufflenptr+1)*width` (1218-1219); `*buffptr` set past the hidden memctl (1225); `use_length = *bufflenptr + 1` (1228); pass 2 real. NOMEMORY at 1220-1224 sets offset 0.\n3. `buffptr != NULL && *buffptr != NULL` → caller buffer; `use_buffer=*buffptr`, `use_length=*bufflenptr` (1174-1178); `dummyrun=FALSE`; single pass. Interesting shape: `*bufflenptr` exactly = needed, one too small (→ NOMEMORY), 0, 1.\n\n`dummyrun` semantics differ between converters:\n- posix: on dummy run `p` is reset to `use_buffer` each iteration (185-187) so 100 bytes always suffice; `convlength` accumulates. On non-dummy overflow → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` from `PUTCHARS` (73-80, `endp = p+use_length-1` reserves the trailing NUL, 157).\n- glob: never bounds-checks; `convert_glob_write`/`_write_str` (408-444) count into `output_size` and only store while `output < output_end`. Non-dummy mismatch `output_size != output-use_buffer` → NOMEMORY at 1082-1083. `*bufflenptr = out.output_size - 1` on success (1092).\n\nError-offset convention: posix sets `*bufflenptr = plength` up-front (171) then final `convlength` (381); glob sets `pattern - pattern_start` on error (1088) and `0` for the UTF sep/escape error (871).\n\n## A4. `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX` — exactly 4 sites (glob only)\n- 872: `utf` and (`separator >= 128 || escape >= 128`) — unreachable via the public setters (they restrict to ASCII), reachable only by direct struct poke.\n- 765: `-` range whose right end is `[:` (e.g. `[a-[:digit:]]`).\n- 771: reversed range `prev_c > c` (e.g. `[z-a]`, `[9-0]`).\n- 1056: escape char is the final code unit (e.g. `abc\\` with escape `\\`).\n\nOther glob errors: `MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET` at 654 (`[` at end), 665 (`[!`/`[^` at end), 803 (unterminated class body); `NOMEMORY` 1083.\nPOSIX errors: `END_BACKSLASH` 303, `MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET` 379, `NOMEMORY` 77/242/309/339/370.\n\n## A5. POSIX converter — special-cased input syntax (`convert_posix`, 149-384)\nShared state machine: `POSIX_START_REGEX / ANCHORED / NOT_BRACKET / CLASS_NOT_STARTED / CLASS_STARTING / CLASS_STARTED` (68-69), `bracount`, `lastspecial`, `nextisliteral`.\n\nPrologue: always emits `(*NUL)` (`STR_STAR_NUL`, 64, emitted 172).\n\nInside a class (`posix_state >= POSIX_CLASS_NOT_STARTED`, 204-246):\n- `]` closes class → 206-210.\n- `[:name:]` recognition: CLASS_STARTED + lowercase run (219, `ISLOWER` 84-90), `:]` → emitted verbatim 221-228; `[` → CLASS_STARTING 232-233; `:` after `[` → CLASS_STARTED 236-238.\n- `\\` inside class is doubled → 241.\n- multi-unit UTF char copied verbatim → 242-244.\n\nOutside a class (250-375):\n| Element | Lines | Basic vs Extended |\n|---|---|---|\n| `[` (start class, plus leading `^` and leading `]`) | 252-300 (281 state; 287-292 `^`; 293-298 `]`) | same |\n| `\\` at end of pattern | 303 → END_BACKSLASH | same |\n| `\\X` | 302-315 | extended: next char literal (304). basic: `\\(`,`\\)`,`\\{`,`\\}`,`\\1`-`\\9` are metas (`posix_meta_escapes` 103-106) — digits get `\\` prefix (308); anything else literal (313) |\n| `)` | 317-320 | extended with `bracount>0` → special, decrement; else escaped literal |\n| `(` | 322-323 | extended: special + `bracount++`; basic: escaped literal (331) |\n| `?` `+` `{` `}` `|` | 326-331 | extended: copied; basic: escaped literal |\n| `.` `$` | 334-341 | always copied special; sets NOT_BRACKET |\n| `*` | 343-351 | repeated `*` collapsed (344, 351); basic: leading `*` or `*` right after `(` → escaped literal (346-348) |\n| `^` | 353-360 | extended: always special (354); basic: special only at START_REGEX or after `(` → ANCHORED (355-359), else literal |\n| other char in `pcre2_escaped_literals` (94-99) | 363-368 | prefixed with `\\`; `lastspecial=0xff` (369) |\n| unterminated class at EOF | 378-379 | MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET |\n\nDead/unused generated fragments (defined 58-63, never referenced): `STR_BACKSLASH_A`, `STR_BACKSLASH_z`, `STR_DOT_STAR_LOOKBEHIND`, `STR_LOOKAHEAD_NOT_DOT`, `STR_QUERY_s`. The `[[:<:]]`/`[[:>:]]` handling is `#ifdef NEVER` (255-277). **There is no leading-`.` special case in either converter** (glob does not hide dotfiles).\n\n## A6. Glob converter — `convert_glob` (846-1094)\nPrologue: `(?s)` always (883-887). `\\A` prefix emitted unless the pattern starts with `*` and (`no_wildsep`, 893-894) or (`**` and `!no_starstar`, 895-897) — 891-905.\n\n`*` (911-1033):\n- `is_start` = `*` is first unit (913); close pending atomic group `)` if `in_atomic` (915-919).\n- `**` branch, requires `!no_starstar` and next unit `*` (921):\n  - `after_separator = is_start || pattern[-2]==separator` (923).\n  - collapse run of `*` (925-926); `***…` at EOF → `no_slash_z=TRUE`, break (928-932).\n  - `after_starstar = TRUE` (934).\n  - `after_separator && escape!=0 && next==escape && next2==separator` → skip escape (936-938) e.g. `a/**\\/b`.\n  - `is_start`: next != separator → emit nothing, continue (940-942); next == separator → `(?:\\A|SEP)` (944-956).\n  - non-start: `(*COMMIT)` (959, printer 813-826); then `!after_separator || next!=separator` → `.*?` (961-967); else `(?:.*?SEP)??` (970-987).\n- single-`*` branch (990-1032): collapse `*` run (990-994); `no_wildsep`: `*` at EOF → `no_slash_z` break (996-1002), `is_start` → continue (1005); non-start prefix: `(?>` (atomic) if `after_starstar` (1010-1016) else `(*COMMIT)` (1019); body `.` if `no_wildsep` (1023) else `[^SEP]` (1025, printer 474-485); quantifier `*?`, or `*+` when at end of pattern (1027-1031).\n\n`?` (1035-1042): `.` if `no_wildsep`, else `[^SEP]`.\n\n`[` (1044-1050) → `convert_glob_parse_range` (636-804):\n- empty after `[` → MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET (651-655).\n- `[!…` or `[^…` negation (657-685): emits `[^`, and unless `no_wildsep` also (optional `\\`) + separator (674-682); `[!` at EOF → error (662-666).\n- non-negated: plain `[` (687).\n- leading `]` literalized as `\\]` and becomes `prev_c` (692-700).\n- loop 702-800: closing `]` (707-725) — if `!is_negative && !no_wildsep && separator_seen`, append `(?<!SEP)` (711-721).\n- POSIX class `[:xxx:]` (729-746) via `convert_glob_parse_class` (499-551, table `posix_classes` 110-124, 14 classes: alpha lower upper alnum ascii blank cntrl digit graph print punct space word xdigit); malformed class falls through to literal handling (734); if `!is_negative` and the class contains the separator → `separator_seen` (741-743) via `convert_glob_char_in_class` (563-621, uses `PRIV(default_tables)`; note `[[:punct:]]`/`[[:graph:]]`/`[[:print:]]`/`[[:ascii:]]` contain `/`, `\\`, `.`).\n- range `x-y` (747-778): escaped right end (757-761); `[:` as right end → CONVERT_SYNTAX (762-766); `prev_c > c` → CONVERT_SYNTAX (768-772); `prev_c < separator < c` → `separator_seen` (774). `-` immediately before `]` is a literal (748).\n- plain member, with optional escape (779-791); truncation after escape → break → MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET (786, 802-803).\n- members `[`, `]`, `\\`, `-` get a `\\` prefix (793-795); `c == separator` sets `separator_seen` (797).\n\nEscape char outside class (1052-1060): `escape != 0 && c == escape` → consume next literally; escape at EOF → CONVERT_SYNTAX.\nLiteral metachar escaping (1062-1065) against `pcre2_escaped_literals` (94-99).\nEpilogue (1068-1084): `\\z` unless `no_slash_z` (1070-1075); close atomic `)` (1077-1078); NUL (1080); size check (1082-1083).\n\nInput shapes worth enumerating: `*`, `**`, `***`, `?`, `a?b`, `[abc]`, `[!abc]`, `[^abc]`, `[]abc]`, `[a-z]`, `[z-a]`, `[[:digit:]]`, `[[:punct:]]`, `[a-[:digit:]]`, `[a`, `[!`, `[`, `**/x`, `/**`, `a/**/b`, `a/**\\/b`, `**` at end, `*` at end, `\\*`, trailing `\\`, empty pattern; each × {no_wildsep, no_starstar} × {sep `/`,`\\`,`.`} × {escape 0, `\\`, `` ` ``, other punct} × {utf on/off}.\n\n## A7. `glob_escape` / `glob_separator` effect on output\nSetters: `pcre2_set_glob_separator` accepts only `/` `\\` `.` else `PCRE2_ERROR_BADDATA` — pcre2_context.c:528-535. `pcre2_set_glob_escape` accepts `0` (disable) or any ASCII punctuation in `globpunct` (pcre2_context.c:537-554); `>255` or non-punct → BADDATA.\n\n- `escape == 0`: escape processing disabled at all 4 sites (757, 781, 936, 1052) → `\\` becomes a literal (and is emitted as `\\\\` via 793-795 / 1062-1063); trailing-escape CONVERT_SYNTAX unreachable.\n- `escape == '\\\\'` (default): `\\x` → literal `x`; `\\` at EOF → CONVERT_SYNTAX.\n- `escape` = other punct (e.g. `` ` ``, `!`, `*`): that char becomes the escape *and* loses its own glob meaning; if the escape is `*` or `[` the earlier `*`/`[` branches (911, 1044) win, so it never reaches 1052 — asymmetric behaviour worth differential coverage.\n- `with_escape = strchr(pcre2_escaped_literals, separator) != NULL` (876) → TRUE for `\\` and `.`, FALSE for `/`. Adds a `\\` before every emitted separator at 459-460 (used by 482, 719, 952, 979) and inside the negated-class prefix (676-679).\n- separator identity also drives: `pattern[-2]==separator` in `**` (923), `*pattern==separator` decisions (942, 961), `c==separator` in ranges (774, 797), `convert_glob_char_in_class(class_index, separator)` (742), and `[^SEP]` wildcards (481).\n- `no_wildsep` (GLOB_NO_WILD_SEPARATOR) removes all separator awareness: `.` instead of `[^SEP]` (1023, 1038), no separator in negated class (674), no `(?<!SEP)` (711), and changes the `\\A` prefix decision (893).\n\n---\n\n# B) pcre2_serialize.c\n\nConstants: magic `0x50523253` (52), version `MAJOR|(MINOR<<16)` (57-58), config `sizeof(PCRE2_UCHAR) | sizeof(void*)<<8 | sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE)<<16` (60-61). Header struct: pcre2_internal.h:2169-2174 (4 words, 16 bytes). `TABLES_LENGTH = ctypes_offset+256` (pcre2_internal.h:598).\n\n## `pcre2_serialize_encode` (69-153)\n| Branch | Line | Input shape |\n|---|---|---|\n| gcontext NULL → default compile context memctl | 82-83 | |\n| `codes==NULL \\|\\| serialized_bytes==NULL \\|\\| serialized_size==NULL` → NULL | 85-86 | any of the 3 NULL |\n| `number_of_codes <= 0` → BADDATA | 88 | 0, -1, INT32_MIN |\n| base size = header + TABLES_LENGTH | 91 | |\n| `codes[i]==NULL` → NULL | 96 | array with a NULL hole (e.g. {code, NULL}) |\n| bad magic → BADMAGIC | 98 | freed/garbage/wrong-width code |\n| first code sets `tables` | 99-100 | |\n| `tables != re->tables` → MIXEDTABLES | 101-102 | ≥2 codes where one was compiled with a custom `pcre2_maketables` table set via compile context and the other with the built-in default |\n| accumulate `re->blocksize` | 103 | |\n| malloc failure → NOMEMORY | 107-108 | |\n| hidden memctl prefix written | 111-112 | consumed by `pcre2_serialize_free` 285-293 |\n| header fields written | 114-118 | |\n| tables blob copied once | 122-123 | single shared table set only |\n| per-code copy + zeroing of `memctl`, `tables`, `executable_jit` | 125-148 (140-145) | makes output byte-identical across runs |\n| returns `number_of_codes` | 152 | |\n\nNote `number_of_codes` larger than the real array length is not detectable → OOB read (shape to avoid/fuzz carefully).\n\n## `pcre2_serialize_decode` (160-260)\n| Branch | Line | Shape |\n|---|---|---|\n| gcontext NULL → default memctl | 165-166 | |\n| `bytes==NULL \\|\\| codes==NULL` → NULL | 176 | |\n| `number_of_codes <= 0` → BADDATA | 177 | |\n| `data->number_of_codes <= 0` → **BADSERIALIZEDDATA** | 178 | header count field zeroed/negative |\n| magic mismatch → BADMAGIC | 179 | first 4 bytes corrupted; also byte-swapped stream (opposite-endian producer) hits this, since magic is compared as a native `uint32_t` — no explicit byte-order field/check exists |\n| version mismatch → BADMODE | 180 | stream from a different PCRE2 major/minor |\n| config mismatch → BADMODE | 181 | different code-unit width (8 vs 16 vs 32), different pointer size (32- vs 64-bit), different `PCRE2_SIZE` |\n| clamp requested count to stored count | 183-184 | request 5 from a 2-code stream → returns 2 |\n| tables copy + refcount stored at `tables+TABLES_LENGTH` = `number_of_codes` (the clamped value) | 191-196 | requesting fewer codes than stored leaves a refcount equal to the number actually created |\n| alignment-safe `blocksize` read via `memcpy` at `offsetof(pcre2_real_code, blocksize)` | 206-208 | deliberately tolerates an unaligned stream (`bytes` need not be aligned) |\n| `blocksize <= sizeof(pcre2_real_code)` → **BADSERIALIZEDDATA** | 209-213 | truncated/zeroed blocksize |\n| per-code malloc failure → NOMEMORY | 217-223 | |\n| copy preserving the fresh memctl (`blocksize - sizeof(pcre2_memctl)` from offset `sizeof(pcre2_memctl)`) | 227-228 | |\n| `dst_re->magic_number != MAGIC_NUMBER` → **BADSERIALIZEDDATA** | 229 | code body corrupted |\n| `name_entry_size > MAX_NAME_SIZE + IMM2_SIZE + 1` (128+2+1=131) → **BADSERIALIZEDDATA** | 230 | |\n| `name_count > MAX_NAME_COUNT` (10000) → **BADSERIALIZEDDATA** | 231 | |\n| set `tables`, `executable_jit=NULL`, `flags |= PCRE2_DEREF_TABLES` | 239-241 | tables are shared+refcounted across all decoded codes |\n| success → returns count | 248 | |\n| cleanup: frees pending `dst_re`, the tables, and `codes[0..i-1]`, NULLing them | 250-259 | any failure at code index i>0 |\n\n## `pcre2_serialize_get_number_of_codes` (267-278)\nNULL 272; magic 273; version 274; config 275; else `data->number_of_codes` 277 — note it does **not** reject `<= 0`, unlike decode (178), so a zeroed count returns 0 here but BADSERIALIZEDDATA there.\n\n## `pcre2_serialize_free` (285-293)\nNULL no-op 288; otherwise frees `bytes - sizeof(pcre2_memctl)` 290-291.\n\n---\n\n# C) pcre2_pattern_info.c\n\n## Length-query mode (`where == NULL`), 66-105\nReturns a size **before** any `re` validation, so `pcre2_pattern_info(NULL, KEY, NULL)` succeeds for known keys:\n- `sizeof(uint32_t)` for ALLOPTIONS, ARGOPTIONS, BACKREFMAX, BSR, CAPTURECOUNT, DEPTHLIMIT, EXTRAOPTIONS, FIRSTCODETYPE, FIRSTCODEUNIT, HASBACKSLASHC, HASCRORLF, HEAPLIMIT, JCHANGED, LASTCODETYPE, LASTCODEUNIT, MATCHEMPTY, MATCHLIMIT, MAXLOOKBEHIND, MINLENGTH, NAMEENTRYSIZE, NAMECOUNT, NEWLINE — 70-92.\n- `sizeof(const uint8_t *)` FIRSTBITMAP — 94-95.\n- `sizeof(size_t)` JITSIZE, SIZE, FRAMESIZE — 97-100.\n- `sizeof(PCRE2_SPTR)` NAMETABLE — 102-103.\n- Unknown key with NULL `where` falls through → 107 (`re==NULL` → PCRE2_ERROR_NULL) or 242 (BADOPTION).\n\n## Common gates\n`re == NULL` → NULL (107); `magic_number != MAGIC_NUMBER` → BADMAGIC (112); `(re->flags & (WIDTH/8)) == 0` → BADMODE (116, i.e. 8-bit code passed to a different-width library).\n\n## Per-key\n| Key | Line | Non-trivial pattern shape |\n|---|---|---|\n| ALLOPTIONS | 120-122 | `overall_options`; differs from ARGOPTIONS when in-pattern `(*UTF)`, `(*UCP)`, `(*ANY)`, `(?i)` at start, `(*LIMIT_*)`, auto-anchor |\n| ARGOPTIONS | 124-125 | exactly the compile-time `options` argument |\n| BACKREFMAX | 128-129 | `top_backref`: 0 for no backrefs; N for `(a)(b)\\2`; also raised by `\\g{-1}`, `(?P=name)`, recursion-free named refs |\n| BSR | 132-133 | set by `(*BSR_ANYCRLF)`/`(*BSR_UNICODE)` or compile context |\n| CAPTURECOUNT | 136-137 | `top_bracket` |\n| DEPTHLIMIT | 140-143 | **returns PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET when `UINT32_MAX`** — non-trivial only with `(*LIMIT_DEPTH=n)` |\n| EXTRAOPTIONS | 145-146 | non-zero only via `pcre2_set_compile_extra_options` (ALLOW_SURROGATE_ESCAPES, BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL, MATCH_WORD/LINE, ESCAPED_CR_IS_LF, ALT_BSUX, ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK, CASELESS_RESTRICT, ASCII_*, etc.) |\n| FIRSTCODETYPE | 149-152 | **3-way**: 1 if `PCRE2_FIRSTSET` (`abc`, `^` absent but fixed first unit); 2 if `PCRE2_STARTLINE` (`^abc` multiline, `.*abc`); 0 otherwise (`\\d`, `a|b` with differing units, anchored) |\n| FIRSTCODEUNIT | 154-157 | value only when FIRSTSET, else 0 |\n| FIRSTBITMAP | 159-162 | non-NULL only when `PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET` — e.g. `[ab]x`, `a|b`, `\\d+`; NULL when FIRSTSET or nothing known |\n| FRAMESIZE | 164-166 | `offsetof(heapframe, ovector) + top_bracket*2*sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE)` — grows with capture count |\n| HASBACKSLASHC | 169-170 | `\\cX` anywhere in the pattern (`PCRE2_HASBKC`) |\n| HASCRORLF | 173-174 | pattern literally contains CR or LF (or `\\r`/`\\n`/`\\x0a` literal), `PCRE2_HASCRORLF` |\n| HEAPLIMIT | 177-180 | **UNSET if UINT32_MAX**; set by `(*LIMIT_HEAP=n)` |\n| JCHANGED | 182-183 | `(?J)` / `(?J:...)` inside the pattern (not the `PCRE2_DUPNAMES` option) |\n| JITSIZE | 186-193 | **no-JIT build → always 0** (191) |\n| LASTCODETYPE | 195-197 | 1 iff `PCRE2_LASTSET` (a required later unit, e.g. `ab`, `a.*b`); 0 otherwise |\n| LASTCODEUNIT | 199-202 | value only when LASTSET |\n| MATCHEMPTY | 204-206 | `PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY`: `a*`, `(?:)`, `\\b`, `()` — vs `a+` |\n| MATCHLIMIT | 208-211 | **UNSET if UINT32_MAX**; `(*LIMIT_MATCH=n)` |\n| MAXLOOKBEHIND | 213-215 | 0 with no lookbehind; N for `(?<=abc)`, `\\K`-free variable lookbehind, `(?<!ab)` |\n| MINLENGTH | 217-219 | study result; 0 for `a*`/alternation with empty branch; >0 for `abc`, `a{3}` |\n| NAMEENTRYSIZE | 221-222 | `IMM2_SIZE + longest name + 1`; 0 when no named groups |\n| NAMECOUNT | 225-226 | number of name table entries; duplicates under `(?J)`/DUPNAMES produce multiple entries for one name |\n| NAMETABLE | 229-232 | always `re + sizeof(pcre2_real_code)` — meaningless unless NAMECOUNT>0; must be read with NAMEENTRYSIZE stride |\n| NEWLINE | 234-236 | `(*CR)`, `(*LF)`, `(*CRLF)`, `(*ANY)`, `(*ANYCRLF)`, `(*NUL)` or compile context |\n| SIZE | 238-240 | `blocksize` in bytes = header + name table + compiled code; grows with pattern size and LINK_SIZE |\n| default | 242 | BADOPTION |\n| success | 245 | 0 |\n\n## `pcre2_callout_enumerate()` (265-428)\n- `re == NULL` → NULL (276). `utf` read from `overall_options` (279) **before** the magic check.\n- magic → BADMAGIC (285); width flag → BADMODE (289).\n- `cb.version = 0` (291); start at `re + re->code_start` (292).\n- Opcode-skip classes (branch shapes to exercise):\n  - `OP_END` → return 0 (299-300).\n  - char/repeat opcodes 302-357: `OP_lengths` + `HAS_EXTRALEN`/`GET_EXTRALEN` extra when `utf` (358-361) → UTF pattern with a multi-byte literal, e.g. `/\\x{100}+/utf`.\n  - TYPE* opcodes 364-376: `+2` when the type is `OP_PROP`/`OP_NOTPROP` (379) → `\\p{L}*`.\n  - `OP_XCLASS` / `OP_ECLASS` (383-388, `SUPPORT_WIDE_CHARS`): skip via `GET(cc,1)` → `[\\x{100}-\\x{200}]`, `[[a-z]&&[^q]]`.\n  - `OP_MARK`, `OP_COMMIT_ARG`, `OP_PRUNE_ARG`, `OP_SKIP_ARG`, `OP_THEN_ARG` (390-396): length + `cc[1]` (arg length) → `(*MARK:X)` etc.\n  - `OP_CALLOUT` (398-408): numeric; `pattern_position = GET(cc,1)`, `next_item_length = GET(cc,1+LINK_SIZE)`, `callout_number = cc[1+2*LINK_SIZE]`, string fields zeroed/NULL → `(?C)`, `(?C1)`, `(?C255)`, auto-callout (`PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT`).\n  - `OP_CALLOUT_STR` (410-421): `callout_number = 0`, `callout_string_offset = GET(cc,1+3*LINK_SIZE)`, `callout_string_length = GET(cc,1+2*LINK_SIZE) - (1+4*LINK_SIZE) - 2`, `callout_string = cc + (1+4*LINK_SIZE) + 1`; advance by `GET(cc,1+2*LINK_SIZE)` → `(?C\"txt\")`, `(?C{txt})`, `(?C[]`…), empty string `(?C\"\")`.\n  - default (423-425): plain `OP_lengths` advance.\n- Non-zero callback return propagated immediately (406, 419) — callback returning >0 and <0 are both distinct shapes.\n\n---\n\n# D) pcre2_config.c — `pcre2_config(what, where)` (70-248)\n\n`where == NULL` length-query switch, 73-103:\n- `default: return PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION` (77-78).\n- returns `sizeof(uint32_t)` (94) for: BSR (80), COMPILED_WIDTHS (81), DEPTHLIMIT (82), EFFECTIVE_LINKSIZE (83), HEAPLIMIT (84), JIT (85), LINKSIZE (86), MATCHLIMIT (87), NEVER_BACKSLASH_C (88), NEWLINE (89), PARENSLIMIT (90), STACKRECURSE (91), TABLES_LENGTH (92), UNICODE (93).\n- JITTARGET (98), UNICODE_VERSION (99), VERSION (100) `break` out (101) and are handled by the *main* switch, which returns `1 + strlen(v)` — these three are the only true \"string length queries\".\n\nMain switch, 105-245:\n| Key | Line | Value in this build |\n|---|---|---|\n| default | 107-108 | BADOPTION |\n| BSR | 110-116 | `PCRE2_BSR_UNICODE` (2) unless `BSR_ANYCRLF` |\n| COMPILED_WIDTHS | 118-130 | bitmask; 8-bit only → 1 |\n| DEPTHLIMIT | 132-134 | `MATCH_LIMIT_DEPTH` |\n| EFFECTIVE_LINKSIZE | 136-138 | `LINK_SIZE * sizeof(PCRE2_UCHAR)` = 2 for 8-bit/LINK_SIZE=2 |\n| HEAPLIMIT | 140-142 | `HEAP_LIMIT` |\n| JIT | 144-150 | 0 (no JIT) |\n| JITTARGET | 152-161 | **no-JIT → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION` (160)**, both with and without NULL `where`; note the NULL-`where` switch `break`s at 98 so it reaches 160 |\n| LINKSIZE | 163-165 | `CONFIGURED_LINK_SIZE` (2) — distinct from EFFECTIVE_LINKSIZE at 16/32-bit |\n| MATCHLIMIT | 167-169 | `MATCH_LIMIT` |\n| NEWLINE | 171-173 | `NEWLINE_DEFAULT` |\n| NEVER_BACKSLASH_C | 175-181 | 0 unless `NEVER_BACKSLASH_C` |\n| PARENSLIMIT | 183-185 | `PARENS_NEST_LIMIT` |\n| STACKRECURSE | 190-192 | always 0 (obsolete) |\n| TABLES_LENGTH | 194-196 | `TABLES_LENGTH` |\n| UNICODE_VERSION | 198-207 | returns `1+len`; with `where` non-NULL copies via `PRIV(strcpy_c8)`; SUPPORT_UNICODE defined → real version string (else `\"Unicode not supported\"`) |\n| UNICODE | 209-215 | 1 here |\n| VERSION | 236-243 | returns `1+len`; runtime empty-prerelease test at 238-240 |\n| fallthrough | 247 | `return 0` for all numeric keys |\n\nBuffer-shape hazard fo