066 | 16/32-bit code fed to 8-bit lib |\n| `(*NOTEMPTY)` / `(*NOTEMPTY_ATSTART)` pattern flags folded into `options` (bit-shift trick) | M:7079-7084 | pattern begins `(*NOTEMPTY)` |\n| UTF/UCP/invalid-UTF flags read | M:7098-7100 | |\n| `mb->partial` = 2 (HARD) / 1 (SOFT) / 0 | M:7105-7107 | |\n| partial + ENDANCHORED (pattern **or** match option) → `BADOPTION` | M:7111-7113 | |\n| offset_limit set without `PCRE2_USE_OFFSET_LIMIT` at compile → `BADOFFSETLIMIT` | M:7117-7120 | |\n| free previous `PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT` buffer; `match_data->subject=NULL` | M:7126-7132 | reused match_data |\n| `match_data->startchar = 0` | M:7136 | |\n| JIT block (dead here: no JIT) | M:7139-7241 | |\n| `mb->check_subject = subject` (default lookbehind floor) | M:7251 | |\n| UTF validity check, non-JIT | M:7271-7386 | `utf && (!NO_UTF_CHECK \\|\\| allow_invalid)` |\n| first-CU-is-continuation: skip if `allow_invalid` (M:7285-7291); else `BADUTFOFFSET` if `start_offset>0` (M:7294-7296) else `UTF8_ERR20` (M:7298) | | subject starting `\\x80` |\n| `check_subject` rewound by `re->max_lookbehind` characters | M:7304-7331 | pattern has lookbehind + nonzero start_offset |\n| `PRIV(valid_utf)` loop; `rc>0 \\|\\| !allow_invalid` → return error; else fragment logic | M:7343-7385 | see §8 |\n| `mcontext==NULL` → `PRIV(default_match_context)`, memctl from pattern | M:7391-7396 | |\n| `anchored`, `firstline`, `startline`, `bumpalong_limit` | M:7398-7402 | see §2 |\n| callout block init (`cb.version=2`) | M:7407-7411 | |\n| `mb->hasthen`, `hasbsk`, `allowemptypartial`, `allowlookaroundbsk`, `poptions` | M:7422-7429 | `allowemptypartial = max_lookbehind>0 \\|\\| PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY` (M:7424-7425) |\n| name table / start_code | M:7436-7439 | |\n| newline + bsr | M:7443-7479 (see §7) | |\n| `frame_size = (offsetof(heapframe,ovector) + top_bracket*2*sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE) + HEAPFRAME_ALIGNMENT-1) & ~(HEAPFRAME_ALIGNMENT-1)` | M:7495-7497 | `HEAPFRAME_ALIGNMENT` = `pcre2_intmodedep.h:1031` |\n| limits: `min(mcontext->X, re->limit_X)` — pattern `(*LIMIT_HEAP=)`, `(*LIMIT_MATCH=)`, `(*LIMIT_DEPTH=)` only tighten | M:7502-7509 | |\n| `heapframes_size = frame_size*10`, floor `START_FRAMES_SIZE` = 20480 (`I:225`) | M:7516-7517 | |\n| `heapframes_size/1024 > heap_limit` → clamp to `1024*heap_limit`; if `max_size < frame_size` → `HEAPLIMIT` immediately | M:7518-7524 | e.g. 60000 capture groups + `(*LIMIT_HEAP=1)` |\n| grow/realloc only if `match_data->heapframes_size < heapframes_size`; `NULL` → `heapframes_size=0` + `NOMEMORY` | M:7528-7541 | |\n| `memset(...+offsetof(ovector), 0xff, frame_size-offsetof(ovector))` — frame-0 ovector preset to UNSET | M:7545-7546 | |\n| char tables `lcc/fcc/ctypes` | M:7550-7552 | |\n| `PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT` on success: malloc+memcpy, `length==0` → subject NULL; else `match_data->subject = original_subject` | M:8187-8202 | |\n\nReturn-value shaping: success `rc = (end_offset_top >= 2*oveccount)? 0 : end_offset_top/2+1` (M:8172-8173); partial (M:8222-8233); nomatch (M:8237-8243). `oveccount` is forced ≥1 by `pcre2_match_data_create` (`pcre2_match_data.c:57`), so `ovector[0..1]` writes at M:1046-1047 are always in range.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Start-of-match optimization (M:7554-7947)\n\nVariable setup:\n- `has_first_cu`/`first_cu`/`first_cu2` ← `PCRE2_FIRSTSET` / `PCRE2_FIRSTCASELESS` (M:7557-7570). Flags set at C:11148-11176 (also from *asserted* first CU, C:11128-11143, e.g. `/(?=a)ab/`), and possibly *replaced* from a 1–2-entry start bitmap by the study pass at S:2024-2038 (`[Ww]ord`, `(word|WORD)`). 8-bit + `ucp && !utf && first_cu>127` → `UCD_OTHERCASE` (M:7566).\n- `start_bits` ← `re->start_bitmap` only if `!startline && PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET` (M:7573-7575). Bitmap built by `set_start_bits()` S:1093-1880 (`study_char_list` S:943, class map S:1840/1856, 8-bit UTF wide-char blanket bits S:1805-1806). Pattern shape: `/[abc]x/`, `/\\d+/`, `/(foo|bar)/`.\n- `has_req_cu`/`req_cu`/`req_cu2` ← `PCRE2_LASTSET`/`PCRE2_LASTCASELESS` (M:7579-7595); set at C:11215-11240 — only if unanchored **or** `REQ_VARY` (`/^\\d+C/`). Cleared by study if it collides with the derived first CU (S:2025-2029, e.g. `/a*a/`).\n- `startline` ← `PCRE2_STARTLINE` (M:7400), set by `is_startline()` C:11188-11190: all branches start with `^` in multiline, or non-atomic `.*` when not DOTALL.\n- `anchored` = pattern-or-option `PCRE2_ANCHORED` (M:7398); auto-anchoring by `is_anchored()` C:11108-11113 (`^`, `\\A`, `.*` under DOTALL when `PCRE2_OPTIM_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR`).\n- `firstline` = `!anchored && PCRE2_FIRSTLINE` (M:7399).\n- `re->minlength` from `find_minlength()`, only when `!(PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY|PCRE2_HASACCEPT)` and `top_backref <= MAX_CACHE_BACKREF` (S:2053-2079); `-1` (e.g. `\\C` in UTF) leaves it 0.\n\nBumpalong loop:\n\n| Item | Line |\n|---|---|\n| `FRAGMENT_RESTART:` label; `start_partial=match_partial=NULL`, `mb->hitend=FALSE`, memchr caches cleared | M:7603-7611 |\n| `for(;;)` bumpalong loop | M:7614 |\n| whole block gated by `re->optimization_flags & PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE` (i.e. `(*NO_START_OPT)` / `PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE` disables) | M:7625 |\n| FIRSTLINE: temporarily truncate `end_subject` at first newline (UTF-aware scan) | M:7633-7652 |\n| anchored + (first_cu or bitmap): single-position check, else `MATCH_NOMATCH` break | M:7655-7676 |\n| unanchored `has_first_cu`, caseless: 8-bit dual `memchr` with `memchr_found_first_cu`/`_cu2` caches | M:7686-7749 |\n| unanchored caseful: single `memchr` | M:7753-7762 |\n| bail unless partial: `mb->partial==0 && start_match >= mb->end_subject` → NOMATCH | M:7774-7778 |\n| `startline`: scan to just-after `WAS_NEWLINE`, plus CR→LF extra bump for ANY/ANYCRLF | M:7784-7815 |\n| `start_bits` bitmap scan (`c>255 → 255` only for non-8-bit) + same partial bail | M:7819-7836 |\n| restore `end_subject = mb->end_subject` | M:7843 |\n| **both remaining opts disabled when `mb->partial != 0`** | M:7847 |\n| studied minlength: `end_subject-start_match < re->minlength` → NOMATCH break | M:7856-7860 |\n|