CURSELOOP_CHECK` is unset. `F->recurse_last_used = mb->last_used_ptr` snapshot at M:5737. Shape: `/(?1)()/` style mutual recursion, or `/(a(?2))((?1))/`. With the option set the same input instead hits MATCHLIMIT/HEAPLIMIT.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Opcode groups reached by the interpreter (with a reaching pattern)\n\nDispatch: `Fop = *Fecode; switch(Fop)` at M:887-888. Repeat decode tables `rep_min/rep_max/rep_typ` used at M:1372-1400 etc.\n\n**Group / capture control**\n| Ops | Lines | Pattern |\n|---|---|---|\n| OP_CLOSE (pre-ACCEPT capture closing; skipped inside recursion) | M:900-921 | `/(a(*ACCEPT))/` |\n| OP_ASSERT_ACCEPT | M:931-934 | `/(?=a(*ACCEPT))/` |\n| OP_ACCEPT (in-recursion path) / OP_END | M:940-1054 | `/a(*ACCEPT)b/`, `/(a(*ACCEPT))(?1)/` |\n| NOTEMPTY / NOTEMPTY_ATSTART empty-match rejection | M:982-991 | `/a*/` + option |\n| ENDANCHORED at END vs ACCEPT (ACCEPT returns MATCH_NOMATCH directly, no backtrack) | M:998-1013 | `/a(*ACCEPT)/` + `PCRE2_ENDANCHORED` |\n| `\\K` sanity: `Fstart_match < start+start_offset \\|\\| > Feptr` → `PCRE2_ERROR_BAD_BACKSLASH_K` unless `PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK` | M:1018-1029 | `/(?=(a\\K))(?1)/`-style sneaky \\K |\n| final ovector fill / tail UNSET | M:1039-1053 | `/(a)(b)?/` |\n| OP_BRA fast path (skipped when `mb->hasthen \\|\\| Frdepth==0`) | M:5622-5651 | `/(?:a|b)c/` vs `/(?:a(*THEN)|b)c/` |\n| OP_CBRA/OP_SCBRA | M:5661-5665 | `/(a)/`, `/(a?)*/` |\n| **OP_ONCE** / OP_SCRIPT_RUN / OP_SBRA + `GROUPLOOP` | M:5671-5687 | `/(?>a+)b/` (atomic), `/(*sr:...)/`, `/(?:a?)*/` |\n| OP_BRAZERO / OP_BRAMINZERO / OP_SKIPZERO | M:5489-5520 | `/(a)?b/`, `/(a)??b/`, `/(?:(a))*+/` |\n| **Possessive groups** OP_BRAPOSZERO/BRAPOS/SBRAPOS/CBRAPOS/SCBRAPOS + `MATCH_KETRPOS` loop | M:5534-5595 | `/(a|b)++c/`, `/(?:ab)*+/` |\n| Possessive single-char/class quantifiers | OP_POSSTAR M:1334, POSPLUS 1342, POSQUERY 1350, POSUPTO 1310; NOT* 1682-1713; TYPEPOS* 2932-2959; class/XCLASS/ECLASS `OP_CRPOS*` M:2311/2453 | `/a*+/`, `/[a-z]++/`, `/\\d?+/`, `/[^a]*+/` |\n| OP_KET/KETRMIN/KETRMAX/KETRPOS | M:6304-6568 | all groups; empty-loop breaker at M:6543 |\n| OP_ALT | M:6292-6296 | |\n\n**Backreferences**\n- `match_ref()` M:349-478: unset-group branch M:376-384 → `PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF` makes it a zero-length match (M:378-381), else `-1`. Caseless UTF/UCP path M:390-448 (length walked along the *reference*, not the subject; `REFI_FLAG_CASELESS_RESTRICT` M:432, `REFI_FLAG_TURKISH_CASING` / `UCD_FOLD_I_TURKISH` M:419-424, `ucd_caseless_sets` M:428-440). Non-UTF caseless M:452-465. Caseful partial-safe unit-by-unit loop M:472-478; fast `memcmp` when not partial M:485-489.\n- `OP_DNREF/OP_DNREFI` M:5248-5264 (walks the name table for the first *set* group) — `/(?<n>a)|(?<n>b)\\k<n>/`.\n- `OP_REF/OP_REFI` M:5267-5271 (`Fecode[1+IMM2_SIZE]` = caseopts byte for REFI).\n- `REF_REPEAT:` M:5277-5316 (`OP_CR*` decode), zero-length/unset shortcuts M:5325-5337, min loop M:5341-5353, `REPTYPE_MIN` loop M:5355+, possessive at `OP_CRPOSSTAR` etc.\n- Partial subtlety: `rrc>0` (partial from match_ref) sets `Feptr = mb->end_subject` then `CHECK_PARTIAL()` (M:5310-5313, 5344-5348, 5368-5372); one site avoids clobbering Feptr and inlines the hitend test (M:5394-5402).\n- Shapes: `/(a)\\1/`, `/(a)\\1{2,3}/`, `/(?i)(a)\\1/`, `/(a)?\\1b/` + `PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF`, `/(?<x>a)\\k<x>/`.\n\n**Recursion** — `OP_RECURSE` M:5707-5783. `number = 0` for whole-pattern recursion (M:5709). Loop-check M:5719-5734. Branch loop M:5741-5776 with verb containment via `mb->verb_current_recurse` (M:5761-5768). End-of-recursion handling: whole pattern at `OP_KET`/`OP_BRA` case M:6368-6396 (detected by `Fcurrent_recurse==0 && Fecode[1+LINK_SIZE]==OP_END`), numbered groups at M:6488-6509; capture restore via `memcpy` or `recurse_update_offsets()` (M:497-570) when the recurse call is followed by `OP_CREF`. Shapes: `/\\((?:[^()]++|(?R))*\\)/`, `/(a)(?1)/`, `/(?<w>a)(?&w)/`, `/(?1)(?<x>a)/`.\n\n**Assertions**\n- `OP_ASSERT / OP_ASSERTBACK / OP_ASSERT_NA / OP_ASSERTBACK_NA` M:5789-5813 (ACCEPT copies captures+mark from `assert_accept_frame`, M:5794-5805; THEN squashed to NOMATCH M:5806).\n- `OP_ASSERT_NOT / OP_ASSERTBACK_NOT` M:5820-5854 (COMMIT/SKIP/PRUNE ⇒ assertion *succeeds*, M:5838-5842).\n- `OP_ASSERT_SCS` (scan-substring, `(*scs:...)`) M:5867-5975: picks the first set `OP_CREF`/`OP_DNCREF` slot, retargets `Feptr`/`end_subject`/`true_end_subject` to that capture and clears `PCRE2_NOTEOL` (M:5926-5934); restores on every exit (M:5947-5966); ket side M:6461-6474.\n- Ket-side assertion semantics M:6398-6520: `ASSERTBACK_NA`→`ASSERT_NA` restore `Feptr=P->eptr` (M:6404-6414); `ASSERTBACK`→`ASSERT`→`ONCE` discard backtracks and force last branch (M:6420-6440); `ASSERTBACK_NOT`/`ASSERT_NOT` → `RRETURN(MATCH_MATCH)` (M:6446-6452). Conditional-assertion ket M:6341-6350.\n- **Variable-length lookbehind**: `OP_REVERSE` (fixed) M:6190-6229 — uses `mb->check_subject` as the floor in UTF (M:6200) but `mb->start_subject` when not UTF (M:6217); `OP_VREVERSE` M:6233-6289 — move back max then walk forward (`available` capped at 65535, M:6272). End-point verification `branch_start[1+LINK_SIZE]==OP_VREVERSE && Feptr != P->eptr` at M:6343-6345, 6403, 6419, 6445.\n- Shapes: `/(?=ab)a/`, `/(?!ab)a./`, `/(?<=ab)c/`, `/(?<!ab)c/`, `/(?<=a{2,5})b/` (VREVERSE), `/(?*ab)c/`/`(?<*...)` NA forms, `/(*scs:(1)...)/`.\n\n**Conditionals** `OP_COND/OP_SCOND` M:6008-6182\n| Condition op | Line | Pattern |\n|---|---|---|\n| callout inserted before assertion condition | M:6027-6041 | auto-callout |\n| `OP_RREF` (`RREF_ANY` = `(?(R))`, or `(?(R1))`) | M:6048-6055 | `/(a)(?(R)b|c)/`, `/(?(R1)x|y)(?1)/` |\n| `OP_DNRREF` (`(?(R&name))`) | M:6057-6071 | `/(?<n>a)(?(R&n)x|y)/` |\n| `OP_CREF` (`(?(1))`) | M:6073-6076 | `/(a)?(?(1)b|c)/` |\n| `OP_DNCREF` (`(?(<name>))`) | M:6078-6091 | `/(?<n>a)?(?(<n>)b|c)/` |\n| `OP_FALSE`/`OP_FAIL` — **DEFINE** and `(?!)` | M:6093-6095 | `/(?(DEFINE)(?<x>a))(?&x)/` |\n| `OP_TRUE` — `(?(VERSION>=10.0)...)` true arm | M:6097-6098 | `/(?(VERSION>=10)y|n)/` (false → `OP_FALSE`) |\n| assertion condition, `GF_CONDASSERT`, `Lpositive` | M:6104-6167 | `/(?(?=a)ab|cd)/`, `/(?(?<=x)y|z)/` |\n| branch selection `Fecode += condition? OP_lengths : Llength` | M:6171 | |\n| `OP_SCOND` descends a level (empty-repeat guard) | M:6178-6182 | `/(?(1)a?)*/` |\n\n**`\\K`** = `OP_SET_SOM` (`I:1645`), M:6689-6692: `Fstart_match = Feptr`. Compile sets `PCRE2_HASBSK` (C:8381-8382) and rejects `\\K` inside lookarounds with ERR7 (C:8338, C:4576). Related: `OP_SOM` = `\\G` (M:6680-6683, `Feptr != start_subject + start_offset`), `OP_SOD` = `\\A` (M:6576-6579). Interaction with `Fstart_match` validity is the `BAD_BACKSLASH_K` check at M:1018-1029.\n\n**Verbs** M:6777-6889\n| Op | Line | Pattern |\n|---|---|---|\n| `OP_MARK` (sets `Fmark`/`nomatch_mark`, matches SKIP:NAME via `PRIV(strcmp)`) | M:6777-6795 | `/a(*MARK:X)b/`, `/a(*MARK:X)b|(*SKIP:X)c/` |\n| `OP_FAIL` | M:6796-6797 | `/(*FAIL)/`, `/(?!)/` |\n| `OP_COMMIT` / `OP_COMMIT_ARG` | M:6803-6814 | `/a(*COMMIT)b/`, `/(*COMMIT:X)/` |\n| `OP_PRUNE` / `OP_PRUNE_ARG` | M:6816-6827 | `/a(*PRUNE)b/` |\n| `OP_SKIP` (passes back `verb_skip_ptr = Feptr`) | M:6829-6835 | `/a(*SKIP)b/` |\n| `OP_SKIP_ARG` (`skip_arg_count`/`ignore_skip_arg` re-run protocol) | M:6844-6864 | `/A(*SKIP:A)B|AC/` on `\"AC\"` — exercises M:7999-8003 |\n| `OP_THEN` / `OP_THEN_ARG` (`verb_ecode_ptr`) | M:6866-6889 | `/a(*THEN)b|ac/` |\n| verb containment inside groups/atomic/possessive/recursion | M:5578-5585, 5691-5697, 5761-5768 | `/(a(*THEN)b|c)/` |\n| `MATCH_*` codes and `MATCH_BACKTRACK_MIN/MAX` range | M:85-101 | |\n\n**Script runs**: `OP_SCRIPT_RUN` enters via `GROUPLOOP` (M:5672) and is validated at the ket by `PRIV(script_run)(P->eptr, Feptr, utf)` (M:6476-6478). Pattern `/(*script_run:\\w+)/` a.k.a. `(*sr:...)`.\n\n**`\\X`**: `OP_EXTUNI` M:2889-2903 (`PRIV(extuni)`), quantified via `OP_EXTUNI_EXTRA`-less path in `REPEATTYPE` (see `Lctype==OP_EXTUNI` handling at M:3252 / M:4077 / M:4666 region). Pattern `/\\X+/`.\n\n**Classes**: `OP_CLASS`/`OP_NCLASS` M:2051-2293 (`/[abc]/`, `/[^abc]/`); `OP_XCLASS` M:2294-2435 (`/[\\p{L}]/`, `/[^\\x{100}]/`); `OP_ECLASS` M:2436-2573 (extended/set-operation class, `/[\\p{L}&&\\p{Latin}]/`). Both use `OP_CR*` quantifier decode at M:2299-2330 / 2441-2470.\n\n**Callouts**: `do_callout()` M:268-334 (`cb->version=2`; ovector aliasing trick `Fovector-2` M:290, save/restore slots 0/1 M:322-329; numeric vs string branch M:308-321). Dispatch `OP_CALLOUT`/`OP_CALLOUT_STR` M:5989-5996 (`rrc>0` → NOMATCH, `rrc<0` → propagate). Conditional-group callout M:6027-6041. Patterns `/a(?C1)b/`, `/a(?C\"str\")b/`, plus `PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT`.\n\n**Anchors / EOD family**\n| Op | Line | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `OP_CIRC` (`^`) | M:6570-6574 | `Feptr != start_subject \\|\\| PCRE2_NOTBOL` |\n| `OP_SOD` (`\\A`) | M:6576-6579 | ignores NOTBOL |\n| `OP_DOLL` (`$`) | M:6584-6589 | `PCRE2_NOTEOL` → fail; `PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY` → jump to `OP_EOD` semantics |\n| `OP_EOD` (`\\z`) | M:6591-6600 | compares against **`true_end_subject`** |\n| `OP_EODN` (`\\Z`) / `ASSERT_NL_OR_EOS` | M:6602-6627 | allows a single trailing newline of `mb->nllen` |\n| `OP_CIRCM` (multiline `^`) | M:6637-6649 | `PCRE2_ALT_CIRCUMFLEX` allows match after a final newline |\n| `OP_DOLLM` (multiline `$`) | M:6651-6674 | NOTEOL only affects the at-end case (M:6669) |\n| `OP_SOM` (`\\G`) / `OP_SET_SOM` (`\\K`) | M:6680-6692 | |\n\n**`.` / `\\C`**: `OP_ANY` M:1061-1072 (newline check + CRLF partial special-case), `OP_ALLANY` M:1076-1091, `OP_ANYBYTE` M:1095-1106 (`\\C`).\n\n**`\\R`**: there is no separate `OP_BSR`; `\\R` compiles to `OP_ANYNL`, handled M:2646-2679 — CR+optional LF atomically (M:2657-2663), and `CHAR_VT/FF/NEL/0x2028/0x2029` rejected when `mb->bsr_convention == PCRE2_BSR_ANYCRLF` (M:2674-2675). Quantified `\\R` goes through the `OP_TYPE*` path with `Lctype == OP_ANYNL` (M:3252-3282, 4077-4112, 4666-4744, 4977-4995 — each with its own CRLF partial handling).\n\n**`\\b`/`\\B`**: `OP_NOT_WORD_BOUNDARY`/`OP_WORD_BOUNDARY`/`OP_NOT_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY`/`OP_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY` M:6702-6767. Previous char floor is `mb->check_subject` (M:6706) — relevant for invalid-UTF fragments. UCP variants use `ucp_L/ucp_N/ucp_Mn/ucp_Pc` (M:6721-6726, 6752-6757); non-UCP uses `CHMAX_255 && ctype_word` (M:6729, 6760). Final polarity test M:6763-6766. UCP variants are chosen at compile time when `PCRE2_UCP && !PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSW` (C:8371-8374). `\\A` bumps `max_lookbehind` to ≥1 (C:8377-8378).\n\n**Other type ops**: `\\d\\D\\s\\S\\w\\W` M:2574-2645; `\\h\\H\\v\\V` M:2681-2747; `\\p{..}`/`\\P{..}` `OP_PROP`/`OP_NOTPROP` M:2748-2888; quantified type ops M:2919-2966 with the shared `REPEATTYPE` engine at M:2968+.\n\n---\n\n# 5. Partial matching\n\n**pcre2_match.c**\n- Option→level: M:7105-7107 (`mb->partial` ∈ {0,1,2}); partial+ENDANCHORED rejected M:7111-7113.\n- `CHECK_PARTIAL()` M:614-621, `SCHECK_PARTIAL()` M:623-632. Core predicate: `mb->partial != 0 && (Feptr > mb->start_used_ptr || mb->allowemptypartial)` → `mb->hitend = TRUE`; and `mb->partial > 1` (**HARD**) → immediate `return PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` (bypasses RRETURN, so no backtracking).\n- `mb->allowemptypartial = (re->max_lookbehind>0) || (re->flags & PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY)` M:7424-7425 — this is what makes `/(?<=abc)def/` partially match `\"abc\"` and `/(?=a)/`-ish empty-capable patterns report partial at offset 0.\n- `match_ref` returns `+1` for \"ran out of subject\" (M:406, M:456, M:474) — only in the caseless loops and the *partial* caseful loop; the non-partial caseful path uses `memcmp` (M:485-489). Callers M:5310-5313, 5344-5348, 5368-5372, 5394-5402.\n- CRLF-aware \"one more code unit could complete the newline\" special cases (all guarded by `nltype==NLTYPE_FIXED && nllen==2 && *Feptr==nl[0]`): `OP_ANY` M:1063-1071; type-repeat sites M:3272-3280, 3528-3536, 4103-4111, 4234-4242, 4733-4741, 4985-4993; `OP_EODN`/`ASSERT_NL_OR_EOS` M:6608-6616; `OP_DOLLM` M:6656-6664.\n- End-of-subject assertions always set hitend under partial, unconditionally (no `start_used_ptr` test): `OP_EOD` M:6593-6597, `OP_EODN` M:6622-6626. So `/abc\\z/` + PARTIAL_HARD on `\"abc\"` returns PARTIAL rather than MATCH.\n- `PCRE2_NOTEOL` interaction: `OP_DOLL` fails outright before any hitend (M:6585), `OP_DOLLM` fails the at-end branch before `SCHECK_PARTIAL()` (M:6669-6671). So `/a$/` with NOTEOL+PARTIAL_SOFT on `\"a\"` → NOMATCH, not PARTIAL.\n- Start-optimizations that are **skipped** under partial: the `start_match >= mb->end_subject` early breaks are conditional (M:7774, M:7833) and the whole minlength+req_cu block is gated by `mb->partial == 0` (M:7847). Differential-testing hook: `/(?<=abc)def/` on `\"abc\"` with/without PARTIAL_SOFT.\n- Result plumbing: `start_partial`/`match_partial` captured at M:7984-7988; final classification M:8215-8243. SOFT partial reaches here with `rc == MATCH_NOMATCH` but `match_partial != NULL`; HARD arrives already as `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`. Partial ovector = `[match_partial-subject, end_subject-subject]`, `leftchar = start_partial`, `rightchar = end_subject` (M:8226-8232). Invalid-UTF fragments suppress partial until the true end (M:8110-8131, `match_partial = NULL` at M:8131).\n- Subject shapes: `/abcd/` on `\"abc\"` → PARTIAL (both modes). `/abcd|abcx/` on `\"abc\"` → PARTIAL. `/ab|abcd/` on `\"abc\"` → SOFT: MATCH \"ab\"; HARD: PARTIAL. `/abc/` on `\"xyz\"` → NOMATCH. `/a+/` on `\"aaa\"` → SOFT MATCH \"aaa\"; HARD PARTIAL.\n\n**pcre2_dfa_match.c**\n- Public option mask includes both partial bits D:85-86; partial+ENDANCHORED → BADOPTION D:3413-3415.\n- `could_continue` set whenever `clen==0 && poptable[codevalue]!=0` (D:800-801) — the \"this op wanted a character\" signal; `reset_could_continue` carries it across negative (delayed) states D:764-773, and is used by multi-char items D:2129-2130 (`\\X`), D:2308-2309, D:2341-2342.\n- HARD-only immediate returns: `OP_EOD` D:963-964, `OP_EODN` D:1015-1016.\n- `OP_DOLL` D:1024-1045 and `OP_DOLLM` D:1051-1071: `clen==0 && HARD` → could_continue; the CRLF-lookahead case splits HARD (delayed state via `ADD_NEW_DATA(-(state_offset+1),0,1)`) vs SOFT (`partial_newline = TRUE`).\n- `partial_newline` set from `OP_ANY` D:991-996 and the `OP_TYPE*`-with-`OP_ANY` sites D:1290-1295, 1321-1326, 1351-1356, 1379-1384, 1408-1413.\n- Final decision, when `new_count <= 0` (D:3274-3295): PARTIAL iff `could_continue` **and** (HARD, or SOFT-with-no-match-yet) **and** (`partial_newline` or (`ptr >= end_subject` and (`ptr > mb->start_used_ptr` or `mb->allowemptypartial`))). `mb->allowemptypartial` D:3531-3532.\n- Start-optimization partial gates D:3855-3856, 3912-3913, 3924 (mirror of M:7774/7833/7847).\n- Reporting: `rc == PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL && oveccount > 0` → `ovector[0]=start_match`, `[1]=end_subject` (D:4046-4050), plus leftchar/rightchar/startchar D:4052-4059.\n- ENDANCHORED post-check can turn a match into NOMATCH after the scan loop (D:3302-3306).\n\n---\n\n# 6. `pcre2_dfa_match()` specifics\n\n**Entry validation** (D:3339-3517): `null_str` D:3330/3391; NULL checks D:3395-3398; `~PUBLIC_DFA_MATCH_OPTIONS` → BADOPTION D:3399-3400 (mask D:83-87 — note DFA accepts `DFA_SHORTEST`/`DFA_RESTART`, has no `DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK`); ZERO_TERMINATED D:3403-3406; **`wscount < 20` → `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE`** D:3407; `start_offset > length` → BADOFFSET D:3408; partial+ENDANCHORED D:3413-3415; **`PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` in the pattern → `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UINVALID_UTF`** D:3419-3420; BADMAGIC D:3425-3426; BADMODE D:3430-3431; `(*NOTEMPTY*)` flag fold D:3444-3448.\n\n**`PCRE2_DFA_RESTART`**\n- Sanity check D:3454-3459: requires `(workspace[0] & -2) == 0` (bit 0 only) and `1 <= workspace[1] <= (wscount-2)/INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK`; otherwise `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_BADRESTART`.\n- `anchored` is forced when restarting: D:3467-3468 (`options & (PCRE2_ANCHORED|PCRE2_DFA_RESTART)`), so no bumpalong.\n- Start-optimizations skipped when restarting: D:3703-3704.\n- State reload in `internal_dfa_match` D:668-675: at `rlevel==1`, `new_count = workspace[1]`, and if `!workspace[0]` copy `active_states` → `new_states`. `workspace[0]` is the current-vector bit maintained at D:694 and toggled each character at D:719-720; `workspace[1] = active_count` D:720.\n\n**Workspace sizing / WSSIZE**: `wscount -= 2; wscount = (wscount - wscount % (INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK*2)) / (2*INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK)` D:570-572; vectors laid out at D:580-581. `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE` returned from all four state-adding macros `ADD_ACTIVE`/`ADD_ACTIVE_DATA`/`ADD_NEW`/`ADD_NEW_DATA` (D:490-525) when `active_count++`/`new_count++ >= wscount`. Shape: a pattern with many simultaneous alternatives (`/(a|b|c|...){20}/`) with a 20-int workspace.\n\n**Recursion workspace (RWS)**: `RWS_BASE_SIZE` stack block D:3384-3388, `RWS_RSIZE`/`RWS_OVEC_RSIZE` D:326-327, anchor struct D:330+. `more_workspace()` D:421-455 — doubles, clamps by `mb->heap_limit - mb->heap_used`, returns `PCRE2_ERROR_HEAPLIMIT` D:443 or `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` D:445. Blocks freed at `EXIT:` D:4113-4118.\n\n**Limits**: `mb->match_call_count++ >= mb->match_limit → PCRE2_ERROR_MATCHLIMIT` and `rlevel++ > mb->match_limit_depth → PCRE2_ERROR_DEPTHLIMIT` at D:566-567 — once per `internal_dfa_match` **call**, not per character, so MATCHLIMIT in DFA counts nested calls (assertions/recursion/ONCE/BRAPOS), not states. Limit selection D:3496-3524 (context values, then `min` with `re->limit_*`; note the DFA takes context values first and clamps, D:3518-3524). `mb->match_call_count = 0` only once (D:3536), i.e. it is **global across bumpalong**, unlike the interpreter.\n\n**Internal recursion via `internal_dfa_match`** — five recursion sites:\n| Purpose | Line | Unsupported-item note |\n|---|---|---|\n| `OP_ASSERT/ASSERT_NOT/ASSERTBACK/ASSERTBACK_NOT` | D:2784-2825 | positive/negative decided by `(rc>=0) == (codevalue==OP_ASSERT||OP_ASSERTBACK)` D:2822 |\n| assertion conditions in `OP_COND/OP_SCOND` | D:2884-2925 | |\n| `OP_RECURSE` | D:2932-3028 | `code[1+LINK_SIZE]==OP_CREF` (recursion with argument list) → `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UITEM` D:2943; loop check → `PCRE2_ERROR_RECURSELOOP` D:2960-2966; `rc == 0` (ran out of internal offsets) → **`PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_RECURSE`** D:2995 |\n| `OP_BRAPOS/SBRAPOS/CBRAPOS/SCBRAPOS/BRAPOSZERO` | D:3030-3130 | |\n| `OP_ONCE` | D:3136-3240 | |\n\n**Unsupported-item errors**\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UITEM`: D:825 (`\\C` = `OP_ANYBYTE` as a quantified type), D:2943 (recursion with args), D:3259 `default:` — catches everything with no DFA case: `OP_REF/OP_REFI/OP_DNREF/OP_DNREFI` (`/(a)\\1/`), all verbs `OP_MARK/PRUNE/SKIP/THEN/COMMIT/ACCEPT` and `_ARG` forms (`/a(*SKIP)b/`) — note `OP_FAIL` **is** supported (D:2781), `OP_SET_SOM` (`\\K`), `OP_SOM`? (no — `OP_SOM` supported D:970-972), `OP_SCRIPT_RUN` (coptable/poptable entries are 0 at D:179/D:259 but there is no case ⇒ UITEM), `OP_ASSERT_NA`/`OP_ASSERTBACK_NA`, `OP_ASSERT_SCS`, `OP_VREVERSE` (variable-length lookbehind), `OP_CLOSE`, `OP_ANYBYTE` standalone.\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UCOND`: D:2857 (`OP_CREF`, `OP_DNCREF`, `OP_DNRREF` conditions: `/(a)(?(1)b|c)/`, `/(?<n>a)(?(<n>)b)/`, `/(?(R&n)..)/`), D:2877 (`OP_RREF` with a specific group number — only `RREF_ANY` i.e. `(?(R))` is supported).\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UFUNC`: **not** produced by pcre2_dfa_match.c at all; it is returned by `pcre2_substring.c:75, 163, 270` and `pcre2_substitute.c:850` when `match_data->matchedby == PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER` (set at D:3688).\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UINVALID_UTF`: D:3420 only.\n\n**`PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST`**: D:891 — on reaching the final ket, `return match_count` immediately instead of continuing to find longer matches.\n\n**Multiple matches in the ovector** (D:857-892, the `code == end_code` branch): guarded by the NOTEMPTY/NOTEMPTY_ATSTART test D:871-874; `match_count` init `(offsetcount >= 2)? 1 : 0` D:875; incremented and forced to 0 on overflow D:876-877 (0 = \"offsets overflowed; longest are present\"); previous pairs shifted up by `memmove(offsets+2, offsets, count*sizeof)` D:879-880; new pair written to `offsets[0]/[1]` D:881-885. Because states are scanned in longest-first discovery order and each new final state is *prepended*, the ovector ends up **longest match first**. `offsetcount &= -2` (round down to pairs) at D:568. `match_count` starts as `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH` D:578.\n\n**Other DFA notes**: `ADD_NEW_DATA` negative-offset \"skip N chars then enter state\" mechanism D:764-778; duplicate-state suppression D:781-787 (O(i) scan); `coptable`/`poptable` inline-argument tables and the `OP_PROP_EXTRA`/`OP_ANYNL_EXTRA`/`OP_EXTUNI_EXTRA`/`OP_HSPACE_EXTRA`/`OP_VSPACE_EXTRA` opcode remapping D:815-834 (constants D:98-101); backward-assertion `max_back`/`gone_back` setup D:588-651 (uses `OP_REVERSE` presence per branch, D:644-650); `do_callout_dfa` D:359-397; bumpalong loop D:3690-4110; `NOMATCH_EXIT`/`EXIT` D:4101-4120.\n\n---\n\n# 7. Newline handling at match time\n\n`mb->nltype`/`nllen`/`nl[]` set from `re->newline_convention` — **six conventions**, identical switch in both files:\n\n| Convention | pcre2_match.c | pcre2_dfa_match.c | Effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `PCRE2_NEWLINE_CR` | M:7446-7449 | D:3543-3546 | FIXED, nllen 1, `\\r` |\n| `PCRE2_NEWLINE_LF` | M:7451-7454 | D:3548-3551 | FIXED, nllen 1, `\\n` |\n| `PCRE2_NEWLINE_NUL` | M:7456-7459 | D:3553-3556 | FIXED, nllen 1, `\\0` |\n| `PCRE2_NEWLINE_CRLF` | M:7461-7465 | D:3558-3562 | FIXED, nllen **2**, `\\r\\n` |\n| `PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY` | M:7467-7469 | D:3564-3566 | `NLTYPE_ANY` |\n| `PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANYCRLF` | M:7471-7473 | D:3568-3570 | `NLTYPE_ANYCRLF` |\n| default | M:7476-7479 (`PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL`) | D:3573-3578 | |\n\n`NLTYPE_*` constants `I:467-469`; `IS_NEWLINE` `I:473-486`, `WAS_NEWLINE` `I:487-500` (both dispatch on `nltype != NLTYPE_FIXED` and use `PRIV(is_newline)`/`was_newline`). `NLBLOCK` = `mb` (M:63-65, same in D:).\n\n`mb->bsr_convention = re->bsr_convention` M:7443, D:3540. The only consumers are `OP_ANYNL` (M:2674-2675, D:1315-1316) and the quantified-`\\R` sites, testing `== PCRE2_BSR_ANYCRLF` to reject VT/FF/NEL/U+2028/U+2029. `(*BSR_UNICODE)`/`(*BSR_ANYCRLF)` are the pattern shapes.\n\n**CRLF treated atomically**\n1. Bumpalong skip: M:8069-8078 / D:4093-4104 — after a failed attempt, if the previous unit was CR, we are now at LF, `(re->flags & PCRE2_HASCRORLF) == 0` (pattern has no literal `\\r`/`\\n`; set at C:8475), and `nltype==ANY || nltype==ANYCRLF || nllen==2`, advance one extra unit. Note M:8069 additionally requires `start_match > subject + start_offset` (a failed `*SKIP` can return to the same position).\n2. `startline` scan: M:7808-7813 / D:3877-3882 — after `WAS_NEWLINE` lands past a CR, if ANY/ANYCRLF and next is LF, bump once more.\n3. `OP_ANYNL` consumes CR+LF as one unit (M:2657-2663; D:1320-1341).\n4. `\\X` (`OP_EXTUNI`) via `PRIV(extuni)` in pcre2_extuni.c.\n5. `OP_EODN`/`\\Z` uses `true_end_subject - mb->nllen` so a CRLF terminator is skipped whole (M:6605-6606); DFA `OP_EODN` uses `end_subject - mb->nllen` (D:1010).\n6. Partial matching treats a trailing CR as \"could be CRLF\" at every `nllen==2` site listed in §5.\n\nFIRSTLINE truncation walks with `IS_NEWLINE` (M:7633-7652 / D:3708-3727) and the failure stop is `firstline && IS_NEWLINE(start_match)` (M:8051 / D:4082).\n\n---\n\n# 8. `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` at match time (pcre2_match.c only)\n\n`allow_invalid = (re->overall_options & PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF) != 0` — M:7019 (decl), M:7099.\n\nDivergent paths:\n1. **Forces a UTF check even with `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK`**: M:7271-7274 (`(options & PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK) == 0 || allow_invalid`). JIT path deliberately excludes it (M:7152, `&& !allow_invalid`).\n2. **Bad leading code unit is skipped rather than an error**: M:7283-7291 sets `skipped_bad_start = TRUE` and advances past continuation units; the `!allow_invalid` alternative returns `BADUTFOFFSET`/`UTF8_ERR20` (M:7293-7300).\n3. **`mb->check_subject` becomes the lookbehind floor** = `start_match` (M:7307), then rewound by `re->max_lookbehind` characters **unless** we skipped a bad start (M:7313-7331).\n4. **Fragment discovery loop** M:7341-7385: `PRIV(valid_utf)` on `[check_subject, end)`; on error, `match_data->startchar` made absolute (M:7357); `if (!allow_invalid || rc > 0) return rc` (M:7358) — note `rc > 0` (a *truncated-at-end* UTF error) is fatal even with allow_invalid; otherwise `end_subject = subject + startchar` (M:7359). If the bad unit lies *before* `start_match` (i.e. inside the lookbehind window), advance `check_subject` past it, skip continuation units, restore `end_subject = true_end_subject`, and retry (M:7366-7374). Else set `fragment_options = PCRE2_NOTEOL` (M:7380) and match the fragment.\n5. **`mb->true_end_subject`** is kept as the real end (M:7421) while `mb->end_subject` is the fragment end — so `\\z`/`\\Z` (`OP_EOD` M:6592, `OP_EODN` M:6605-6606) still reference the true end and cannot match at a fragment boundary, whereas `$`/`$m`/`SCHECK_PARTIAL`/all character ops use `mb->end_subject`.\n6. **`mb->moptions = options | fragment_options`** M:7963-7967 — the injected `PCRE2_NOTBOL`/`PCRE2_NOTEOL` are what stop `^`/`$` from matching at synthetic fragment edges (`OP_CIRC` M:6571, `OP_CIRCM` M:6638, `OP_DOLL` M:6585, `OP_DOLLM` M:6669).\n7. **Fragment iteration** `ENDLOOP` M:8102-8163: entered only when `utf && end_subject != true_end_subject && (rc == MATCH_NOMATCH || rc == PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL)`. Advances past the bad unit and continuation units (M:8118-8123); exhaustion → `rc = MATCH_NOMATCH; match_partial = NULL` (M:8128-8133) — **a partial match is only reported at the true end of the subject**; a clean remainder → `end_subject = true_end_subject`, `fragment_options = PCRE2_NOTBOL`, `goto FRAGMENT_RESTART` (M:8144-8148); another error → `fragment_options = PCRE2_NOTBOL|PCRE2_NOTEOL` and restart if the fragment is non-empty (M:8152-8160).\n8. **`FRAGMENT_RESTART:`** M:7601-7603 (inside `#ifdef SUPPORT_UNICODE`) resets `start_partial`/`match_partial`/`hitend`/memchr caches per fragment.\n9. **Lookbehind/`\\b` floors** honour `check_subject` rather than `start_subject`: `OP_REVERSE` UTF path M:6200 (`Feptr <= mb->check_subject` fails) — note the non-UTF branch M:6217 uses `start_subject`; word boundary \"previous character\" M:6706.\n\nDFA has none of this: `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` is rejected outright at D:3419-3420 with `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UINVALID_UTF`.\n\nUseful differential inputs: pattern `/def/` with `PCRE2_UTF|PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` on `\"abc\\x80def\"`; `/(?<=abc)def/` on `\"\\x80abcdef\"` at `start_offset=1`; `/^x/` and `/x$/` on `\"\\xffx\\xff\"` (fragment NOTBOL/NOTEOL); `/x\\z/` on `\"x\\xff\"`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":922,"cache_read_input_tokens":136248,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":922,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UrZfWraAS46KWhBiSfuc71","session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503","uuid":"dd01bb62-8c64-4b98-bd56-22503c6ba9f3","timestamp":"2026-09-08T18:32:04.516Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map match/dfa runtime branch surface"}
