ytes ≥ 0x80 are **sign-extended negative** on platforms with signed char before assignment to `PCRE2_UCHAR c2`; use `str2` bytes >0x7f as a differential shape.\n- `strncmp`/`strncmp_c8` (`:122`/`:151`): (a) `len == 0` -> 0 without any deref; (b) all `len` equal -> 0; (c) first difference at k<len, either sign; (d) embedded NUL is *not* a stopper — it is compared like any unit; (e) difference at exactly `len-1`; (f) difference at index ≥ len (ignored -> 0).\n- `strlen` (`:174`): (a) empty string -> 0; (b) length n>0; (c) 8-bit: units 0x80-0xff count as 1 each (no UTF decoding).\n- `strcpy_c8` (`:194-196`): (a) empty source -> writes single NUL, returns 0; (b) n>0 -> returns n and NUL-terminates at `str1[n]`; (c) source bytes >0x7f: `*t++ = *str2++` widens a possibly-signed char (8-bit: truncates back to same byte).\n\n# 2. pcre2_ord2utf.c — `_pcre2_ord2utf`\n\n`unsigned int PRIV(ord2utf)(uint32_t cvalue, PCRE2_UCHAR *buffer)` — def `pcre2_ord2utf.c:77-95` (8-bit arm `:82-94`); decl `pcre2_internal.h:2337`.\n\nLogic: `for (i=0; i<PRIV(utf8_table1_size); i++) if ((int)cvalue <= PRIV(utf8_table1)[i]) break;` (`:85-86`), then continuation bytes `:88-92`, lead byte from `PRIV(utf8_table2)[i]` (`:93`), returns `i+1` (`:94`).\n\n`utf8_table1 = {0x7f,0x7ff,0xffff,0x1fffff,0x3ffffff,0x7fffffff}` (`pcre2_tables.c:114-115`).\n\n| output len | cvalue range | boundary pairs to test |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 0x0 – 0x7f | 0x0, 0x7f / 0x80 |\n| 2 | 0x80 – 0x7ff | 0x80, 0x7ff / 0x800 |\n| 3 | 0x800 – 0xffff | 0x800, 0xffff / 0x10000 |\n| 4 | 0x10000 – 0x1fffff | 0x10000, 0x10ffff, 0x1fffff / 0x200000 |\n| 5 | 0x200000 – 0x3ffffff | 0x200000, 0x3ffffff / 0x4000000 |\n| 6 | 0x4000000 – 0x7fffffff | 0x4000000, 0x7fffffff |\n\nExtra shape (signedness quirk at `:86`, worth a differential test): `cvalue >= 0x80000000` casts to a **negative** `int`, so the loop breaks at `i=0` and the function returns 1, emitting `(PCRE2_UCHAR)cvalue` masked to 8 bits. Test 0x80000000, 0xffffffff. Also test s