ALSE |\n| ANY | LF, VT 0x0B, FF 0x0C | `:108-112` | TRUE, 1 |\n| ANY | CR + LF | `:114-116` | TRUE, 2 |\n| ANY | CR alone / CR at end | `:115` | TRUE, 1 |\n| ANY | NEL 0x85 | `:120-122` | TRUE, `utf? 2 : 1` — **two distinct shapes**: non-utf byte `0x85`; utf `\"\\xC2\\x85\"` |\n| ANY | LS U+2028 (`\"\\xE2\\x80\\xA8\"`), PS U+2029 (`\"\\xE2\\x80\\xA9\"`) | `:124-127` | TRUE, **3**; reachable **only when utf=TRUE** (non-utf 8-bit `c=*ptr` ≤ 0xff) |\n| ANY | other | `:138-139` | FALSE |\n\n`_pcre2_was_newline` (`ptr--` at `:169`; utf does `BACKCHAR` then `GETCHAR` `:174-175`):\n\n| type | char at ptr-1 | line | result / nllen |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ANYCRLF | LF, `ptr>startptr && ptr[-1]==CR` | `:185-187` | TRUE, **2** |\n| ANYCRLF | LF, prev != CR **or** `ptr==startptr` | `:186` | TRUE, **1** |\n| ANYCRLF | CR | `:189-191` | TRUE, 1 |\n| ANYCRLF | else | `:193-194` | FALSE |\n| ANY | LF preceded by CR / not | `:201-203` | TRUE, 2 / 1 |\n| ANY | VT, FF, CR | `:208-212` | TRUE, 1 |\n| ANY | NEL 0x85 | `:216-218` | TRUE, `utf? 2 : 1` |\n| ANY | U+2028 / U+2029 | `:220-223` | TRUE, 3 (utf only) |\n| ANY | else | `:234-235` | FALSE |\n\nNote the asymmetry to exploit: `is_newline` looks *forward* for the CRLF pair, `was_newline` looks *backward*; the boundary guards differ (`ptr < endptr - 1` vs `ptr > startptr`).\n\n# 5. pcre2_extuni.c — `_pcre2_extuni`\n\n`PCRE2_SPTR PRIV(extuni)(uint32_t c, PCRE2_SPTR eptr, PCRE2_SPTR start_subject, PCRE2_SPTR end_subject, BOOL utf, int *xcount)` — def `:92-94`; decl `pcre2_internal.h:2327`. Table: `PRIV(ucp_gbtable)` (`pcre2_tables.c:203-223`); bit means \"break NOT permitted\".\n\nBranches / shapes (`c` is the already-consumed first char, `eptr` points at the second):\n1. `eptr >= end_subject` at entry -> loop never runs, returns `eptr` (`:99`, `:154`). Shape: single-char subject.\n2. `utf` FALSE -> `c = *eptr`, `len=1`; TRUE -> `GETCHARLEN(c,eptr,len)` (`:103`). Multi-unit char changes the returned pointer advance.\n3. Table says break: `(ucp_gbtable[lgb] & (1u<<rgb)) == 0` -> break (`:105`). Shape: `\"ab\"` (Other,Other).\n4. Table says join, plain: `\"a\" + U+0301` (Other,Extend) — ESZ = Extend|SpacingMark|ZWJ (`pcre2_tables.c:201`).\n5. CR+LF joins: `\"\\r\\n\"` (`gbtable[0] = 1<<gbLF`).\n6. CR + non-LF, and Control + anything -> break (`gbtable[1]=gbtable[2]=0`).\n7. **ZWJ + Extended_Pictographic with no preceding EP** -> break at `:110-111`. Shape: `\"a\" ZWJ EMOJI` (i.e. `a\\u200D\\u26A1`): `a`+ZWJ joins (ESZ), lgb becomes ZWJ, then ZWJ+EP passes the table test but `was_ep_ZWJ` is FALSE -> break.\n8. **EP + ZWJ + EP** -> joins; `was_ep_ZWJ` set at `:143`. Shape `\\U0001F468\\u200D\\U0001F469`.\n9. **EP + Extend(s) + ZWJ + EP** -> `:148` keeps `lgb` at Extended_Pictographic across `Extend`, so `was_ep_ZWJ` can still become TRUE. Shape `\\U0001F468\\uFE0F\\u200D\\U0001F469`; test with 0, 1, and ≥2 intervening Extends.\n10. **Regional indicators**: `lgb==rgb==gbRegional_Indicator` -> back-scan loop `:116-138`. Even preceding-RI count -> join; **odd -> break at `:137`**. Shapes: `RI RI` (ricount 0, join), `RI RI RI` (third one sees ricount 1 -> break), `RI RI RI RI`. Also `\"a\" RI RI RI` to make the back-scan terminate on a non-RI at `:134`, and `bptr > start_subject` exhaustion at `:124` (RI run starting exactly at subject start). `utf` affects `BACKCHAR` at `:120` and `:129`.\n11. **Prepend**: `gbtable[4]` joins almost everything (`pcre2_tables.c:208-211`) — shape `U+0600` + `\"a\"`.\n12. **SpacingMark**: `\"a\" + U+0903` joins via ESZ.\n13. **Hangul**: L+L / L+V / L+LV / L+LVT (`gbtable[6]`), V+V / V+T (`[7]`), T+T (`[8]`), LV+V/LV+T (`[9]`), LVT+T (`[10]`), plus a *breaking* pair such as V+L.\n14. `xcount == NULL` vs non-NULL (`:151`) — count of additional characters.\n15. Loop terminating on `eptr == end_subject` rather than a break (`:99`).\n\n# 6. pcre2_script_run.c — `_pcre2_script_run`\n\n`BOOL PRIV(script_run)(PCRE2_SPTR ptr, PCRE2_SPTR endptr, BOOL utf)` — def `:83-84`; decl `pcre2_internal.h:2338`. States enum `:72-78`; `UCD_MAPSIZE`/`FULL_MAPSIZE` `:80-81`.\n\nBranch shapes:\n1. `ptr >= endptr` -> TRUE (`:99`). Empty range.\n2. Exactly one character -> TRUE (`:101`), even if script is Unknown.\n3. `script == ucp_Unknown` at position ≥2 -> FALSE (`:132`). Shape: `\"a\" + U+0378`.\n4. Common/Inherited **without** script extensions -> whole script check skipped, only digit check applies (`:138`). Shape: `\"a\" + \"!\"` (Po/Common), `\"a\" + U+0301` (Inherited).\n5. Character **with** scriptx even though script is Common/Inherited -> takes the map path (`:138` first disjunct); `MAPSET` skipped for Common/Inherited (`:150`).\n6. `SCRIPT_UNSET` sub-branches (`:159-183`): Han -> HANPENDING (`:163`); Hiragana or Katakana -> HANHIRAKATA (`:168`); Bopomofo -> HANBOPOMOFO (`:172`); Hangul -> HANHANGUL (`:176`); default -> copy map, SCRIPT_MAP (`:180-181`).\n7. `SCRIPT_HANPENDING` (`:203-223`): another Han -> no state change (`:204`); `chspecial==0` -> **FALSE** (`:213`, e.g. Han + Latin); `==FOUND_BOPOMOFO` -> HANBOPOMOFO (`:215-216`); `==(FOUND_HIRAGANA|FOUND_KATAKANA)` -> HANHIRAKATA (`:217-218`); any other combination (e.g. a char whose scriptx has Bopomofo+Hangul+Han+Hiragana+Katakana) -> stay pending (`:220-222`). Flags `:198-201`.\n8. `SCRIPT_HANHIRAKATA` -> FALSE unless Han|Hiragana|Katakana bit (`:229-230`).\n9. `SCRIPT_HANBOPOMOFO` -> FALSE unless Han|Bopomofo (`:234`).\n10. `SCRIPT_HANHANGUL` -> FALSE unless Han|Hangul (`:238`).\n11. `SCRIPT_MAP` (`:244-288`): intersection loop `:247-254`; empty intersection -> FALSE (`:256`); then the same 5-way transition on `script` (`:261-286`), the `default` narrowing `require_map &= map` at `:284`.\n12. Digit consistency (`:302-327`): only when `ucd->chartype == ucp_Nd`. Fast path `c <= ucd_digit_sets[1]` (=0x39) -> `digitset=1` (`:306`); otherwise binary chop `:308-320` (`top<=bot+1` exit at `:313`). First digit sets `require_digitset` (`:325`); a digit from a different set -> **FALSE** (`:326`). Shapes: `\"12\"` (both ASCII), `\"1\" + U+0669` (ASCII + Arabic-Indic -> FALSE), `U+0669 U+066A`-style same-set pair (TRUE), two non-ASCII sets from different scripts, and a high digit like U+1FBF9 to force many chop iterations.\n13. Loop exit `ptr >= endptr` -> TRUE (`:331`); `utf` toggles `GETCHARINCTEST` (`:100`, `:332`).\n\nGood positive shapes: `\"ab\"` (Latin), Japanese Han+Hiragana, Taiwanese Han+Bopomofo, Korean Han+Hangul, Latin+Cyrillic (-> FALSE).\n\n# 7. pcre2_xclass.c\n\n### `_pcre2_xclass`\n`BOOL PRIV(xclass)(uint32_t c, PCRE2_SPTR data, const uint8_t *char_lists_end, BOOL utf)` — def `:66-67`; decl `pcre2_internal.h:2350`.\nConstants: `XCL_NOT 0x01` / `XCL_MAP 0x02` / `XCL_HASPROP 0x04` (`pcre2_internal.h:1481-1483`); items `XCL_END 0`, `XCL_SINGLE 1`, `XCL_RANGE 2`, `XCL_PROP 3`, `XCL_NOTPROP 4` (`:1485-1489`); `XCL_LIST 0x10` in 8-bit (`:1493`); list-encoding constants `:1526-1565`.\n\nShapes:\n- `not_negated = (*data & XCL_NOT)==0` (`:71`) — every terminal return is `not_negated` / `!not_negated`, so **every** shape below must be run in both polarities.\n- **8-bit forces `utf = TRUE`** at `:77`, so the non-UTF alternatives at `:282` and `:300` are dead code in this build.\n- `XCL_MAP` present and `c < 256` -> bitmap answer, returned raw (**not** polarity-adjusted) at `:85`. Shapes: bit set / bit clear.\n- `XCL_MAP` present and `c >= 256` -> skip 32 bytes (`:87`).\n- `XCL_MAP` absent -> no bitmap (`:82`).\n- Property loop `:93-263` (`do…while(*data==XCL_PROP||XCL_NOTPROP)` at `:98`/`:262`), `isprop` distinguishes PROP vs NOTPROP (`:101`). One shape per `PT_*` case, each with matching/non-matching `c`: `PT_LAMP :106`, `PT_GC :112`, `PT_PC :117`, `PT_SC :121`, `PT_SCX :125` (two sub-branches: direct script equality vs `MAPBIT` scriptx hit), `PT_ALNUM :131`, `PT_SPACE`/`PT_PXSPACE :142-143` with inner switch (`HSPACE_CASES`/`VSPACE_CASES` at `:146-147` vs the `ucp_Z` default at `:152`), `PT_WORD :158`, `PT_UCNC :166` (two sub-branches: `c < 0xa0` at `:167` testing `$ @ \\``; `c >= 0xa0` at `:175` testing the surrogate range — test c=0x24/0x40/0x60/0x41/0xa0/0xd800/0xe000), `PT_BIDICL :180`, `PT_BOOL :185`, `PT_PXGRAPH :203` (Z / C / Cf-with-exception 0x061C, 0x180E, 0x2066-0x2069), `PT_PXPRINT :216` (Zl, Zp, Cf exceptions 0x061C, 0x2066-0x2069 — note **0x180E differs from PXGRAPH**), `PT_PXPUNCT :231` (P, plus `c<128 && S`), `PT_PXXDIGIT :240` (ASCII 0-9/A-F/a-f plus fullwidth 0xFF10-0xFF19, 0xFF21-0xFF26, 0xFF41-0xFF46), `default` unreachable `:254-256`.\n- Also: property list where **no** property matches, so control falls out of the loop to the range/list code.\n- **Legacy item list** taken when `*data < XCL_LIST` (`:269`): loop `:271`; `XCL_SINGLE` (`:284-290`) with `c<x`, `c==x`, `c>x` (the `continue`); `XCL_RANGE` (`:292-304`) with `c<x`, `x<=c<=y`, `c>y`; `XCL_END` fallthrough -> `!not_negated` (`:307`).\n- **Char-list encoding** taken when `*data >= XCL_LIST`: type read as 2 big-endian units in 8-bit (`:311-312`); `next_char = char_lists_end - (GET(data,0)<<1)` (`:319`); `type &= XCL_TYPE_MASK` (`:320`).\n  - `c >= XCL_CHAR_LIST_HIGH_16_START (0x8000)` -> skip low-16 block (`:325-337`), including the `max_index == XCL_ITEM_COUNT_MASK` escape reading a 16-bit count (`:328-333`).\n  - `c < XCL_CHAR_LIST_LOW_32_START (0x10000)` -> 16-bit search (`:339-375`): `max_index==0` or `c < first` -> `XCL_BEGIN_WITH_RANGE` answer (`:352-353`); `c >= last` (`:357-358`); binary search `:363-374` with the three sub-branches `:368`, `:370`, `:372`.\n  - `c >= 0x10000` -> skip 16-bit ranges (`:378-387`) then 32-bit search (`:410-440`), same three shapes (`:418-419`, `:423-424`, `:429-439`). The `PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH == 32` block `:394-408` is dead here.\n  - Each `max_index == XCL_ITEM_COUNT_MASK` (=3) escape hatch is a separate shape (`:328`, `:345`, `:379`, `:412`).\n\n### `_pcre2_eclass`\n`BOOL PRIV(eclass)(uint32_t c, PCRE2_SPTR data_start, PCRE2_SPTR data_end, const uint8_t *char_lists_end, BOOL utf)` — def `:461-463`; decl `pcre2_internal.h:2351`. Opcodes `ECL_MAP 0x01` (`pcre2_internal.h:1570`), `ECL_AND 1`, `ECL_OR 2`, `ECL_XOR 3`, `ECL_NOT 4`, `ECL_XCLASS 5` (`:1576-1580`).\n\nShapes: `ECL_MAP` set and `c<256` -> bitmap short-circuit (`:478-481`, bit set / clear); `ECL_MAP` set and `c>=256` -> skip 32 bytes (`:484`); `ECL_MAP` clear. Then the RPN loop `:488-538`: `ECL_AND :492-497` (`stack = (stack>>1) & (stack | ~1u)`), `ECL_OR :499-504`, `ECL_XOR :506-511`, `ECL_NOT :513-517`, `ECL_XCLASS :519-527` (calls `PRIV(xclass)` on `ptr+1+LINK_SIZE`, advances by `GET(ptr,1)`, pushes the match bit), `default` unreachable `:533-535`. Final result `(stack & 1u) != 0` at `:544`; assertion `stack_depth == 1` at `:540`.\nMinimal driving shapes: single `XCLASS` (depth 1); `XCLASS XCLASS AND` / `OR` / `XOR` for each truth-table row (00,01,10,11); `XCLASS NOT`; nested 3-operand expressions to exercise stack depth >2; and `stack` shifting past bit 0 (>1 pending operand).\n\n### `_pcre2_update_classbits`\n`void PRIV(update_classbits)(uint32_t ptype, uint32_t pdata, BOOL negated, uint8_t *classbits)` — def **`pcre2_compile_class.c:751-866`** (not in pcre2_xclass.c); decl `pcre2_compile.h:303`; guarded by `SUPPORT_UNICODE` (`:749`). Comment `:754` pairs it with `PRIV(xclass)`.\n\nShapes: `ptype == PT_ANY` early return (`:760-764`) — `negated` FALSE -> `memset(classbits,0xff,32)`, TRUE -> leaves buffer untouched. Otherwise the 0-255 loop (`:766-865`) with one case per property: `PT_LAMP :774`, `PT_GC :779`, `PT_PC :783`, `PT_SC :787`, `PT_SCX :791` (two disjuncts), `PT_ALNUM :796`, `PT_SPACE`/`PT_PXSPACE :801-802` (inner `HSPACE_BYTE_CASES`/`VSPACE_BYTE_CASES` `:805-806` vs `ucp_Z` default `:811`), `PT_WORD :816`, `PT_UCNC :823` (note the `c >= 0xa0` blanket, differing from `xclass`'s surrogate test), `PT_BIDICL :828`, `PT_BOOL :832`, `PT_PXGRAPH :837`, `PT_PXPRINT :843`, `PT_PXPUNCT :849`, `default`/`PT_PXXDIGIT :854-858` (ASCII only — **no fullwidth**, unlike `xclass`). `negated` inverts every bit at `:862`; bits OR-ed into the incoming buffer at `:863`, pointer advanced every 8 (`:864`) — so a **pre-populated non-zero `classbits`** is a distinct shape from an all-zero one. `pdata` matters only for GC/PC/SC/SCX/BIDICL/BOOL.\n\n# 8. pcre2_chkdint.c — `_pcre2_ckd_smul`\n\n`BOOL PRIV(ckd_smul)(PCRE2_SIZE *r, int a, int b)` — def `:65-66`; decl `pcre2_internal.h:2326`.\n\nThis build has **no** `HAVE_BUILTIN_MUL_OVERFLOW` (`config.h:66`) and `INT64_OR_DOUBLE == int64_t` (`pcre2_internal.h:182`), so the active code is `:75-83`: `PCRE2_ASSERT(a >= 0 && b >= 0)` (`:77`), `m = (int64_t)a * (int64_t)b` (`:79`), overflow test `sizeof(m) > sizeof(*r) && m > PCRE2_SIZE_MAX` (`:82`), store `:83`, `return FALSE` (`:91`).\n\nShapes:\n- No overflow, ordinary: (0,0), (1,1), (0, INT_MAX), (INT_MAX, 0), (2,3), (65536, 65536).\n- Products that exceed 32 bits but fit in `int64_t`: (INT_MAX, INT_MAX) = 0x3FFFFFFF00000001, (100000, 100000). On LP64 `sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE)==8 == sizeof(int64_t)`, so `sizeof(m) > sizeof(*r)` is **false** and the function returns FALSE even for huge products — the 64-bit product is stored verbatim. This is the important shape: **on a 64-bit target `_pcre2_ckd_smul` never reports overflow** in this configuration.\n- Overflow-reporting return TRUE at `:82` is only reachable when `sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE) < 8` (32-bit target). Note the `#else` arm at `:85` and the builtin arm at `:71` are compiled out.\n- Negative inputs violate the assertion at `:77` (release build: UB-ish, product stored as-is). Include (-1, 2) and (INT_MIN, -1) if the harness tolerates assertion-disabled behaviour.\n\n# 9. pcre2_find_bracket.c — `_pcre2_find_bracket`\n\n`PCRE2_SPTR PRIV(find_bracket)(PCRE2_SPTR code, BOOL utf, int number)` — def `:66-67`; decl `pcre2_internal.h:2330`.\n\nSpecial handling / shapes:\n- `OP_END` -> NULL (`:73`). Shape: number not present.\n- `OP_XCLASS`, `OP_ECLASS` -> length from `GET(code,1)` (`:81`).\n- `OP_CALLOUT_STR` -> length from `GET(code, 1+2*LINK_SIZE)` (`:82`).\n- `OP_REVERSE`, `OP_VREVERSE` -> **if `number < 0` return this code** (`:86-88`); else skip by table (`:89`). Shapes: pattern with a fixed-length lookbehind (`(?<=abc)x`) and a variable-length one (`(?<=ab|abc)x`) called with `number = -1`; same patterns with `number > 0`.\n- `OP_CBRA`, `OP_SCBRA`, `OP_CBRAPOS`, `OP_SCBRAPOS` -> compare `GET2(code, 1+LINK_SIZE)` to `number` (`:94-99`). Shapes: match on first/second/nth group; `SCBRA` variants arise from groups that can match empty (`(a*)`); `CBRAPOS` from possessive groups (`(?>(a))`/`(a)++`).\n- Named-vs-numbered: the function only ever matches by **number**; the negative-`number` call is exclusively the lookbehind search. Callers wanting a named group resolve the name to a number first.\n- `switch` at `:109-138`: `OP_TYPESTAR/MINSTAR/PLUS/MINPLUS/QUERY/MINQUERY/POSSTAR/POSPLUS/POSQUERY` with `code[1]` being `OP_PROP`/`OP_NOTPROP` -> `+2` (`:111-121`). Shapes: `\\d+` (no extra) vs `\\p{L}+` and `\\P{L}+` (extra 2).\n- `OP_TYPEUPTO/TYPEMINUPTO/TYPEEXACT/TYPEPOSUPTO` with `code[1+IMM2_SIZE]` a prop -> `+2` (`:123-129`). Shapes: `\\d{2,5}` vs `\\p{L}{2,5}`, `\\p{L}{3}`.\n- `OP_MARK`, `OP_COMMIT_ARG`, `OP_PRUNE_ARG`, `OP_SKIP_ARG`, `OP_THEN_ARG` -> `code += code[1]` (`:131-136`). Shapes: `(*MARK:abc)(x)`, `(*COMMIT:a)`, `(*PRUNE:a)`, `(*SKIP:a)`, `(*THEN:a)`.\n- Fixed length from `PRIV(OP_lengths)[c]` (`:142`).\n- `MAYBE_UTF_MULTI` block `:148-209` (**active** in this build): with `utf` TRUE, the 56 listed char/repeat opcodes get `GET_EXTRALEN(code[-1])` added when `HAS_EXTRALEN` (`:207`). Shapes: `utf=TRUE` with a multi-byte literal before the target group (`é(x)`, `\\x{10000}(x)`), a repeat of a multi-byte char (`é+(x)`, `é{2,3}(x)`, `[^é]*(x)` for the NOT* forms), and the same patterns with `utf=FALSE` (the `(void)utf` path at `:211` is compiled out here).\n\n# 10. pcre2_compile_cgroup.c — `_pcre2_compile_get_hash_from_name`\n\n`uint16_t PRIV(compile_get_hash_from_name)(PCRE2_SPTR name, uint32_t length)` — def `:58-68`; decl `pcre2_compile.h:326`, name macro `pcre2_compile.h:273`.\n\nBody is branch-free: `hash = (uint16_t)((name[0] & 0x7f) | ((name[length-1] & 0xff) << 7));` (`:65`), with `PCRE2_ASSERT(length > 0)` (`:63`) and `PCRE2_ASSERT(hash <= NAMED_GROUP_HASH_MASK)` (`:66`; mask `0x7fff` at `pcre2_compile.h:294`).\n\nWhat varies: only `name[0]` and `name[length-1]`; **all middle characters are ignored**. Shapes: `length == 1` (first and last are the same unit, so the byte is used twice); `length == 2`; long names; two different names sharing first+last chars (`\"abc\"`/`\"axc\"` -> identical hash — collision shape); `name[0]` with bit 0x80 set (masked to 0x7f); `name[length-1] == 0xff` (max hash 0x7fff); mixed-case names. Consumer: `PRIV(compile_find_named_group)` at `:86-99`, which combines the hash with `PRIV(strncmp)`.\n\n# 11. pcre2_context.c — `_pcre2_memctl_malloc`\n\n`extern void *PRIV(memctl_malloc)(size_t size, pcre2_memctl *memctl)` — def `:81-97`; decl `pcre2_internal.h:2336`. `pcre2_memctl` struct: `pcre2_internal.h:2105-2109`.\n\nShapes:\n1. `memctl == NULL` -> `malloc(size)` (`:85`), then the header is filled with `default_malloc`/`default_free`/`NULL` (`:89-94`; `default_free` at `:59-63`).\n2. `memctl != NULL` -> `memctl->malloc(size, memctl->memory_data)` (`:86`), then `*newmemctl = *memctl` copies all three fields (`:95`).\n3. Allocation failure -> `return NULL` early (`:87`); drive with a custom `memctl->malloc` that returns NULL, and (for the NULL-memctl path) an absurd `size`.\n4. `size` smaller than `sizeof(pcre2_memctl)` -> the header write at `:88-95` overruns; a size-boundary shape worth recording.\n5. `memctl->memory_data` non-NULL, to confirm it is threaded through to the user allocator and copied into the block header.\n\n# 12. pcre2_study.c — `_pcre2_study`\n\n`int PRIV(study)(pcre2_real_code *re)` — def `:1915-1916`; decl `pcre2_internal.h:2346`. Doc block `:1902-1912`.\n\nWhat it computes:\n- **Start bitmap** `re->start_bitmap` (via `set_start_bits`, `:1092`; `SET_BIT` macro `:56`), plus flag `PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET`.\n- **First code unit** `re->first_codeunit` + `PCRE2_FIRSTSET`/`PCRE2_FIRSTCASELESS`, derived by collapsing a bitmap with 1 or 2 bits (`:1946-2042`).\n- May **clear** `PCRE2_LASTSET|PCRE2_LASTCASELESS` and `re->last_codeunit` (`:2028-2031`) when the deduced first unit equals the required last unit — the `/a*a/` case.\n- **Minimum subject length** `re->minlength`, clamped to `UINT16_MAX` (`:2076-2077`), via `find_minlength` (`:2062`).\n- Return codes: 0 normal; 1 = `SSB_UNKNOWN` from `set_start_bits` (`:1935-1939`); 2 = missing capturing bracket, `find_minlength` -2 (`:2069-2071`); 3 = unrecognized opcode, -3 (`:2072-2074`). 1/2/3 are all `PCRE2_DEBUG_UNREACHABLE`.\n\nShapes that **skip** `set_start_bits` entirely: `(re->flags & (PCRE2_FIRSTSET|PCRE2_STARTLINE)) != 0` (`:1929`). Drive with `/abc/` (first unit known -> FIRSTSET) and a multiline `/^abc/m` (STARTLINE).\n\nShapes that **run** `set_start_bits`:\n- `SSB_DONE` -> bitmap post-processing (`:1949`): all-zero-ish cases, exactly one bit set (-> FIRSTSET, e.g. `/(?:a)x|(?:a)y/`-shaped patterns), exactly two bits that are case-pairs (-> FIRSTSET|FIRSTCASELESS; `/[Ww]ord/`, `/(word|WORD)/` per comment `:1954-1956`), two bits that are **not** a case pair -> `goto DONE` keeping FIRSTMAPSET (`/[ab]c/`), three or more bits -> `goto DONE` (`/[abc]x/`), a bit whose lowest-bit extraction fails (`y != x`, `:1968`) i.e. a byte with >1 bit -> DONE.\n- 8-bit UTF specific: `utf && c > 127` -> `goto DONE` (`:1991`) — pattern like `/[\\x{e9}\\x{ff}]x/` with PCRE2_UTF.\n- Caseless-set escape: `UCD_CASESET(c) != 0` -> DONE (`:2003`); `c > 127` uses `UCD_OTHERCASE` rather than the `fcc` table (`:2004`) — drive with PCRE2_UTF or PCRE2_UCP set (`utf||ucp` at `:2001`).\n- `SSB_FAIL` returns from `set_start_bits` leave the bitmap unused. Sources: the big opcode list at `:1196-1208` (`OP_REF`, `OP_REFI`, `OP_REVERSE`, `OP_VREVERSE`, `OP_RREF`, `OP_SCOND`, `OP_SET_SOM`, `OP_SKIP`, `OP_SKIP_ARG`, `OP_SOD`, `OP_SOM`, `OP_THEN`, `OP_THEN_ARG`); `OP_PROP` with `tcode[1] != PT_CLIST` (`:1223` — `/\\p{L}x/`) vs the PT_CLIST path that *does* set bits (`:1224-1237`, which itself calls `PRIV(ord2utf)` in 8-bit UTF at `:1229-1234`); `OP_ANY`/`OP_ALLANY` under `OP_TYPE*QUERY` (`:1623`); `OP_ECLASS` (`:1720`, extended-set classes always give up); `OP_XCLASS` with `XCL_HASPROP` set or a negative XCLASS without a map (`:1734-1736`).\n- `SSB_CONTINUE` / `SSB_TOODEEP` (`:1373`, `:1381`, `:1106` depth > 1000) — deeply nested groups; at top level `SSB_CONTINUE` means the bitmap is not usable.\n- `SSB_UNKNOWN` -> return 1 (`:1132`, `:1783`) — only via a corrupt code block.\n\nShapes for the **minlength** phase: gate at `:2058-2059` is `(re->flags & (PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY|PCRE2_HASACCEPT)) == 0 && re->top_backref <= MAX_CACHE_BACKREF` (128, `:52`).\n- Skipped: pattern that can match empty (`/a*/`), pattern containing `(*ACCEPT)`, pattern with >128 backreferences.\n- `min == -1` \"cannot compute\" -> minlength left 0 (`:2064-2065`). Sources: recursion/complexity counter `(*countptr)++ > 1000` (`:129`); `OP_ACCEPT`/`OP_ASSERT_ACCEPT` (`:220-222`); `OP_ANYBYTE` (`\\C`) in UTF mode (`:388`). Also the early `return 0` for `OP_SBRA..OP_SCOND` at `:120`.\n- Normal: `/abc/` -> 3; `/a{2,5}/` -> 2; alternation `/abc|de/` -> 2; backreference `/(ab)\\1/` -> 4; a pattern whose min exceeds `UINT16_MAX` to hit the clamp at `:2076`.\n- Return 2 (`-2` at `:500`, `:560`) needs a missing capturing bracket; return 3 (`-3` at `:758`, `:765`) an unknown opcode.\n\n# 13. pcre2_auto_possess.c — `_pcre2_auto_possessify`\n\n`int PRIV(auto_possessify)(PCRE2_UCHAR *code, const compile_block *cb)` — def `:1171-1172`; decl `pcre2_internal.h:2322`. Doc `:1152-1169`. Note it **mutates** the compiled code in place.\n\nDecision tables (compare wholesale in a differential test as well — they are `static`, so only reachable through behaviour):\n- `autoposstab[APTROWS][APT