prop-extension `+2` for `OP_TYPE{STAR,MINSTAR,PLUS,MINPLUS,QUERY,MINQUERY,POSSTAR,POSPLUS,POSQUERY}` (`:1300-1310`) and for `OP_TYPE{UPTO,MINUPTO,EXACT,POSUPTO}` (`:1312-1317`); `OP_CALLOUT_STR` (`:1319`); `OP_XCLASS`/`OP_ECLASS` (`:1323-1326`); `OP_MARK`/`OP_COMMIT_ARG`/`OP_PRUNE_ARG`/`OP_SKIP_ARG`/`OP_THEN_ARG` (`:1330-1336`); then `PRIV(OP_lengths)[c]` (`:1341`) and the `MAYBE_UTF_MULTI` extra-length fixup for the ~56 char-repeat opcodes (`:1348-1400+`).\n5. `rec_limit = 1000` (`:1176`) threaded into `compare_opcodes` (`:1201`, `:1266`); `utf` and `ucp` read from `cb->external_options` (`:1178-1179`).\n\nPattern shapes that **trigger** possessification (from `autoposstab`, rows/cols per `:75-105`): `\\d+\\D`, `\\d+\\s`, `\\d+\\W`, `\\d+\\R`, `\\d+\\h`, `\\d+\\v`, `\\d+\\Z`, `\\d+\\z`, `\\d+$`, `\\d+$` multiline; `\\D+\\d`; `\\S+\\s`; `\\s+\\d`, `\\s+\\S`, `\\s+\\w`; `\\W+\\d`, `\\W+\\w`; `\\w+\\s`, `\\w+\\W`, `\\w+\\R`; `.+\\R`; `\\R+\\d`, `\\R+\\s`, `\\R+\\w`, `\\R+.`, `\\R+\\h`; `\\H+\\h`; `\\h+\\d`, `\\h+\\S`, `\\h+\\w`, `\\h+\\R`, `\\h+\\H`, `\\h+\\v`; `\\V+\\R`, `\\V+\\v`; `\\v+\\d`, `\\v+\\S`, `\\v+\\w`, `\\v+\\h`, `\\v+\\V`; `\\X+\\z`; plus literal/class shapes `a+b`, `[ab]+c`, `a*\\d`.\nShapes that **decline**: `\\d+\\d`, `\\w+\\w`, `.+.`, `\\C+x`, anything with `\\P`/`\\p` on either side of the plain table (rows `:1046`-equivalents are all zero at `:1047-1048` of the table — `:1046`/`:1047` in the listing are the `\\P`/`\\p` all-zero rows at file lines `:1044`? — concretely the two all-zero rows at `pcre2_auto_possess.c:1044` region are rows `/* \\P */` and `/* \\p */` at `:87-88`); already-possessive input (`a++b`, `\\d++\\D`); `OP_EXACT`-style fixed repeats (`a{3}b`, since `c > OP_MINUPTO` -> `end = NULL`); overlapping classes `[a-z]+[c-x]`; recursion beyond `rec_limit`.\nProperty-pair shapes exercising `propposstab` values: 3 -> `\\p{L}+\\P{L}`; 1 -> `\\p{Lu&Ll-ish LAMP}+\\s`-style distinct groups; 2 -> `\\p{Han}+\\p{Latin}` / `\\p{L}+\\p{N}`; 4/5 -> `\\p{L}+\\p{Nd}` and `\\p{Nd}+\\p{L}`; 6-11 -> ALNUM/SPACE/WORD vs general category (`[[:alnum:]]+\\p{Z}`); 12-17 -> the same vs particular category (`[[:space:]]+\\p{Cc}`); 0 -> `\\p{Bidi_Control}+…`, `PT_CLIST`, `PT_BIDICL`, `PT_BOOL` rows.\n\n---\n\n# Exported DATA tables\n\n### pcre2_tables.c\n| Symbol | Def | Type / length | What varies across entries |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `_pcre2_OP_lengths` | `pcre2_tables.c:67` (macro `OP_LENGTHS` = `pcre2_internal.h:1977-2065`) | `const uint8_t[]`, **173** entries (`OP_TABLE_LENGTH`, `pcre2_internal.h:1908`; last opcode `OP_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY` = 172 at `:1901`) | Per-opcode compiled size. Values in this build (LINK_SIZE=2, IMM2_SIZE=2): 1, 2, 3, 4 (=2+IMM2), 3 (=1+LINK), 5 (=1+LINK+IMM2), 1+2\\*IMM2=5. Entries for `OP_XCLASS`/`OP_ECLASS`/`OP_CALLOUT_STR` are 0/placeholder — actual length lives in the code. Compare the whole 173-byte array. |\n| `_pcre2_hspace_list` | `:72` (macro `pcre2_internal.h:377-381`) | `const uint32_t[]`, **20** elements | `CHAR_HT(0x09), CHAR_SPACE(0x20), CHAR_NBSP(0xA0), 0x1680, 0x180e, 0x2000-0x200a, 0x202f, 0x205f, 0x3000, NOTACHAR` — ascending, `NOTACHAR`-terminated. |\n| `_pcre2_vspace_list` | `:73` (macro `pcre2_internal.h:410-411`) | `const uint32_t[]`, **8** elements | `CHAR_LF(0x0A), CHAR_VT(0x0B), CHAR_FF(0x0C), CHAR_CR(0x0D), CHAR_NEL(0x85), 0x2028, 0x2029, NOTACHAR`. |\n| `_pcre2_callout_start_delims` | `:84-87` | `const uint32_t[]`, **9** elements | `` ` ' \" ^ % # $ { `` then 0 terminator. |\n| `_pcre2_callout_end_delims` | `:89-92` | `const uint32_t[]`, **9** elements | Same as start except the last is `}` instead of `{`; positionally paired with the start table. Index-wise identical for 7 of 8 entries. |\n| `_pcre2_utf8_table1` | `:114-115` | `const int[6]` | Max code point per encoded length: `0x7f, 0x7ff, 0xffff, 0x1fffff, 0x3ffffff, 0x7fffffff`. |\n| `_pcre2_utf8_table1_size` | `:117` | `const unsigned` = **6** | Scalar. |\n| `_pcre2_utf8_table2` | `:122` | `const int[6]` | Lead-