the no-op `set_recursion_memory_management`), `pcre2_config` (numeric + string keys), `pcre2_get_error_message` |\n| C078–C123 | `pcre2_compile` — argument/option legality, `PCRE2_LITERAL` subset, each option family paired with the pattern shapes that exercise its branches, all context limits, workspace/heap/LINK_SIZE=2/65535 boundaries, class/property/assertion/lookbehind/conditional/callout/verb/pso/inline-option shapes, plus `code_copy`/`code_copy_with_tables` |\n| C124–C125 | `pcre2_match_data_create` / `_from_pattern` and the getters |\n| C126–C157 | `pcre2_match` — validation, start-optimizations, the three limits, recursion-loop check, `COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT`, UTF/`MATCH_INVALID_UTF` fragments, partial matching, newlines, and one row per opcode family (backrefs, recursion, atomic/possessive, assertions, `(*scs:)`, `\\K`, verbs, script runs, `\\X`, classes, callouts, anchors/boundaries, `.`/`\\C`) |\n| C158–C167 | `pcre2_dfa_match` — WSSIZE, `DFA_RESTART`, `DFA_SHORTEST`, multi-match ovector, `DFA_UITEM`/`UCOND`/`UFUNC`/`UINVALID_UTF`/`DFA_RECURSE`, DFA limits, partial |\n| C168–C169 | `pcre2_next_match` and `do_bumpalong` |\n| C170–C183 | `pcre2_substitute` (all 8 `SUBSTITUTE_*` bits, `$`/`\\` syntax, EXTENDED `${:-}`/`${:+}`, case forcing, both callouts, overflow bookkeeping, `SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED` identity checks) |\n| C184–C187 | all 11 `pcre2_substring_*` |\n| C188–C189 | `pcre2_serialize_encode`/`decode`/`get_number_of_codes` |\n| C190–C192 | `pcre2_pattern_info` (all `PCRE2_INFO_*`) and `pcre2_callout_enumerate` |\n| C193–C199 | `pcre2_pattern_convert` (mode legality, UTF, POSIX basic, POSIX extended, glob stars, glob classes, the two composite GLOB flags) |\n| C200 | the whole free-function family (hidden `pcre2_memctl` prefix contract) |\n| C201–C202 | the JIT stub family, public and PRIV |\n\n## Axes deliberately merged (with justification)\n\n1. **`pcre2_substring_copy_byname` / `get_byname` / `length_byname` share one row (C184)**, and `copy_bynumber`/`get_bynumber`/`length_bynumber` share C185. The three by-name functions are line-for-line the same branch set (`pcre2_substring.c:68-91`, `156-179`, `263-286`) differing only in the final delegate; splitting would produce identical input shapes.\n2. **`pcre2_get_ovector_pointer` / `_count` / `_startchar` / `_mark` / `_match_data_size` folded into C124/C125/C157.** They are unconditional field reads with no branches at all (`pcre2_match_data.c:117-170`); the only meaningful axis is *what a preceding match left in the field*, which is where they now live.\n3. **The 21 `PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_ERRn` cases are 4 rows (C026–C029) rather than 21**, grouped by the shared code path (valid / truncation / bad-continuation-byte / range-and-overlong). Each row still names the exact triggering byte sequence for every individual error number, so no error is lost.\n4. **`autoposstab` is one row (C064) listing 41 patterns** rather than 41 rows: the table is a single 2-D lookup at one call site, so the distinguishing input is which pattern you feed, not a configuration change.\n5. **`pcre2_set_recursion_memory_management` is merged into C074** with `set_recursion_limit`, because the C body discards all four arguments and returns 0 (`pcre2_context.c:514-527`) — there is literally nothing else for the C to branch on.\n6. **`PCRE2_NO_JIT`, the JIT stubs, and `PCRE2_CONFIG_JITTARGET` are 3 rows (C139, C201, C202), not one per stub.** Without `SUPPORT_JIT` every stub returns a constant; the rows exist only to pin that the options are *accepted* rather than rejected, and that `PCRE2_INFO_JITSIZE`/`PCRE2_CONFIG_JIT` read 0.\n7. **`pcre2_pattern_info` keys are 3 rows (C190–C192), not 27.** C190 covers the gate ordering (the NULL-`where` length query succeeds *before* `re` is validated — worth its own row), C191 enumerates one non-trivial pattern per key inline, since the per-key code is a one-line field read in a single switch.\n\nOne finding worth flagging for the translation work: `_pcre2_ckd_smul` (C050) **can never report overflow in this build** — with `HAVE_BUILTIN_MUL_OVERFLOW` undefined and `INT64_OR_DOUBLE = int64_t`, the guard is `sizeof(int64_t) > sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE)`, which is false on LP64 (`pcre2_chkdint.c:75-91`). A Rust translation that returns `true` on `i64` overflow would diverge.","usage":{"total_tokens":275178,"tool_uses":49,"duration_ms":1391876},"uuid":"036d7352-9373-4c7a-ae0f-be8425b67cca","session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503"}
