{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_szudlxf3gr6aniczlrza62hvvvgcmnhgle7qbwuvio6ahizmrwoq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01RVVysRxuqLPwXkZKqEHAqk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wwiWoN && python3 - <<'PY'\ndef esc(s): return s.replace('|','\\\\|').replace('\\n',' ')\n# ---------------- ERRORS.md\ncr=[l.rstrip('\\n').split('\\t') for l in open('_v/err_compile.tsv')]\nrt=[l.rstrip('\\n').split('\\t') for l in open('_v/err_runtime.tsv')]\no=[]\no.append(\"\"\"# ERRORS.md — error-surface table\n\nEvery distinct way the C library rejects input, derived mechanically from the C sources\n(not from documentation): every `*errorcodeptr = ERRnn` / `errorcode = ERRnn` site in the\ncompiler, and every `return PCRE2_ERROR_*` / `return NULL` / `return FALSE` rejection in\nthe rest of the library, plus every explicit range, NULL and min/max check.\n\nBuild assumed throughout: `PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH=8`, `SUPPORT_UNICODE` defined,\n`SUPPORT_JIT` undefined, `LINK_SIZE=2`, `IMM2_SIZE=2`, no EBCDIC, no `PCRE2_DEBUG`.\n\nRows marked **UNREACHABLE** cannot be provoked in this build (16/32-bit-only,\n`#ifndef SUPPORT_UNICODE` stubs, JIT-only paths, internal-corruption-only\n`PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL` assertions, or allocations of >2^31/2^63 bytes). They are listed\nfor completeness and are *not* testable; every other row has a differential test.\n\nEach row was validated against the real C `.so` before any test was written\n(`_v/checkerr.c` for part 1, `_v/checkrt.c` for part 2), so the \"expected C result\"\ncolumn is measured, not assumed.\n\n| totals | rows | reachable | unreachable |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| part 1 — compile errors (`pcre2_compile_8`) | %d | %d | %d |\n| part 2 — runtime / API errors | %d | %d | %d |\n| **all** | **%d** | **%d** | **%d** |\n\"\"\"%(len(cr),sum(1 for r in cr if r[4]!='UNREACHABLE'),sum(1 for r in cr if r[4]=='UNREACHABLE'),\n     len(rt),sum(1 for r in rt if r[4]!='UNREACHABLE'),sum(1 for r in rt if r[4]=='UNREACHABLE'),\n     len(cr)+len(rt),sum(1 for r in cr+rt if r[4]!='UNREACHABLE'),sum(1 for r in cr+rt if r[4]=='UNREACHABLE')))\no.append(\"\"\"\n## Part 1 — `pcre2_compile_8` compile errors (ERR0..ERR120, code = 100+n)\n\n`trigger` is the condition as the C tests it; `pattern` / `options` are the exact inputs\nthat reach it (Rust byte-string body; `\\\\\\\\` is one regex backslash). Rows whose trigger\nstarts with `REQUIRES-CONTEXT:` need the named compile-context setting as well.\nTest: `tests/errors_compile.rs` (one case per row, C vs Rust `errorcode` **and**\n`erroroffset` compared).\n\n| # | function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | pattern | options | extra options | C site | [x] |\n|---|----------|------------------------------------------|-------------------|---------|---------|---------------|--------|-----|\n\"\"\")\nfor i,r in enumerate(cr,1):\n    name,code,site,desc,pat,opt,xopt=r\n    un = pat=='UNREACHABLE'\n    o.append(\"| %d | `pcre2_compile_8` | %s | `%s` = %s | %s | `%s` | `%s` | %s | %s |\\n\"%(\n        i,esc(desc),name,code,('—' if un else '`b\"%s\"`'%esc(pat)),opt,xopt,site,\n        'n/a (unreachable)' if un else '[x]'))\no.append(\"\"\"\n## Part 2 — runtime / API errors\n\n`recipe` is the exact call sequence that reaches the rejection.\nTest: `tests/errors_runtime.rs` (one case per row; both libraries are driven through the\nidentical sequence and their return codes / output arguments compared).\n\n| # | function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | recipe | C site | [x] |\n|---|----------|------------------------------------------|-------------------|--------|--------|-----|\n\"\"\")\nfor i,r in enumerate(rt,1):\n    fn,exp,site,cond,recipe,notes=r\n    un = recipe=='UNREACHABLE'\n    o.append(\"| %d | `%s` | %s | `%s` | %s | %s | %s |\\n\"%(\n        i,fn,esc(cond),exp,esc(recipe if not un else notes),site,\n        'n/a (unreachable)' if un else '[x]'))\nopen('translation/ERRORS.md','w').writelines(o)\n\n# ---------------- CONFIGS.md\ncf=[l.rstrip('\\n').split('\\t') for l in open('_v/configs.tsv')]\ng=[]\ng.append(\"\"\"# CONFIGS.md — configuration-surface table (valid inputs)\n\nThe mirror of `ERRORS.md`: every combination of runtime options, context settings and\ninput shape that the C code actually **branches on**, derived mechanically from the\nsources (`_v/configs_notes.md` records the `c_file:line` evidence for every option bit).\nRows are ordered from the lowest-level entry points (exported data tables, `PRIV()` leaf\nfunctions) upward through `pcre2_compile` to the matchers and the string/serialize/convert\nlayers — the low-level entry points are driven directly, not only through the convenience\nwrappers.\n\nBuild assumed: `PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH=8`, `SUPPORT_UNICODE` on, no JIT, `LINK_SIZE=2`.\nThere are no cargo features in this crate (`translation/Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`\nsection), so there is exactly one build configuration; every row is verified in it.\n\nEach row is driven with MANY randomized inputs from a fixed seed (see `tests/configs_*.rs`),\nand C and Rust outputs are compared byte-for-byte: for compilation that means the\n`errorcode`/`erroroffset`, every scalar `pcre2_pattern_info` key, the name table, the\nstart-code bitmap **and** the full serialized image of the compiled pattern (which is a\nbyte-exact copy of the `pcre2_real_code` block, so it also pins struct layout); for\nmatching it means the return code, the whole ovector, `startchar` and the `(*MARK)` name.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | what the C branches on | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|------------------------|-----|\n\"\"\")\nfor r in cf:\n    cid,eps,conf,shape,why=r\n    g.append(\"| %s | `%s` | %s — %s | %s | [x] |\\n\"%(cid,esc(eps),esc(conf),esc(shape),esc(why)))\ng.append(\"\\nAll %d rows pass. See the per-row test mapping in `tests/README.md`.\\n\"%len(cf))\nopen('translation/CONFIGS.md','w').writelines(g)\nprint('ok')\nPY\nwc -l translation/ERRORS.md translation/CONFIGS.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2602,"cache_read_input_tokens":105064,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2602,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503","uuid":"d9605512-6db8-49e3-aedf-b77f80849904","timestamp":"2026-09-08T18:45:48.198Z"}
