bol_name\")` for anything not in the struct.\n40\t* `api.data(\"_pcre2_utt_8\")` -> `*const u8` for exported DATA symbols.\n41\t* `api.compile_probe(pattern, len, options, ccontext) -> CompileOut` — compiles and\n42\t  captures EVERYTHING observable: errorcode, erroroffset, every scalar\n43\t  `pcre2_pattern_info` key, the name table, the start bitmap, and the full serialized\n44\t  image of the compiled pattern (`pcre2_serialize_encode`, whose output is a byte-exact\n45\t  copy of the `pcre2_real_code` block with pointer fields zeroed — so comparing it\n46\t  compares every compiled opcode and the struct layout). Two `CompileOut`s compare with\n47\t  `assert_eq!`.\n48\t* `read_match(api, match_data, rc) -> MatchOut` — rc + full ovector + startchar + mark.\n49\t* `Rng::new(seed)` — deterministic xorshift: `.below(n)`, `.pick(&slice)`, `.byte()`,\n50\t  `.next_u64()`. ALWAYS use a fixed seed so runs are reproducible.\n51\t* All `PCRE2_*` option/error/info/config constants are already defined in `common`.\n52\t\n53\t## Method for each CONFIGS.md row you are assigned\n54\t1. Read the row in `_v/configs.tsv` (5 tab-separated fields:\n55\t   id, entry points, configuration, input shape, what-the-C-branches-on).\n56\t2. Build the configuration EXACTLY as described (options, context settings).\n57\t3. Drive the SAME inputs through the C `.so` and the Rust `.so` and assert the outputs\n58\t   are byte-identical — return codes, every output argument, every buffer the call\n59\t   filled in, and the length/`PCRE2_SIZE` values.\n60\t4. Use MANY randomized inputs per row (a fixed-seed loop of at least ~200 iterations\n61\t   where the row admits random data), not one hand-picked value; combine the row's\n62\t   fixed shapes with random subjects/lengths/offsets. Also include the explicit\n63\t   hand-picked shapes the row names.\n64\t5. One `#[test]` fn per row (or per small group of closely-related rows), named after\n65\t   the row id, e.g. `fn c078_compile_option_legality()`. Print the row id with\n66\t   `println!` so the mapping is visible with `--nocapture`.\n67\t6. Tests in one file run CONCURRENTLY on separate threads: no shared mutable globals\n68\t   unless the test is the only user (prefer thread-local or per-test state).\n69\t\n70\t## Memory rules (these tests deliberately handle raw pointers)\n71\t* Anything allocated by a library MUST be freed with THAT library's free function\n72\t  (`pcre2_code_free_8`, `pcre2_match_data_free_8`, `pcre2_substring_free_8`,\n73\t  `pcre2_substring_list_free_8`, `pcre2_serialize_free_8`, `pcre2_converted_pattern_free_8`,\n74\t  `pcre2_maketables_free_8`, the context frees). Never pass a C-allocated pointer to a\n75\t  Rust free function or vice versa.\n76\t* Never dereference a NULL result; assert both libraries returned NULL together instead.\n77\t\n78\t## Building and running\n79\tThe Rust `.so` under test is `translation/target/release/libpcre2.so` and is ALREADY\n80\tbuilt; if you need to rebuild it: `cd translation && cargo build --release --offline`.\n81\tThe crates.io network is BLOCKED — always pass `--offline` to cargo.\n82\tUse your OWN target dir so you do not fight other agents for the cargo lock:\n83\t\n84\t    cd translation && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-$$ timeout 900 \\\n85\t      cargo test --offline --test <YOUR_TEST_FILE_STEM> -- --nocapture\n86\t\n87\t(`CARGO_TARGET_DIR` only moves the test binary; the `.so` paths are absolute.)\n88\tNever run a single command longer than 900s. If one row's test is too slow, shrink the\n89\titeration count for that row (keep at least 50 iterations) rather than dropping the row.\n90\t\n91\t## Reporting (your final message)\n92\tReport, concisely:\n93\t1. The file you wrote and the row ids covered (confirm every assigned id has a test).\n94\t2. The exact command you ran and the pass/fail counts.\n95\t3. For EVERY divergence found: the row id, the MINIMAL reproducing input (pattern,\n96\t   options, subject, offsets — as Rust literals), the C output and the Rust output, and\n97\t   the C source location that computes it. Do not attempt a fix. If you found none, say\n98\t   \"no divergences\" explicitly.\n99\t4. Anything in your assigned rows you could NOT test, and precisely why.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01ECtBBNfFJNi6SYKFLUKdLD","session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503","uuid":"e71d0ff0-3ff7-4059-b5f8-796edb572643","timestamp":"2026-09-08T18:49:16.628Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Tests for data tables + leaf fns"}
