buffer bytes compared.\n- C026–C029 `valid_utf`: all 21 `UTF8_ERRn` shapes with exact `*erroroffset`, every valid code point (1 112 064), **100 000** random byte strings (len 0..40); rc histogram shows all 21 error codes plus rc 0 hit.\n- C043–C048 `xclass`/`eclass`: real OP_XCLASS/OP_ECLASS blocks obtained by compiling in the C lib; opcode located at `code_start+1+LINK_SIZE` and verified three ways (OP_BRA at `code_start`, plausible `GET(code,1)`, OP_KET exactly at block end). Each block swept over **all** 0..=0x10FFFF plus 20 000 random points × both `utf` values (≈204 M FFI calls in C044 alone). `char_lists_end` = `(uint8_t*)re + re->code_start`, matching `mb->start_code`.\n- C051–C053 `find_bracket`: real compiled blocks, every bracket number present plus absent ones plus negative numbers.\n\n## Notes on things that could not be tested as literally written\n\n1. **C048 `ECL_NOT` / \"a single ECL_XCLASS\"** — the compiler *never* emits `ECL_NOT`: it applies De Morgan and folds negation into the nested XCLASS's `XCL_NOT` flag (verified over 20+ candidate patterns incl. `(?[![\\p{L}]|[\\x{100}]])`, `(?[!(!(...)|...)])`); nor does it ever emit a body consisting of one bare `ECL_XCLASS`. To reach those arms I reassembled RPN programs out of `ECL_XCLASS` items copied **verbatim** from C-compiled blocks (asserting each copied item uses the legacy, non-char-list encoding so `char_lists_end` stays valid), covering single-XCLASS, AND/OR/XOR, NOT, NOT NOT, and depth-3 stacks, with a proven 4/4 truth-table for both operand pairs.\n2. **C044 `PT_ANY` / `PT_CLIST`** — `pcre2_xclass.c` has no switch arm for either, so there is nothing to exercise there. They *are* covered in C049 (`PT_ANY` early return; `PT_CLIST` falls into the `default:`/PXXDIGIT arm).\n3. **C053 with `utf=FALSE` on UTF-compiled patterns** — not done. Walking UTF code with `utf=FALSE` desynchronises the scan (`\\x{e9}` → the 0xa9 continuation byte is read as an opcode) and walks outside the block; that is undefined in the C reference too. ASCII-only patterns are walked with **both** flags; UTF patterns with `utf=TRUE`.\n4. **C055 sizes below `sizeof(pcre2_memctl)`** — tested only via custom allocators that deliberately over-allocate. With `memctl == NULL` the C does `malloc(size)` then unconditionally writes 24 bytes, so `size < 24` is a heap overflow *in the C reference*; those sizes use `size >= 24` for the NULL path.\n5. **`_pcre2_compile_get_hash_from_name8` signature** — the harness `Api` declares it `fn(Sptr, usize) -> u32`, but the C prototype is `uint16_t f(PCRE2_SPTR, uint32_t)`. I reached it with `api.raw::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(Sptr, u32) -> u16>` to avoid a spurious upper-eax-garbage mismatch. Worth fixing in `tests/common/mod.rs` (I did not touch it).\n\n## Row-text corrections found while deriving constants (not divergences — both libraries agree)\n\n- **C001**: values are not only 1–5; `OP_lengths[OP_CLASS]` = `OP_lengths[OP_NCLASS]` = 33 (1 + 32-byte bitmap).\n- **C016**: the ranges are non-*decreasing*, not strictly ascending — e.g. `0x007a,0x00b5` is followed by `0x00b5,0x00c0` (`pcre2_ucd.c:164`). The test now reproduces `get_nocase_range()` (`pcre2_compile_class.c:126-146`) verbatim over both tables.\n- **C017**: `_pcre2_utt_size_8` is **518** (not 519) in both libraries (ELF size 0xc24 / 6). Also, no script *value* appears with both `PT_SC` and `PT_SCX`; the table has 150 `PT_SC` and 194 `PT_SCX` entries and the split is identical in both libraries.\n- **C008**: `pcre2_config(PCRE2_CONFIG_TABLES_LENGTH, where)` returns 0, not 4 (4 is only returned for a NULL `where`).\n- **C045**: a lone `[\\x{100}]` compiles to `OP_CHAR`, not `OP_XCLASS`; `[\\x{100}\\x{102}]` was used instead.","usage":{"total_tokens":288413,"tool_uses":93,"duration_ms":1814189},"uuid":"1175bf9a-8147-4e0a-8d46-c36a3cedf440","session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503"}
