{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01N41Tgk4DozUEGcP6ebaBSE","type":"tool_result","content":"C001\t_pcre2_OP_lengths_8\tnone (pure data)\tread all OP_TABLE_LENGTH=173 bytes, index 0..172\tper-opcode compiled size depends on LINK_SIZE=2 and IMM2_SIZE=2; values 1/2/3/4/5 and 0 placeholders for OP_XCLASS/OP_ECLASS/OP_CALLOUT_STR (pcre2_tables.c:67, OP_LENGTHS macro pcre2_internal.h:1977-2065)\nC158\tpcre2_dfa_match\toptions 0, mcontext NULL\tthe same argument-validation shapes as C126 and C127; plus workspace count 0, 19 (PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE), 20, 100, 1000; plus a pattern compiled with PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF (PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UINVALID_UTF)\twscount < 20 is rejected outright; PUBLIC_DFA_MATCH_OPTIONS accepts PCRE2_DFA_RESTART and PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST but has no PCRE2_DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK; PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF is rejected because the DFA has no fragment logic (pcre2_dfa_match.c:83-87,3395-3431)\nC159\tpcre2_dfa_match\tworkspace sized so the state vectors hold exactly n states\tpatterns with many simultaneous alternatives such as \"(a|b|c|d|e|f|g|h){20}\" and \"[a-z]{50}\" against a long subject, with a 20-int workspace and with a generous one\tall four state-adding macros return PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE when the active or new state count reaches wscount, which is derived as (wscount-2)/(2*INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK) (pcre2_dfa_match.c:490-525,570-581)\nC160\tpcre2_dfa_match\tPCRE2_DFA_RESTART on and off\ta first call on a truncated subject with PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT that leaves workspace state, then a restart call on the remainder with the same workspace; a restart call with workspace[0] having a bit other than bit 0 set; a restart call with workspace[1] equal to 0 and to (wscount-2)/INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK + 1 (both PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_BADRESTART); a restart call with a fresh zeroed workspace\tthe restart sanity check requires (workspace[0] & -2) == 0 and workspace[1] in range; restarting also forces anchored mode and skips the start optimizations (pcre2_dfa_match.c:668-675,3454-3468,3703-3709)\nC161\tpcre2_dfa_match\tPCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST on and off\tpatterns \"a+\", \"ab|abcd\", \"a*\", \"(?:ab)+\" on subjects with several possible match lengths\twith SHORTEST the scan returns as soon as the first final state is reached instead of continuing to look for longer matches (pcre2_dfa_match.c:891)\nC162\tpcre2_dfa_match\toptions 0, oveccount 0, 2, 4, 10\tpatterns with several matches at the same starting offset such as \"a|ab|abc\" and \"(?:a){1,3}\" on \"abc\"\tthe DFA prepends each newly found final state's pair into the ovector, shifting the previous ones up, so the ovector ends up longest-match-first; match_count is forced to 0 when the pairs overflow and offsetcount is rounded down to whole pairs (pcre2_dfa_match.c:568,857-892)\nC163\tpcre2_dfa_match\toptions 0\tpatterns containing items the DFA cannot handle: \"(a)\\\\1\" (OP_REF), \"(?i)(a)\\\\1\" (OP_REFI), \"(?J)(?<n>a)|(?<n>b)\\\\k<n>\" (OP_DNREF), \"a(*SKIP)b\", \"a(*SKIP:x)b\", \"a(*THEN)b\", \"a(*PRUNE)b\", \"a(*COMMIT)b\", \"a(*ACCEPT)b\", \"a(*MARK:x)b\", \"a\\\\Kb\" (OP_SET_SOM), \"(*sr:\\\\w+)\" (OP_SCRIPT_RUN), \"(*pla:a)b\" (OP_ASSERT_NA), \"(*plb:a)b\" (OP_ASSERTBACK_NA), \"(a)(*scs:(1)b)\" (OP_ASSERT_SCS), \"(?<=a|bb)c\" (OP_VREVERSE), \"\\\\C+\" (OP_ANYBYTE as a quantified type), \"(?1)(a)\" where the recursion has an argument list (OP_CREF after OP_RECURSE); also \"(*FAIL)\" which IS supported\tPCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UITEM comes from the quantified-\\\\C site, the recursion-with-arguments site and the switch default, so every unsupported opcode is a separate input shape (pcre2_dfa_match.c:825,2943,3259)\nC164\tpcre2_dfa_match\toptions 0\tconditional patterns the DFA cannot handle: \"(a)(?(1)b|c)\" (OP_CREF), \"(?<n>a)(?(<n>)b|c)\" (OP_DNCREF), \"(?<n>a)(?(R&n)b|c)\" (OP_DNRREF), \"(a)(?(R1)b|c)\" (OP_RREF with a specific number); and the one it can: \"(a)(?(R)b|c)\" (RREF_ANY)\tPCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UCOND is returned from two separate sites; only (?(R)) is supported (pcre2_dfa_match.c:2857,2877)\nC165\tpcre2_dfa_match\tpcre2_set_match_limit and pcre2_set_depth_limit at 0, 1, 2, small and default values; pcre2_set_heap_limit at 0, 1, small and default\tpatterns that force nested internal_dfa_match calls: \"(?=a)b\" and \"(?<=a)b\" (assertions), \"(?(?=a)b|c)\" (assertion conditions), \"\\\\((?:[^()]|(?R))*\\\\)\" (recursion), \"(?>a+)b\" (OP_ONCE), \"(a|b)++c\" (BRAPOS); on subjects deep enough to exhaust the base RWS block so more_workspace is called\tin the DFA the match limit counts internal_dfa_match calls (not characters) and is NOT reset per bumpalong, unlike the interpreter; more_workspace doubles the recursion workspace and returns PCRE2_ERROR_HEAPLIMIT or PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY (pcre2_dfa_match.c:421-455,566-567,3496-3536)\nC166\tpcre2_dfa_match\tPCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT and PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD, on and off, each with every newline convention\tthe same subject shapes as C142, plus a subject ending in a bare CR against \".\", \"$\", \"$\" with PCRE2_MULTILINE, \"\\\\Z\" and \"\\\\z\"; plus a pattern with a lookbehind (allowemptypartial); plus a pattern that can match empty\tcould_continue is set whenever an opcode wanted a character at clen==0; PARTIAL_HARD returns immediately at OP_EOD and OP_EODN, while the CRLF-lookahead case splits into a delayed state for HARD and a partial_newline flag for SOFT; the final decision combines could_continue, partial_newline, start_used_ptr and allowemptypartial (pcre2_dfa_match.c:764-801,963-1071,1290-1413,3274-3295)\nC167\tpcre2_dfa_match, pcre2_substring_length_bynumber, pcre2_substitute\toptions 0\tafter a successful DFA match, call pcre2_substring_copy_byname, pcre2_substring_get_byname, pcre2_substring_length_byname and pcre2_substitute with PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED on the same match_data\tmatch_data->matchedby is set to PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER, which makes those four entry points return PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UFUNC; pcre2_substring_length_bynumber instead takes a different (top_bracket-free) validation path (pcre2_dfa_match.c:3688, pcre2_substring.c:75,163,270,333-337, pcre2_substitute.c:850)\nC168\tpcre2_next_match\toptions and match_data from a preceding pcre2_match\tmatch_data whose rc is negative (NOMATCH, PARTIAL, an error) - must return FALSE with the outputs untouched; a non-empty match that made progress; an empty match not at the end of the subject (must return PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART at the same offset); an empty match exactly at the end of the subject (FALSE); a \\\\K-in-lookaround match where ovector[1] == start_offset but ovector[0] != start_offset, both mid-subject and at the end of the subject\tthe three-way classification (no progress, empty match, ordinary progress) plus the rc<0 short circuit are the whole function; only the no-progress case calls do_bumpalong (pcre2_match_next.c:96-169)\nC169\tpcre2_next_match\tthe code compiled with each of the six newline conventions; PCRE2_UTF on and off\ta no-progress or empty-match state whose bump point is: a CR immediately followed by LF (skipped atomically only under CRLF, ANY and ANYCRLF); a CR at the last unit; a multi-byte UTF character (advanced one whole character); an ill-formed UTF byte (FORWARDCHARTEST clamps to the subject end); an ordinary byte\tdo_bumpalong has three exits: +2 for an atomic CRLF, one full character in UTF mode, and +1 otherwise (pcre2_match_next.c:49-88)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_015QwkpUyFvJ7XA1rUHAaQD3","session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503","uuid":"5c43773d-ffe4-40c0-825f-b55fc6124a90","timestamp":"2026-09-08T19:21:27.988Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Tests for DFA and next_match rows"}
