ry EVERY key 0..=30 (including out-of-range keys and the gap) in both libraries, with\n  a real `where` buffer poison-filled beforehand (compare the return code AND all 8 bytes\n  written) and with `where == NULL`. For the pointer-valued keys (`PCRE2_INFO_NAMETABLE`,\n  `PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTBITMAP`) compare the POINTED-AT CONTENTS (name table = namecount ×\n  nameentrysize bytes; bitmap = 32 bytes), not the pointer values. Also query with a NULL\n  `code`.\n* `pcre2_callout_enumerate_8`: patterns with numeric callouts, string callouts, auto callouts\n  (`PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT`), no callouts, and callouts inside classes/verbs/lookarounds. Mirror\n  the `pcre2_callout_enumerate_block` layout from `c_src/include/pcre2.h` and compare EVERY\n  field of EVERY enumeration step between the two libraries, using a thread-local log (tests\n  run concurrently). Test the callback returning 0 and non-zero (which stops enumeration) and\n  assert the rc matches.\n* `pcre2_pattern_convert_8`: for each mode, drive a fixed-seed corpus of >= 3000 random\n  glob/POSIX pattern strings (random length 0..30 over an alphabet rich in\n  `* ? [ ] ^ - ! \\ / . { } ( ) | + $ ,` and letters/digits/high bytes/UTF-8 sequences) plus\n  the hand-picked shapes each row names. Compare: the return code, `*blength`, and the FULL\n  converted pattern bytes (and, when conversion succeeds, compile the converted pattern in\n  both libraries and compare `compile_probe` output). Also test with a caller-supplied\n  `buffer` (a non-NULL `*buffptr` with a `*blength` limit — read the C to learn that\n  convention) at sizes from 0 to len+4, and with `PCRE2_CONVERT_NO_UTF_CHECK` on invalid\n  UTF-8, and with every glob escape/separator value the setters accept. Free with the owning\n  library's `pcre2_converted_pattern_free_8`.\n* C200: for each free function, verify that a block allocated with a CUSTOM allocator\n  (installed through a general context) is released through the correct hidden-memctl path,\n  by counting allocations and frees in your own allocator callbacks and asserting the counts\n  agree between the two libraries (and that everything is freed). Cover\n  `pcre2_code_free_8`, `pcre2_match_data_free_8`, `pcre2_substring_free_8`,\n  `pcre2_substring_list_free_8`, `pcre2_serialize_free_8`,\n  `pcre2_converted_pattern_free_8`, `pcre2_maketables_free_8` and the four context frees,\n  plus passing NULL to every one of them (documented no-op).\n* C201–C202: call every JIT entry point in both libraries with valid and invalid arguments\n  (including `pcre2_jit_compile_8` with each `PCRE2_JIT_*` option bit and with undefined bits,\n  a NULL code, `pcre2_jit_match_8` on a non-JIT-compiled code, `pcre2_jit_stack_create_8` with\n  various sizes incl. 0 and mismatched min>max, `_pcre2_jit_get_target_8`'s returned string)\n  and compare return values / returned strings / NULL-ness exactly.\n\nCover EVERY id C190–C202. Then report per the brief."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6708,"cache_read_input_tokens":137448,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6708,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503","uuid":"13c5d601-4a02-4e2c-83dc-6607df92e2b3","timestamp":"2026-09-08T19:22:10.029Z"}
