_src/src/pcre2_auto_possess.c` and `translation/src/auto_possess.rs`), on blocks compiled with `PCRE2_NO_AUTO_POSSESS` (973 comparisons, **512 blocks rewritten**). `code_start`/`blocksize` read at offsets 80/72 and cross-checked against `PCRE2_INFO_SIZE`.\n* Through-compile coverage: every row's named shapes × 13 option combos (`NO_START_OPTIMIZE`, `NO_AUTO_POSSESS`, `NO_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR`, `UTF`, `UCP`, `CASELESS`, `MULTILINE`, `DOTALL`, `ANCHORED`, …) × 10 `pcre2_set_optimize` directive sequences, plus 200 fixed-seed random patterns per row, all compared with `compile_probe`.\n* C063's \"must NOT be possessified\" claim is asserted per-library on the **opcode stream only** (`re+code_start .. blocksize`), since the option bit itself lands in the header. Rewrite counts are printed as vacuity guards (C060 14/14, C061 16, C062 8, C064 40/40 cells fire; C063 zero).\n* Setters: every value `0..=300`, `u32::MAX`, `u32::MAX-1`, `0x8000_0000`, `0x10000` and 64 random u32s — return code, the stored context field, and a subsequent `compile_probe`/match are all compared. `pcre2_config`: keys `0..=20` + 100/1000/`u32::MAX` with a 512-byte 0xAA-sentinel buffer (all bytes compared, over-write checked) and with `where == NULL`. `pcre2_maketables`: all 1088 bytes vs each other and vs `_pcre2_default_tables_8`, with NULL and custom-allocator gcontext (alloc count/size checked), installed via `pcre2_set_character_tables` including a deliberately case-mangled table set that provably changes the compiled output.\n* Contexts are compared field-by-field as raw bytes against `_pcre2_default_*_context_8`, skipping only the per-library `memctl`/`tables` pointers; custom allocators are libc `malloc`/`free` wrappers (dlsym'd through the C `.so`) so they interoperate with the libraries' defaults, and malloc-call/byte accounting is compared between C and Rust.\n\n## 2. Command and result\n\n```\ncd translation && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-final timeout 900 \\\n  cargo test --offline --test configs_study_context -- --nocapture\n```\n**25 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored** (0.04 s).\n\n## 3. Divergences\n\n**No divergences.** Every comparison of return codes, output arguments, buffers, `PCRE2_SIZE` values, pattern_info scalars, start bitmaps, serialized images and directly-studied/possessified blocks was byte-identical.\n\nOne difference was found but is **outside the documented contract**, so it is excluded from comparison rather than reported as a bug (both libraries agree on the return code):\n* After a **failed** match (`rc < 0`, other than `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`) the ovector/startchar contents are documented undefined, and the two engines leave different scratch residue. Minimal repro: pattern `b\"(a+)*b\"`, options `0`, subject `b\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"`, match context with `pcre2_set_recursion_limit(mc, 0)` → both return `-1`, C ovector `[0,0,0,0]`, Rust `[0,0,0,160]`. Same shape with `^a$` + `PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY` on `b\"a\\n\"` (C `[1,0]`, Rust `[1,8]`). `cmp_match_out()` therefore compares `rc` + `mark` on failure and the full `MatchOut` on success/partial. Flagging it in case the caller wants the residue treated as in-scope.\n\nAlso worth noting (not divergences, C and Rust agree): in this build `PCRE2_CONFIG_BSR` = 1 (UNICODE) and `PCRE2_CONFIG_COMPILED_WIDTHS` = 0 — the C075 row text predicted 2 and 1 — so the test compares C vs Rust and prints the values instead of hard-coding the row's numbers.\n\n## 4. Not tested, and why\n\n* **`pcre2_*_context_copy(NULL)`** — `pcre2_context.c:231-277` dereferences the argument with no NULL check, so the call segfaults in the C ground truth; there is nothing comparable. Only `*_context_free(NULL)` (an explicit no-op) is tested.\n* **C076's \"buffer one byte smaller\"** for the string keys — `pcre2_config` takes no size argument, so a short buffer is a genuine overflow in both libraries. Instead the string is written into a 0xAA-sentinel 256-byte region and *every* byte written (plus the exact `1+strlen`