ontent + offset-from-code. Callback returns 0 and non-zero (`1, -1, 42, -48, i32::MIN, i32::MAX`) at **every** step index, asserting the rc propagates and enumeration stops. Plus `code == NULL`, BADMAGIC, BADMODE. |\n| `c193_convert_mode_legality` | C193 | all 267 option values (0..=0xFF + high/undefined bits) × 6 patterns; `pattern == NULL` with plength 0/1/5/ZERO_TERMINATED; `bufflenptr == NULL` (with `buffptr` NULL and non-NULL); `ccontext` NULL and non-NULL; all three buffer shapes. |\n| `c194_convert_utf` | C194 | 23 UTF shapes (valid + every ill-formed class: isolated continuation, truncated 2/3/4-byte, overlong, surrogate, >10FFFF, 5-byte, 0xFE/0xFF) × 3 modes × 3 separators × `{0, UTF, NO_UTF_CHECK, UTF|NO_UTF_CHECK}` + 3000 random. **30 706** `pcre2_pattern_convert` calls/library. |\n| `c195_convert_posix_basic` | C195 | the row's 76 hand-picked shapes × `{BASIC, BASIC|0x20, BASIC|0x40, BASIC|0x60}` + 3000 random; also shows `BASIC|GLOB_NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` / `|GLOB_NO_STARSTAR` are **two type bits ⇒ BADOPTION** (they are not \"silently ignored\" — the 0x20/0x40 halves alone are). **19 261** calls/library. |\n| `c196_convert_posix_extended` | C196 | same 76 shapes + the extended-specific extras + 3000 random. **14 839** calls/library. |\n| `c197_convert_glob_stars` | C197 | 57 star/question shapes × 3 separators × escapes `{0,'\\\\','`','*'}` + 3000 random over 18 sep/escape contexts. **31 054** calls/library. |\n| `c198_convert_glob_classes` | C198 | setter acceptance for escape `0..=300` (33 accepted: 0 + 32 `globpunct` chars) and separator `0..=300` (exactly `. / \\`); 61 class shapes incl. all 14 POSIX class names, `[z-a]`/`[9-0]`/`[a-[:digit:]]` syntax errors, separator-spanning ranges, over **every accepted escape × every accepted separator**; + 3000 class-heavy random. **42 874** calls/library. |\n| `c199_convert_glob_composites` | C199 | `GLOB` vs `GLOB_NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` vs `GLOB_NO_STARSTAR` vs both, over the C197+C198 corpora × 3 seps × 4 escapes + 3000 random. **35 363** calls/library. |\n| `c200_free_family_memctl` | C200 | custom counting allocator installed through a general context; every allocating API and its matching free, all four context creates/copies/frees, `maketables`/`maketables_free`, match_data with and without heapframes and with `PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT`, `substring_get`/`substring_list_get` (with and without lengths), `serialize_encode`/`decode`/`free`, `code_copy` (no `DEREF_TABLES`) and `code_copy_with_tables` + decoded code (`DEREF_TABLES`), `pattern_convert`/`converted_pattern_free`. NULL passed to all eleven free functions incl. `maketables_free(gcontext, NULL)` (which does reach the custom `free(NULL)`). Asserts alloc==free, zero leaks, no free of an un-allocated pointer, and that the **full allocation/free/free(NULL) counts and the ordered list of requested sizes are identical between the two libraries** (26/26/3 for two patterns, 28/28/3 for the 1760-byte 31-group pattern). Also repeated with the default allocator. |\n| `c201_jit_public_stubs` | C201 | `pcre2_jit_compile` over 22 option values (each `PCRE2_JIT_*` bit, combinations, `TEST_ALLOC` alone and combined, undefined bits, `0xFFFFFFFF`) × 6 patterns, and with `code == NULL`; **verifies the documented no-JIT side effect** that `PCRE2_JIT_INVALID_UTF` still ORs `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` into `overall_options` (checked through `PCRE2_INFO_ALLOPTIONS`) and that nothing else in the block changes; `pcre2_jit_match` on non-JIT code at 7 offset/option shapes, comparing rc, the stored `match_data->rc` (read back through `pcre2_substring_length_bynumber`), and the untouched ovector/startchar/mark; `pcre2_jit_stack_create` at 9 size pairs incl. `(0,0)`, `min>max`, `SIZE_MAX`, gcontext NULL/non-NULL; `jit_stack_assign` NULL/non-NULL mcontext and callback with a before/after byte snapshot of the match context; `jit_stack_free`/`jit_free_unused_memory` NULL and non-NULL; `PCRE2_CONFIG_JIT == 0` and `PCRE2_CONFIG_JITTARGET == PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION`. |\n| `c202_jit_priv_stubs` | C202 | `_pcre2_jit_get_target_8` (NULL-ness + full string, asserted `\"JIT is not supported\"`, stable across calls), `_pcre2_jit_get_size_8` on NULL/blob/1/`SIZE_MAX` (== 0), `_pcre2_jit_free_8` and `_pcre2_jit_free_rodata_8` with NULL and with a real code block + its head memctl, then asserting all 31 info keys are unchanged and the block is still freeable. |\n\n## 2. Command and results\n\n```\ncd translation && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-c190 timeout 900 \\\n  cargo test --offline --test configs_info_convert -- --nocapture\n```\n`test result: ok. 13 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out` (runs in ~0.05 s; ~175 000 `pcre2_pattern_convert` calls, ~50 000 `pcre2_pattern_info` calls per library, 0 compiler warnings).\n\n## 3. Divergences\n\n**No divergences.** Every compared value (return codes, `*bufflenptr`, full converted-pattern bytes, whole caller-supplied buffers including 16 guard bytes, every `pcre2_callout_enumerate_block` field, all 31 info keys with both `where` shapes, allocator traffic, and the JIT stub returns/strings) was identical between `c_src/build/libpcre2.so` and `translation/target/release/libpcre2.so`.\n\n## 4. What I could not test, and why\n\n* **`PCRE2_CONVERT_UTF | PCRE2_CONVERT_NO_UTF_CHECK` on *truncated* ill-formed UTF-8 at the very end of the pattern.** `GETCHARLENTEST`/`GETCHARINCTEST` trust `PRIV(utf8_table4)` (up to 5 extra code units) and `convert_posix` then does `plength -= clength`, so a lead byte fewer than its declared length from the end makes the **C itself** read out of bounds and underflow `plength` into an unbounded loop — I reproduced a SIGSEGV in the C library doing exactly this. Since the C is ground truth only where it is defined, that combination is driven with inputs padded by 8 trailing ASCII bytes (`pad_utf`), which keeps the over-read inside the buffer while still letting the ill-formed bytes reach the macros. All ill-formed shapes *are* tested unpadded with `utf == FALSE` and with the UTF check on.\n* **A non-ASCII glob separator/escape** (the `separator >= 128 || escape >= 128` early return at `pcre2_convert.c:868`) is unreachable through the public API: `pcre2_set_glob_separator` accepts only `. / \\` and `pcre2_set_glob_escape` only `0` plus ASCII `globpunct`. I verified the setters reject everything else identically instead.\n* **`PCRE2_INFO_CAPTURECOUNT == 65535`** is not in the pool (the row names it); a 65 535-group pattern takes prohibitively long to compile for a 900 s budget. Counts 0, 1, 8, 64 and 300 are covered.\n* **`pcre2_jit_match` with a NULL `match_data`** is untestable: the no-JIT stub does `return match_data->rc = PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION` (`pcre2_jit_match_inc.h:103`), i.e. it unconditionally dereferences it, so NULL is undefined in the C too."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":641,"cache_read_input_tokens":211423,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":641,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013qZpUC2GEF1G9qxZU9u1vo","session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503","uuid":"af36545b-4fb6-4377-ab24-39877d94767b","timestamp":"2026-09-08T19:41:38.632Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Tests for info/convert/free/jit rows"}
