{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_q7qvmnrztxeps75cdkr7tux6kdsjmff2uciei675bdtboonpr7pq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Final state:\n\n## File written\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wwiWoN/translation/tests/errors_runtime.rs` (4120 lines, 62 `#[test]`s — 43 written out + 19 generated by a `setter_test!` macro).\n\n## Coverage — all 267 reachable rows, grouped by public function\nOne `#[test]` per public function (56 functions), each printing `row <n> <function> <expected>` per row. Row lists are `const R_*: &[usize]` and every test asserts it executed exactly its list:\n`pcre2_match_8`(45: 63–107), `pcre2_substitute_8`(44: 209–252), `pcre2_dfa_match_8`(31: 14–44), `pcre2_pattern_convert_8`(18: 126–143), `pcre2_serialize_decode_8`(13), `pcre2_pattern_info_8`(9), `pcre2_substring_length_bynumber_8`(7), `pcre2_serialize_encode_8`(8), `pcre2_get_error_message_8`(6), `pcre2_callout_enumerate_8`/`pcre2_jit_compile_8`(5 each), plus the 4-, 3-, 2- and 1-row functions (config, serialize_get_number_of_codes, substring_*, match_data_create*, next_match, all context create/copy, jit_match, jit_stack_create, maketables, set_bsr/newline/glob_*/optimize and the 16 never-rejecting setters).\n\nDesign notes:\n- Recipes are ports of `_v/checkrt.c`, executed as one `probe(&Api)` per function, run once per library, then compared row-by-row. Each row asserts (a) C == the TSV's tabulated value, (b) Rust == C, including every output argument: ovector (pre-filled with a sentinel so untouched slots are distinguishable), `*outlengthptr` and the whole 1 KiB output buffer for `pcre2_substitute_8`, `*blengthptr`/`*bufferptr`/buffer for `pcre2_pattern_convert_8`, `*where` for `pattern_info`/`config`, the 256-byte message buffer for `get_error_message`, `startoffset`/`options` for `next_match`, sizes/pointers/buffers for all `substring_*`.\n- The TSV is `include_str!`d and parsed at runtime, so the expected value, `c_file:line`, trigger, recipe and UNREACHABLE marking in every assertion message come straight from the table (no transcription drift).\n- Rust counting allocator (`cmalloc`/`cfree`, thread-local budget, 16-byte size header) installed via `pcre2_general_context_create_8` for the 14 NOMEMORY rows; every library-allocated object is freed by that same library's free function.\n- Out-of-range enums are passed as raw ints (`set_optimize` 2/63/70, `config`/`pattern_info` key 999, `set_newline` 0/7, `set_bsr` 0/3, `jit_compile` 0x80000000, undefined convert/match option bits).\n- Corroborating non-row assertions (as in checkrt.c) also compared C-vs-Rust: `heapframes_size == 20480` after both `pcre2_match.c:778`/`:791` HEAPLIMIT rows, `*blength == 11` for the OVERFLOW_LENGTH row, `serialize_encode == 1` for the good stream.\n- `rt_row_accounting` asserts: 300 rows parsed, 267 reachable, 33 unreachable, per-function lists identical to the TSV grouping, and 267 executed rows == exactly the reachable set. `rt_unreachable_rows_skipped` prints all 33 skipped rows with their reason from the notes field.\n\n## Beyond the table\n- `bd_null_pointers_and_documented_null_checks` — 78 cases: every documented NULL check (compile pattern/errorcode/erroroffset, code_copy(_with_tables), match/dfa/substitute NULL subject+replacement with 0 and non-0 length, dfa NULL workspace, `pattern_info(where=NULL)` size path for keys 0..27, `config(where=NULL)` length path for keys 0..20 + 999, serialize NULL/negative counts, `set_optimize(NULL)`, jit stubs, all 10 `*_free(NULL)` no-ops, `maketables(NULL)` full table image).\n- `bd_zero_and_oversized_lengths_and_offsets` — 1220 cases: lengths 0/1/3/4/64/`PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED`, `start_offset == length`, `length+1`, `length+2`, ovector counts 0..3, DFA `wscount` 0/1/19/20/21, substitute buffer caps 0..64 around the required length.\n- `bd_one_step_past_each_documented_range` — 1226 cases: `set_bsr`/`set_newline` 0..8, `set_optimize` {0,1,2,3,62,63,64,70,~0}, glob escape/separator sets, ovector 65534/65535/65536/70000/~0, jit option bit combos, `get_error_message` for every code −80..200 × sizes {0,1,4,64}.\n- `rand_runtime_error_surface` — 6300 fixed-seed random cases (15 patterns × 140 iterations × match/dfa/substitute) with random subjects, lengths, offsets, option masks (incl. illegal bits), ovector counts, workspace sizes and replacements.\n\n## Result\nCommand: `cd translation && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-rt cargo test --offline --test errors_runtime -- --nocapture`\n→ `test result: ok. 62 passed; 0 failed` (also verified with `--test-threads=1`). No compiler warnings.\n\n- **No divergences.** The Rust library matched the C library on all 267 rows (return code and every output argument), on all 2524 boundary cases and on all 6300 random cases.\n- **No stale table rows:** every one of the 267 C-library results equalled its tabulated expectation, so no row numbers to report.\n\n## Not tested / caveats\n- The 33 UNREACHABLE rows (45, 46, 108–115, 144–147, 253–256, 280, 287–300) are counted and printed with their notes, not triggered.\n- For match/dfa rows I compare the ovector but not `match_data->startchar` or `mark`: `pcre2_match_data_create` leaves those fields uninitialised, so reading them on early-error paths would compare uninitialised heap (and dereferencing `mark` would be UB).\n- I do not compare the DFA `workspace` array contents (documented scratch, not an output argument); the DFA's observable outputs (rc, ovector) are compared."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":174,"cache_read_input_tokens":234784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":174,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01KoDqKQoFkTKgmHT8MAq4VS","session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503","uuid":"7f8e124a-570e-4363-872b-9ff47e134158","timestamp":"2026-09-08T19:44:31.163Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Port runtime error recipes to Rust"}
