{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5oeo4o343wj4pvwm5xtdqu52ozfso4zmy42i5xahyx35ailjiqaa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_019pov4HGZ8dmNfXQaYbojUc","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit unchecked table indexing","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wwiWoN . The C in `c_src/` is the ground truth and must NEVER be modified. You MAY modify `translation/src/**`. Do NOT modify `translation/SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, or anything in `translation/tests/`.\n\nCONTEXT — a real defect class was just found and fixed in ONE place; your job is to find and fix\nthe REST of the same class.\n\nThe bug class: the C indexes its static tables with NO bounds check, so an out-of-range index\nsilently reads adjacent static data and the function returns a value. The Rust translation\nsometimes uses bounds-checked SLICE INDEXING (`TABLE[i]`) for the same lookup, which PANICS —\nand because `[profile.release]` has `panic = \"abort\"`, the whole process dies with SIGABRT\nwhere the C would have returned normally. That is a hard behavioural divergence.\n\nThe instance already fixed (use it as the model): `GET_UCD!` in `translation/src/macros.rs`\nused `_pcre2_ucd_stage1_8[(ch as usize)/UCD_BLOCK_SIZE]`. Reached from `PRIV(extuni)` with a\ncode point above MAX_UTF_CODE_POINT (`GETCHARLEN` on a 5- or 6-byte UTF-8 lead byte yields\nc > 0x10FFFF, and in the 8-bit build `GET_UCD` has no MAX_UTF_CODE_POINT guard — that arm is\n`#if PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH == 32` only, `c_src/src/pcre2_internal.h:2123-2131`). Reproducer:\npattern `b\"\\\\X\"` + `PCRE2_UTF`, subject `b\"a\\xf8\\x88\\x80\\x80\\x80\"`, match option\n`PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` → C returns rc=1, Rust panicked at `src/extuni.rs:47`\n(\"len is 8704 but the index is 16384\"). It is now fixed by using raw pointer arithmetic with\nC's `(int)` cast semantics (read the current `GET_UCD!` body in `translation/src/macros.rs`\nbefore you start — copy its style, including the `i32` division/modulo).\n\nYOUR TASK:\n1. Enumerate EVERY place in `translation/src/**` where a `static` table (or any fixed-size\n   array) is indexed with `[...]` by a value that can be derived from INPUT DATA — a code\n   point, code unit, opcode byte, character type, script number, property number, group\n   number, an offset read out of a compiled pattern, a bracket count, etc. Useful starting\n   greps (make your own too):\n     grep -rn \"_pcre2_ucd_stage1_8\\[\\|_pcre2_ucd_stage2_8\\[\\|_pcre2_ucd_records_8\\[\" translation/src/\n     grep -rn \"_pcre2_ucp_gentype_8\\[\\|_pcre2_ucp_gbtable_8\\[\\|_pcre2_utt_8\\[\\|_pcre2_utt_names_8\\[\" translation/src/\n     grep -rn \"_pcre2_utf8_table1\\|_pcre2_utf8_table2\\|_pcre2_utf8_table3\\|_pcre2_utf8_table4\" translation/src/\n     grep -rn \"_pcre2_OP_lengths_8\\[\\|_pcre2_hspace_list_8\\[\\|_pcre2_vspace_list_8\\[\" translation/src/\n     grep -rn \"_pcre2_ucd_caseless_sets_8\\[\\|_pcre2_ucd_digit_sets_8\\[\\|_pcre2_ucd_script_sets_8\\[\\|_pcre2_ucd_boolprop_sets_8\\[\\|_pcre2_ucd_nocase_ranges_8\\[\" translation/src/\n     grep -rn \"_pcre2_posix_class_maps8\\[\\|_pcre2_callout_start_delims_8\\[\\|_pcre2_callout_end_delims_8\\[\\|_pcre2_default_tables_8\\[\" translation/src/\n     grep -rn \"autoposstab\\|posspropstab\\|catposstab\\|coptable\\|poptable\\|opcode_possessify\" translation/src/\n   Then, for EACH site, read the corresponding C expression and decide: can the index exceed\n   the table length for SOME input the C accepts? Judge it from the C, not from intuition —\n   in particular remember that with `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK`, or via `PRIV(extuni)`/`\\X`,\n   `PRIV(script_run)`, `PRIV(xclass)`, `PRIV(eclass)`, `_pcre2_ord2utf`, the case-folding\n   tables and the auto-possessification tables, values ABOVE 0x10FFFF and malformed UTF-8\n   sequences do reach these lookups.\n2. For every site that CAN go out of range, replace the slice indexing with UNCHECKED raw\n   pointer arithmetic that reproduces the C exactly — same integer widths, same signedness,\n   same division/modulo semantics as the C expression (`(int)` casts in C mean `i32`\n   arithmetic). Where the C would read a table with a signed/negative index, reproduce that\n   too. Add a short comment at each site saying which C line it mirrors and why the check\n   must not be there.\n3. Do not change any observable value for in-range inputs. Do not add bounds checks, do not\n   clamp, do not return early, do not \"fix\" the C's behaviour.\n4. Rebuild after your changes: `cd translation && cargo build --release --offline` (the\n   crates.io network is BLOCKED, always use `--offline`). Then sanity-run the existing\n   differential test suite, which loads both `.so`s:\n     cd translation && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-audit timeout 880 \\\n       cargo test --offline --release --test fuzz_crosscheck --test configs_tables_leaf 2>&1 | tail -20\n   Both must stay green (they were green before your change).\n5. Also write yourself a scratch reproducer (put scratch files in `_v/`, NOT in\n   `translation/tests/`) for at least two of the sites you fix, showing that BEFORE the fix\n   the Rust aborted and AFTER it returns the same value as the C .so. Report the exact inputs.\n\nREPORT: a table of every site you inspected (file:line, table, index expression, C source\nline, verdict \"can overflow / provably in range\"), what you changed, the reproducers and their\nbefore/after results, and confirmation that the two test files above still pass."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":419,"cache_read_input_tokens":217090,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":419,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503","uuid":"423db619-4175-4acf-8c2a-bbdefcd6a56b","timestamp":"2026-09-08T19:47:08.466Z"}
