{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_opnyauaznr3efqxg2bl2masnwadf2pkasxpqb7yuly5kghp6l64a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 14 tests pass against the current `.so` pair. Final report:\n\n## 1. File and coverage\n\n**Wrote exactly one file:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wwiWoN/translation/tests/configs_dfa.rs` (2448 lines, 14 `#[test]`s). No other file was touched.\n\n| id | test fn |\n|---|---|\n| C158 | `c158_dfa_argument_validation` |\n| C159 | `c159_workspace_threshold` |\n| C160 | `c160_dfa_restart` |\n| C161 | `c161_dfa_shortest` |\n| C162 | `c162_ovector_semantics` |\n| C163 | `c163_unsupported_items` |\n| C164 | `c164_unsupported_conditions` |\n| C165 | `c165_dfa_limits` |\n| C166 | `c166_partial_matching` |\n| C167 | `c167_dfa_ufunc` |\n| C168 | `c168_next_match_classification` |\n| C169 | `c169_next_match_bumpalong` |\n| C158–C166 | `c158_c166_random_sweep` (fixed seed, 400 000 iterations) |\n| C168–C169 | `c168_c169_random_sweep` (fixed seed, 120 000 iterations) |\n\nEvery comparison is C-`.so` vs Rust-`.so`: `read_match` (rc + **full** ovector + `startchar` + `mark`) **plus the entire `int` workspace** after each `pcre2_dfa_match_8` call, plus (for C163) the full public `pcre2_callout_block` trace, and (for C168/C169) the entire *sequence* of `(rc, ovector, startchar, mark, next_match rc, *offset, *options)` tuples until the loop terminates.\n\nTwo harness decisions worth knowing:\n* Both match-data blocks are allocated through a **zeroing allocator** installed via `pcre2_general_context_create_8`, because `pcre2_match_data_create` leaves `startchar`/`rc`/`subject_length` indeterminate — otherwise the early-error return paths compare garbage.\n* Every ovector is pre-filled with `0x5A5A…` so \"slot the DFA never wrote\" is itself compared.\n* Workspaces are allocated `2*wscount+64` ints and the *whole* buffer is compared, which also asserts neither library writes past `wscount`.\n* Subjects are padded with 8 extra defined bytes because `GETCHARLENTEST` (pcre2_intmodedep.h:342) is not bound-checked.\n\n## 2. Command and results\n\n```\ncd translation && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-dfa timeout 880 \\\n  cargo test --offline --test configs_dfa -- --nocapture\n```\n\n`test result: ok. 14 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored` in 1.53 s.\n**≈ 639 000 C-vs-Rust comparisons** (C158 1337, C159 4095, C160 2147, C161 25746, C162 3038, C163 2253, C164 280, C165 540, C166 36918, C167 231, C168 18315, C169 2450, random sweeps 420134 + 121568). The random sweep's rc histogram covers 40 distinct return codes including `-1, -2, 0, 1..10, -22/-23` (UTF errors), `-33, -34, -36, -38, -43, -47, -53, -56`.\n\nCoverage the tests self-assert (they fail if the site is not reached): ≥40 `DFA_UITEM`, 53 `DFA_UCOND`, `DFA_RECURSE` reached, `NOMEMORY` from `more_workspace` in 3/12 patterns, and all three `do_bumpalong` exits (atomic CRLF 36, UTF-character 126, +1 342). C159 independently computes the smallest working `wscount` in each library and asserts the two numbers are equal — the thresholds genuinely differ per pattern (20 / 32 / 38 / 68 / 530 …), so this is a real signal.\n\n## 3. Divergences\n\n**No divergences.** Every assertion passed.\n\n## 4. What could not be tested, and why (both are C undefined behaviour, not translation gaps)\n\n1. **`PCRE2_UTF` + `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` + an ill-formed subject.** The brief asked for invalid UTF-8 combined with `NO_UTF_CHECK`; that input crashes the **C** library. `GETCHARLENTEST` builds a code point of up to `0x7FFFFFFF` out of a 5/6-byte ill-formed sequence and 8-bit-mode `GET_UCD` has no `> MAX_UTF_CODE_POINT` guard, so `ucd_stage1` (8704 entries) is indexed out of bounds. Minimal C repro (linked straight against `c_src/build/libpcre2.so`, **exit 139 / SIGSEGV**):\n   ```c\n   code = pcre2_compile(\"\\\\w+\\\\s\\\\w+\", ZERO_TERMINATED, PCRE2_UTF|PCRE2_UCP|PCRE2_CASELESS, ...);\n   unsigned char s[] = {0xfa,0xbf,0xbf,0xbf,0xbf,0x20,0x61,0x62};\n   pcre2_dfa_match(code, s, 8, 0, PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK, md, NULL, ws, 50);\n   ```\n   The Rust aborts with `index out of bounds: the len is 8704 but the index is 376027` at `translation/src/dfa_internal.rs:1357` (`PROP_TEST!`). Since the C has no defined behaviour here I excluded it: when the compile options contain `PCRE2_UTF` and the subject is not valid UTF-8, the sweep leaves the validity check ON and forces `start_offset = 0`, so the whole subject is validated and both libraries return a well-defined `PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_*`. Ill-formed UTF *is* still exercised with `NO_UTF_CHECK` in C169 (truncated/stray-continuation bytes at the bumpalong point, where nothing decodes them).\n\n2. **Crafted `PCRE2_DFA_RESTART` data with `(wscount-2)/6 < workspace[1] <= (wscount-2)/3`.** These values pass the restart sanity check at `pcre2_dfa_match.c:3456-3458` (which uses `INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK`) but the `memcpy(new_states, active_states, new_count * sizeof(stateblock))` at `:672` then writes past `wscount` (that code uses `2 * INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK` state slots per vector). My first version of C160 hit this and corrupted the heap (`malloc(): unaligned tcache chunk detected`). The crafted `workspace[1]` values are therefore restricted to `{-1, 0, 1, 2, (wscount-2)/6, maxst+1, maxst+100}`; the accepted-but-overflowing band is skipped and documented in a comment at that spot. Everything else about restart (real two-stage partial→restart including byte-exact workspace contents, incremental one-unit-at-a-time feeds, `workspace[0]` bit patterns, out-of-range `workspace[1]`, fresh zeroed workspace, and cross-pattern restart data → `-42`) is covered.\n\n3. `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMODE`/`BADMAGIC` are produced with a synthetic 4096-byte zeroed `pcre2_real_code` block, patching `magic_number@88`, `overall_options@96`, `flags@104` (offsets verified with `offsetof` against the real headers). Both libraries are handed the identical bytes, so this also cross-checks that 