{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_giejtej2sjtp6irtmq7b4tbtxocasdlsbdd6r4pqxyf7bofjp4nq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01TfEkdjgeHxJiUtTakktqsQ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wwiWoN/translation/src/match_engine.rs","old_string":"/* ---- Values and tables from the head of pcre2_match.c ---- */\n\npub const RECURSE_UNSET: u32 = 0xffffffffu32;","new_string":"/* ---- Values and tables from the head of pcre2_match.c ---- */\n\n/* PRIV(ucp_gentype)[i] and PRIV(ucp_gbtable)[i] - unchecked table lookups.\nThe C indexes these tables (30 and 15 entries) with a byte taken straight out of a\nucd_record obtained from GET_UCD(c). In the 8-bit library GET_UCD has no\nMAX_UTF_CODE_POINT guard (pcre2_internal.h:2123-2131 makes that arm 32-bit only), so\nwhen the subject is scanned with PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK a malformed 5- or 6-byte UTF-8\nsequence produces c > 0x10FFFF, GET_UCD reads past its own tables and the chartype /\ngbprop bytes can be any value 0..255. The C performs the lookup anyway, reads adjacent\nstatic data and returns normally; slice indexing would panic and (panic = \"abort\") kill\nthe process. Hence raw, unchecked pointer arithmetic - do not add a bounds check.\nThese mirror the helper already used in xclass.rs. */\n#[inline]\nunsafe fn ucp_gentype(i: i32) -> u32 {\n    *crate::tables::_pcre2_ucp_gentype_8.as_ptr().add(i as usize)\n}\n\n#[inline]\nunsafe fn ucp_gbtable(i: i32) -> u32 {\n    *crate::tables::_pcre2_ucp_gbtable_8.as_ptr().add(i as usize)\n}\n\npub const RECURSE_UNSET: u32 = 0xffffffffu32;"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1861,"cache_read_input_tokens":95757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1861,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},