{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jxixjc5shnwkjko47x3p6bdolpfswfvpcplleingpovpnldad7ya","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Final state: `translation/tests/configs_compile.rs`, 48/48 tests green.\n\n## 1. File and coverage\n**Wrote one file:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wwiWoN/translation/tests/configs_compile.rs` (4520 lines).\n\nOne `#[test]` per row, named `cNNN_*`, printing its row id — **all 48 assigned ids present exactly once**: C078 C079 C080 C081 C082 C083 C084 C085 C086 C087 C088 C089 C090 C091 C092 C093 C094 C095 C096 C097 C098 C099 C100 C101 C102 C103 C104 C105 C106 C107 C108 C109 C110 C111 C112 C113 C114 C115 C116 C117 C118 C119 C120 C121 C122 C123 C124 C125.\n\nEvery case compares `api.compile_probe` output (errorcode, erroroffset, all 25 scalar `pattern_info` keys, name table, start bitmap, byte-exact serialized image) between the two `.so`s; a `describe()` helper reports *which* field diverged (field name, or first differing image byte with 24-byte context). Divergences are accumulated per kind (count + first example) so one run reports all of them instead of stopping at the first.\n\nAlso included: the fixed-seed random pattern generator (token pool exactly as briefed: literals incl. ≥0x80/invalid UTF-8, all `\\d..\\Q\\E` escapes, `\\p`/`\\P`, classes, all group/assertion openers incl. `(*scs:(1)`, all quantifiers incl. `{1,65535}`, backrefs, recursion, conditionals, verbs, callouts, inline options, `\\x{} \\o{} \\N{U+} \\c@ \\e \\a \\f \\v0 \\777`), driven per row with the row's option bits forced on/off and all other compile options + extra options + newline (1..6) + BSR randomized, 1/8 of them zero-terminated. Default 200 000 patterns/group (`FUZZ_N` overrides; `FUZZ_N=4000` = the brief's minimum). Failing compiles are kept and compared (errorcode + erroroffset): 40–74 distinct compile error codes per row.\n\nTwo structural things worth knowing:\n* **Per-row process isolation** (`isolate!(\"Cxxx\")`): a Rust panic in the cdylib unwinds out of `extern \"C\"` and aborts the process, which would hide all other rows. Each row body runs in a child copy of the test binary; a crashing row fails loudly with its output forwarded. No check is relaxed. `PCRE2_TRACE=1` prints every probe before running it (used to bisect the crash below).\n* **Self-check** in C078 asserts the probe is not vacuous (image > 1100 bytes, all info keys present) and that `describe()` detects/localizes a single flipped image byte and a flipped info value. I also verified positively that an injected option difference is caught and pinpointed.\n\n## 2. Command and results\n```\ncd translation && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-final timeout 890 \\\n  cargo test --offline --test configs_compile -- --nocapture\n```\n`test result: ok. 48 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored` — 2.2 s wall on 48 cores (39.6 s with `--test-threads=1`), **6 911 351 differential comparisons** per run. Additional hunting runs: `FUZZ_N=600000` (6.5 s) and `FUZZ_N=6000000` (58 s, ≈220 M comparisons) — also all green.\n\n## 3. Divergences\n**No divergences.** Every compared field (errorcode, erroroffset, all `pattern_info` scalars, name tables, start bitmaps, full serialized compiled images, `maketables` output, match-data sizes/counts/ovector offsets, recursion-guard depth sequences) is identical between C and Rust for all ~7 M cases per run, and for ~220 M in the extended run.\n\nOne **undefined-behaviour input** must be flagged (not a translation bug, so it is excluded from the comparison, with the reason documented in the file at `utf_safe_opts`):\n* `pcre2_compile_8(b\"\\xff\\xfe\", 2, 0xe689010c /* LITERAL|UTF|NO_UTF_CHECK|CASELESS|AUTO_CALLOUT|FIRSTLINE|NO_START_OPTIMIZE|USE_OFFSET_LIMIT|MATCH_INVALID_UTF|ANCHORED|ENDANCHORED */, &ec, &eo, NULL)`\n  Rust: SIGSEGV, or `panicked at src/compile_branch.rs:2696: index out of bounds: the len is 8704 but the index is 13817` (index varies: 16515496, 16515626 …). C: **also non-deterministic** — observed both a clean return and SIGSEGV (exit 139) for the same call in different processes.\n  Cause: `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` with a pattern that is not valid UTF is documented UB; the caseless path then evaluates `UCD_CASESET(meta)` = `ucd_stage1[meta/128]` (`pcre2_compile.c:8429`, `UCD_CASESET` `pcre2_internal.h:2146`) on a garbage code point > 0x10FFFF — an out-of-bounds read that C performs silently and Rust bounds-checks. There is no C ground truth here, so `utf_safe_opts()` drops `NO_UTF_CHECK` **only** when the pattern is not valid UTF-8 and UTF/MATCH_INVALID_UTF is set; all invalid-UTF shapes stay in the suite with the validity check enabled, and `NO_UTF_CHECK` is still exercised on valid-UTF patterns.\n\n## 4. Not testable, and why\n* **ERR97 / >65535 captures (C108), 10000+ names (C089/C109), 65535-capture patterns (C125), a group body >65535 code units (C107):** unreachable in this build — every capture/name costs code units, so `MAX_PATTERN_SIZE = 65536` (ERR20) or the parse-time name-count check fires first. I still drive 0/1/2/63/64/65/100/1000/8000/65535/65536 groups and 9999/10000/10001 names and assert both libraries produce the *same* error; the LINK_SIZE=2 offsets are pushed to within a few code units of the cap instead.\n* **Pre-match `startchar`/`mark` and the ovector tail (C124/C125):** `pcre2_match_data_create` leaves them uninitialised (`pcre2_match_data.c:53-68`), and `pcre2_dfa_match` leaves `startchar` uninitialised on NOMATCH, so those bytes are deliberately not compared (`MState`/`md_out` document exactly which parts are defined). Everything defined — `rc`, the defined ovector slots, `mark`, `startchar` after `pcre2_match`, sizes, counts, `heapframes_size`, and `offsetof(ovector)` — is compared.\n* **C124 \"general context whose malloc returns NULL\":** `pcre2_general_context_create` allocates the context with the supplied malloc, so a malloc that fails from the start cannot produce a context. Implemented with an allocator that works until both contexts exist, then fails (`FAIL_MALLOC`); both libraries then return NULL from `match_data_create` for every ovecsize.\n* JIT-related keys are inert in this build (no `SUPPORT_JIT`); `PCRE2_INFO_JITSIZE` is compared but always 0."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":391,"cache_read_input_tokens":273194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":391,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01M8g96MGKaRbRoXDS1vhSZJ","session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503","uuid":"24249ca8-af97-43e1-8110-b8a0d9e18644","timestamp":"2026-09-08T19:55:56.844Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Tests for compile option rows"}
