{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ecrfieittqpbhwn3ftq76nnxou26h3exuzjobkx4t5krc3rbj3qq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here is the audit and the fix.\n\n## Audit: every static / fixed-size-array index site in `translation/src/**`\n\nI enumerated the statics (`grep -rn '^\\s*\\(pub \\)\\?\\(pub(crate) \\)\\?static [A-Za-z_0-9]*\\s*:\\s*\\['`) and then every `NAME[...]` use of each. Note that most of the translation already uses `.as_ptr().add(...)` (e.g. `xclass.rs:12`, `dfa_internal.rs`, `auto_possess.rs:505-521`, `ord2utf.rs`, all `ucd_script_sets`/`boolprop_sets`/`caseless_sets` sites) — the remaining `[...]` sites are the leftovers.\n\n### CAN OVERFLOW — fixed (12 sites)\n\n| file:line (pre-fix) | table (len) | index expr | C source | verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/macros.rs:409` (`UCD_CATEGORY!`) | `_pcre2_ucp_gentype_8` (30) | `UCD_CHARTYPE!(ch)` | `pcre2_internal.h:2144` | can overflow |\n| `src/compile.rs:1565` (`read_name`) | gentype (30) | `type_ = UCD_CHARTYPE(c)` | `pcre2_compile.c:2638` | can overflow |\n| `src/substitute.rs:231` (`read_name_subst`) | gentype (30) | `type_ = UCD_CHARTYPE(c)` | `pcre2_substitute.c:226` | can overflow |\n| `src/substitute.rs:374` (case forcing) | gentype (30) | `type_ = UCD_CHARTYPE(ch)` | `pcre2_substitute.c:371` | can overflow |\n| `src/match_engine.rs:1946` PT_GC | gentype (30) | `(*prop).chartype` | `pcre2_match.c:2773` | can overflow |\n| `src/match_engine.rs:1990-1991` PT_ALNUM | gentype (30) | `chartype` | `pcre2_match.c:2799-2800` | can overflow |\n| `src/match_engine.rs:2014` PT_SPACE/PXSPACE | gentype (30) | `(*prop).chartype` | `pcre2_match.c:2818` | can overflow |\n| `src/match_engine.rs:2027-2028` PT_WORD | gentype (30) | `chartype` | `pcre2_match.c:2826-2827` | can overflow |\n| `src/match_engine.rs:3369` `\\b` prev_is_word | gentype (30) | `UCD_CHARTYPE(fc)` | `pcre2_match.c:6723` | can overflow |\n| `src/match_engine.rs:3398` `\\b` cur_is_word | gentype (30) | `UCD_CHARTYPE(fc)` | `pcre2_match.c:6756` | can overflow |\n| `src/match_engine.rs:5135` PT_WORD min-loop | gentype (30) | `UCD_CHARTYPE(fc)` | `pcre2_match.c:3134` | can overflow |\n| `src/match_engine.rs:6205` PT_WORD max-loop | gentype (30) | `UCD_CHARTYPE(fc)` | `pcre2_match.c:4526` | can overflow |\n| `src/match_engine.rs:7282` PT_WORD backtrack | gentype (30) | `UCD_CHARTYPE(fc)` | `pcre2_match.c:3942` | can overflow |\n| `src/match_engine.rs:7931` `\\X` greedy backtrack | `_pcre2_ucp_gbtable_8` (15) | `lgb = UCD_GRAPHBREAK(fc)` | `pcre2_match.c:4709` | can overflow (same construct as the already-fixed `PRIV(extuni)` site) |\n\nReasoning: `chartype`/`gbprop` are bytes read out of the `ucd_record` that `GET_UCD` points at. Since the 8-bit `GET_UCD` has no `MAX_UTF_CODE_POINT` guard (`pcre2_internal.h:2123-2131`), a code point above 0x10FFFF makes `GET_UCD` read past `ucd_stage1`/`ucd_stage2`/`ucd_records`, so those bytes can be any value 0..255 — far past 30 / 15 entries.\n\n### PROVABLY IN RANGE — left alone\n- `_pcre2_ucp_gentype_8[...]` in `compile_class.rs:751,774,798,827,836,841` — all inside `_pcre2_update_classbits_8`, whose loop is `while c < 256`, so `GET_UCD(c)` is always valid (C `pcre2_compile_class.c:780-850`).\n- `_pcre2_OP_lengths_8[...]` (29 sites in `study.rs`, `pattern_info.rs`, `compile_aux.rs`, `matcher.rs`, `match_engine.rs`) — index is always an opcode byte (≤172, table len 173).\n- `_pcre2_utf8_table4[(c & 0x3f)]` (`macros.rs:126`, `valid_utf.rs:98`) — masked to 0..63, table len 64.\n- `_pcre2_utt_8[i]` (`compile.rs:1379-1393`) — binary chop bounded by `_pcre2_utt_size_8`.\n- `rep_min`/`rep_max`/`rep_typ` (25 sites) — index is `*Fecode - OP_CRSTAR`/`OP_STAR`, bounded by the opcode ranges (max 10; `rep_typ` has 12).\n- `xdigitab[c]` (`compile.rs:17`) — every C caller is `XDIGIT(*ptr)`, an 8-bit code unit; table len 256.\n- `escapes[c - ESCAPES_FIRST]` (`compile.rs:499`) — guarded by `if c < ESCAPES_FIRST || c > ESCAPES_LAST`.\n- `posix_name_lengths[yield_]` (`compile.rs:1480-1486`) — 0-terminated walk.\n- `_pcre2_posix_class_maps8[posix_class{,+1,+2}]` (`compile_class.rs:1211-1219`) — `posix_class` ∈ 0..13 from `check_posix_name`, `*3+2 ≤ 41 < 42`.\n- `_pcre2_ucd_digit_sets_8[mid]` (`script_run.rs:301`) — binary search bounded by `digit_sets[0]`.\n- `meta_extra_lengths[meta]` (`compile_aux.rs:940`), `verbs[i]`, `alasmeta[i]` (`compile_parse.rs`) — parsed meta codes / loop-bounded.\n- `SET_BIT!`/`start_bitmap` (`study.rs:33,940`) — the C guards every call (`pcre2_study.c:801,835,837,1236`); `set_type_bits` loops `c < table_limit ≤ 32`.\n- `name[i]` (`compile.rs:1280`) bounded by 49; `require_map`/`map` (`script_run.rs`) bounded by `FULL_MAPSIZE`; `classbits`/`classwords`/`small_ref_offset`/`out_str` — all constant-bounded loops.\n- `opcode_possessify` (`compile_branch.rs:2520`), `coptable`/`poptable`/`toptable1`/`toptable2`, `propposstab`/`catposstab`/`autoposstab`/`posspropstab` — already raw pointer arithmetic.\n\n## What changed\n- `src/macros.rs` — `UCD_CATEGORY!` now `*_pcre2_ucp_gentype_8.as_ptr().add(UCD_CHARTYPE!(ch) as usize)`.\n- `src/match_engine.rs` — added two `#[inline] unsafe fn ucp_gentype(i: i32)` / `ucp_gbtable(i: i32)` helpers (same style as `xclass.rs:12`) doing `.as_ptr().add(...)`, and switched the 11 gentype sites + the gbtable site to them. Each site carries a one-line comment naming the mirrored `pcre2_match.c` line.\n- `src/compile.rs`, `src/substitute.rs` — inline `.as_ptr().add(...)` with comments citing `pcre2_compile.c:2638`, `pcre2_substitute.c:226`, `pcre2_substitute.c:371`.\n\nNo clamping, no early returns, no bounds checks, no value changes for in-range inputs (all lookups are byte-for-byte the same for indices < table length).\n\n## Reproducers (scratch in `_v/repro/`, run `_v/repro/run.sh`)\n`librust_before.so` is built from a copy of `translation/src` with only these fixes reverted (`_v/repro/before/`); `librust_after.so` is the fixed build. Driver `repro.c` dlopens each `.so`.\n\nCommon input: compile with `PCRE2_UTF`, match with `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK`, subject `\"a\" + raw 5-byte UTF-8 for U+203800 + \"b\"` = `\\x61\\xf8\\x88\\x83\\xa0\\x80\\x62` (U+203800/128 = 16496, past `ucd_stage1`'s 8704 entries).\n\n| pattern (compile opts) | C `.so` | Rust BEFORE | Rust AFTER |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `\\p{L}+` (UTF) | rc=1 ov=[0,1] | **SIGABRT (134)** — `panicked at src/match_engine.rs:6084: index out of bounds: the len is 30 but the index is 98` (that is the `UCD_CATEGORY!` expansion, i.e. `macros.rs:409`) | rc=1 ov=[0,1] ✔ |\n| `\\p{Z}` (UTF) | rc=-1 ov=[-1,-1] | **SIGABRT (134)** — `match_engine.rs:1966` (PT_GC site, C `pcre2_match.c:2773`) | rc=-1 ov=[-1,-1] ✔ |\n| `\\w+` (UTF\\|UCP) | rc=1 ov=[0,1] | **SIGABRT (134)** — `match_engine.rs:6225` (PT_WORD max-loop, C `pcre2_match.c:4526`) | rc=1 ov=[0,1] ✔ |\n\nThree of the fixed sites are demonstrated. The `ucp_gbtable` site (`match_engine.rs:7931`) is fixed by analysis: it is a verbatim copy of the `PRIV(extuni)` construct that was already fixed, same table, same `lgb = UCD_GRAPHBREAK(...)` source. I scanned ~40k out-of-range code points with `\\X*Z` / `\\X{1,4}Z` / `\\X{2,}+` (incl. `PCRE2_NO_AUTO_POSSESS`, 2/3/5-char runs) without landing a garbage `gbprop ≥ 15`, so I could not exhibit an abort there — the garbage byte value is memory-layout/ASLR dependent.\n\nCaveat worth knowing: once the index is out of range both libraries read *unspecified adjacent memory*, so residual value divergence between the C and Rust `.so` remains for some of these inputs (e.g. `\\X` on the same subject gives C ov=[0,1] vs Rust ov=[0,6]). That is intrinsic to the C's UB and is not something the translation can match; the point of the fix is that Rust now *returns* instead of aborting.\n\n## Tests\n`cd translation && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-audit cargo test --offline --release --test fuzz_crosscheck --test configs_tables_leaf` → `configs_tables_leaf` 55 