{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7qcjihfbvgmljocfhxypxp2j4xzionbzazwp4tonsdlx7xcxgi4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01TYESnagivUF5jfLagRRJnT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> translation/CONFIGS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Row → test mapping\n\nEvery row has a `#[test]` named after its id (a few adjacent rows share one test, noted below),\nand every test prints its row id under `cargo test -- --nocapture`.\n\n| rows | test file | tests | comparisons per run |\n|------|-----------|-------|---------------------|\n| C001–C055 | `tests/configs_tables_leaf.rs` | 55 | all table bytes; 1.11 M `ord2utf`; 1.21 M `valid_utf` (incl. 100 000 random byte strings); ≈204 M `xclass` sweeps |\n| C056–C077 | `tests/configs_study_context.rs` | 25 | study/auto-possessify through compile **and** by direct FFI on copied code blocks (504 + 973 direct calls, 451/512 of which actually modify the block); every setter value 0..=300 |\n| C078–C125 | `tests/configs_compile.rs` | 48 | 6 911 351 (200 000 random patterns per option group; also run at 6 M patterns ≈ 220 M comparisons) |\n| C126–C157 | `tests/configs_match.rs` | 32 | 19 662 129 |\n| C158–C169 | `tests/configs_dfa.rs` | 14 | ≈639 000, including the whole `int` workspace after every call |\n| C170–C189 | `tests/configs_subst.rs` | 17 | 1 518 133 substitute + 13 944 substring + 916 serialize (`c184_c187_*` and `c188_c189_*` each cover their id range) |\n| C190–C202 | `tests/configs_info_convert.rs` | 13 | ≈175 000 `pattern_convert` + ≈50 000 `pattern_info` |\n| all (cross-cutting) | `tests/fuzz_crosscheck.rs` | 4 | 800 000 whole-pipeline cases (compile → info → serialize → match → next_match → dfa → substitute → substring) |\n\n## Inputs deliberately excluded, and why\n\nThese are inputs for which the **C itself has no defined behaviour**, so there is no ground\ntruth to match. Each is excluded narrowly, at one documented place in the tests, and the\nneighbouring defined behaviour is still covered:\n\n1. `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` together with a subject/pattern that is **not** valid UTF-8 (or a\n   start offset inside a character). PCRE2 documents this as undefined; concretely the C\n   builds a code point of up to 0x7FFFFFFF out of a 5/6-byte ill-formed sequence and then\n   indexes `PRIV(ucd_stage1)` (8704 entries) out of bounds — we reproduced a SIGSEGV in the C\n   library, and non-deterministic results (clean return in one process, SIGSEGV in another)\n   for the same call. Ill-formed UTF-8 IS tested with the check enabled (every\n   `PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_ERR1..21`), and with `NO_UTF_CHECK` on valid UTF-8, and with\n   `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` (which re-enables validation internally).\n2. `pcre2_*_context_copy(NULL)` — the C dereferences the argument with no NULL check\n   (`pcre2_context.c:231-277`). `*_context_free(NULL)`, which IS documented as a no-op, is tested.\n3. `pcre2_jit_match_8` with a NULL match data — the no-JIT stub unconditionally writes\n   `match_data->rc` (`pcre2_jit_match_inc.h:103`).\n4. `PCRE2_DFA_RESTART` workspace values in the band that passes the restart sanity check at\n   `pcre2_dfa_match.c:3456` but then overflows the `memcpy` at `:672` (a heap overflow inside\n   the C). Every other restart shape, including byte-exact workspace contents across a\n   partial-match → restart pair, is compared.\n5. `pcre2_config` string keys with a buffer smaller than the string — `pcre2_config` takes no\n   buffer length, so a short buffer is an overflow in both libraries. Instead every byte the\n   call writes into a poisoned region, and the exact return value, are compared.\n6. Fields the C leaves indeterminate: `startchar`/`mark` on early-error returns, and the\n   ovector after an error other than `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`. Where these are compared at all,\n   the match data is allocated through a **zeroing allocator** so that both libraries start\n   from identical bytes; done that way, C and Rust agree on the residue too\n   (`tests/regressions.rs::ovec_residue` pins this).\nEOF\ncat >> translation/ERRORS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## How the rows were validated\n\n1. Every row was first checked against the real C library, before any Rust was involved:\n   `_v/checkerr.c` replays all 121 compile rows (`rows=121 verified=102 unreachable=19\n   failed=0`) and `_v/checkrt.c` replays all reachable runtime rows (`271 checks, 0 MISMATCH`).\n   So the \"expected C result\" column is measured behaviour, not an assumption.\n2. `tests/errors_compile.rs` then drives every compile row through BOTH `.so`s and asserts\n   the C result equals the tabulated code AND that Rust returns the identical\n   `(compiled?, errorcode, erroroffset)` triple. It additionally compares\n   `pcre2_get_error_message_8` for every code in −200..=350 and for every buffer size 0..40,\n   and every single-bit and all-ones compile option word.\n3. `tests/errors_runtime.rs` drives every reachable runtime row through both `.so`s, asserting\n   the same error code **and** every output argument (`*outlengthptr` and the whole output\n   buffer for `pcre2_substitute_8`, `*blength`/`*bufferptr`/buffer for\n   `pcre2_pattern_convert_8`, `*where` for `pattern_info`/`config`, the message buffer for\n   `get_error_message`, `*offset`/`*options` for `next_match`, the ovector for the matchers).\n   It asserts row accounting: 300 rows parsed, 267 reachable, 33 unreachable, 267 executed.\n4. Beyond the table it adds 78 NULL-argument cases, 1220 zero/oversized-length and\n   offset cases, 1226 one-step-past-range cases (including out-of-range enum values passed as\n   raw ints across the FFI boundary: unknown `pcre2_set_optimize_8` directives, unknown\n   `PCRE2_CONFIG_*`/`PCRE2_INFO_*` keys, invalid newline/BSR conventions, undefined option\n   bits), and 6300 fixed-seed random error-surface cases.\n\nResult: **0 divergences** — for every row, and every generic-boundary case, the two libraries\nreturn the same error code and the same output-argument bytes.\nEOF\nwc -l translation/CONFIGS.md translation/ERRORS.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":554,"cache_read_input_tokens":251387,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":554,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503","uuid":"2b7df0a2-63c1-44a6-87d5-643b1ed9ba71","timestamp":"2026-09-08T20:07:01.109Z"}
