{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7a2soz6f53gd2o7xnpt7abn2qzlequdb6ktetgmb25samt7y23fa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — all four phases pass.\n\n## Result\n\n**278 differential tests, 0 failures.** Every test loads both `.so`s via `libloading` and calls only exported symbols, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are under test too.\n\n**2 real defects found and fixed** (same class, 15 sites):\n- `GET_UCD!` and 14 `ucp_gentype`/`ucp_gbtable` lookups used bounds-checked slice indexing where the C indexes unchecked. `\\X` on a 5-byte UTF-8 lead byte reaches `GET_UCD` with a code point > 0x10FFFF (the 8-bit build has no guard, `pcre2_internal.h:2123-2131`): C returns `rc=1`, Rust **aborted** (`panic = \"abort\"`). Fixed with unchecked pointer arithmetic reproducing C's `(int)` division/modulo. Pinned by `tests/regressions.rs`.\n\n## Phase artifacts (crate root)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | all 143 C dynamic symbols, per-symbol C/Rust source mapping — **0 missing, 0 extra, 0 undefined non-libc** |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **421 rows** (121 compile ERR0–ERR120 + 300 runtime), 369 reachable, each pre-validated against the real C lib (`_v/checkerr.c`, `_v/checkrt.c`) then diff-tested → all `[x]` |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **202 rows** across the cross-product of option flags, extra options, context settings, newline/BSR, input shapes and *all* entry points incl. the low-level `PRIV()` ones and data tables → all `[x]` |\n| `tests/README.md` | row→test mapping, UB exclusions, mutation-test evidence |\n\n## Gate\n\n- **Phase B** — all 202 rows, fixed-seed randomized: ~30 M comparisons/run (19.7 M match, 6.9 M compile, 1.5 M substitute, 800 k whole-pipeline fuzz), plus a 220 M-comparison extended mode.\n- **Phase C** — all 369 reachable error rows return identical codes *and* output-argument bytes, plus ~2500 boundary cases (NULLs, zero/oversized lengths, out-of-range enum ints across FFI).\n- **Phase D** — symbol diff empty; crate declares no `[features]` and no `cfg(feature)` (single configuration, enumerated generically by `_v/verify.sh`); no binary target in either project — instead the two C driver programs were linked against each `.so` and their stdout compared: **2 576 785** and **20 031 354** lines identical.\n- **Not vacuous** — 3 injected defects (config value, UCP `\\b` category, `max_lookbehind`) were each caught and reverted.\n\nExcluded, narrowly and documented: inputs where the C itself is undefined (`PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` on invalid UTF-8 — the C SIGSEGVs), `*_context_copy(NULL)`, and the DFA-restart band that overflows a `memcpy` inside the C. `c_src/` was not modified. Re-run everything with `bash _v/verify.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1066,"cache_read_input_tokens":269980,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1066,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4f10895-a33e-435f-9410-97f386d0c503","uuid":"58890c53-a2bf-4062-a766-122e71216683","timestamp":"2026-09-08T20:10:31.148Z"}
